tps://owasp.org/Top10/A05_2021-Security_Misconfiguration)\n","text":"Detected a cookie where the `Secure` flag is either missing or disabled. The `Secure` cookie flag instructs the browser to forbid sending the cookie over an insecure HTTP request. Set the `Secure` flag to `true` so the cookie will only be sent over HTTPS."},"helpUri":"https://semgrep.dev/r/python.flask.web.flask-talisman-cookie-secure-false.flask-talisman-cookie-secure-false","id":"python.flask.web.flask-talisman-cookie-secure-false.flask-talisman-cookie-secure-false","name":"python.flask.web.flask-talisman-cookie-secure-false.flask-talisman-cookie-secure-false","properties":{"precision":"very-high","tags":["CWE-614: Sensitive Cookie in HTTPS Session Without 'Secure' Attribute","HIGH CONFIDENCE","OWASP-A02:2025 - Security Misconfiguration","OWASP-A05:2021 - Security Misconfiguration","security"]},"shortDescription":{"text":"Semgrep Finding: python.flask.web.flask-talisman-cookie-secure-false.flask-talisman-cookie-secure-false"}},{"defaultConfiguration":{"level":"note"},"fullDescription":{"text":"Detected a cookie where the `Secure` flag is either missing or disabled. The `Secure` cookie flag instructs the browser to forbid sending the cookie over an insecure HTTP request. Set the `Secure` flag to `true` so the cookie will only be sent over HTTPS."},"help":{"markdown":"Detected a cookie where the `Secure` flag is either missing or disabled. The `Secure` cookie flag instructs the browser to forbid sending the cookie over an insecure HTTP request. Set the `Secure` flag to `true` so the cookie will only be sent over HTTPS.\n\n<b>References:</b>\n - [Semgrep Rule](https://semgrep.dev/r/python.flask.web.flask-talisman-decorator-cookie-secure-false.flask-talisman-decorator-cookie-secure-false)\n - [https://owasp.org/Top10/2025/A02_2025-Security_Misconfiguration/](https://owasp.org/Top10/2025/A02_2025-Security_Misconfiguration/)\n - [https://owasp.org/Top10/A05_2021-Security_Misconfiguration](https://owasp.org/Top10/A05_2021-Security_Misconfiguration)\n","text":"Detected a cookie where the `Secure` flag is either missing or disabled. The `Secure` cookie flag instructs the browser to forbid sending the cookie over an insecure HTTP request. Set the `Secure` flag to `true` so the cookie will only be sent over HTTPS."},"helpUri":"https://semgrep.dev/r/python.flask.web.flask-talisman-decorator-cookie-secure-false.flask-talisman-decorator-cookie-secure-false","id":"python.flask.web.flask-talisman-decorator-cookie-secure-false.flask-talisman-decorator-cookie-secure-false","name":"python.flask.web.flask-talisman-decorator-cookie-secure-false.flask-talisman-decorator-cookie-secure-false","properties":{"precision":"very-high","tags":["CWE-614: Sensitive Cookie in HTTPS Session Without 'Secure' Attribute","HIGH CONFIDENCE","OWASP-A02:2025 - Security Misconfiguration","OWASP-A05:2021 - Security Misconfiguration","security"]},"shortDescription":{"text":"Semgrep Finding: python.flask.web.flask-talisman-decorator-cookie-secure-false.flask-talisman-decorator-cookie-secure-false"}},{"defaultConfiguration":{"level":"note"},"fullDescription":{"text":"Untrusted input could be used to tamper with a web page rendering, which can lead to a Cross-site scripting (XSS) vulnerability. XSS vulnerabilities occur when untrusted input executes malicious JavaScript code, leading to issues such as account compromise and sensitive information leakage. To prevent this vulnerability, validate the user input, perform contextual output encoding or sanitize the input. In Flask apps, it is recommended to use the `jsonify()` function instead of the `json.dumps()` functions. It is more convenient as it converts the JSON data to a Response object, using `json.dumps()` is more error prone. Additionally, `jsonify()` sets the correct security headers and the response type for JSON responses. This means the response data will never be interpreted by browsers as HTML or JavaScript and will be secure against XSS attacks."},"help":{"markdown":"Untrusted input could be used to tamper with a web page rendering, which can lead to a Cross-site scripting (XSS) vulnerability. XSS vulnerabilities occur when untrusted input executes malicious JavaScript code, leading to issues such as account compromise and sensitive information leakage. To prevent this vulnerability, validate the user input, perform contextual output encoding or sanitize the input. In Flask apps, it is recommended to use the `jsonify()` function instead of the `json.dumps()` functions. It is more convenient as it converts the JSON data to a Response object, using `json.dumps()` is more error prone. Additionally, `jsonify()` sets the correct security headers and the response type for JSON responses. This means the response data will never be interpreted by browsers as HTML or JavaScript and will be secure against XSS attacks.\n\n<b>References:</b>\n - [Semgrep Rule](https://semgrep.dev/r/python.flask.web.flask-use-jsonify-secure-default.flask-use-jsonify-secure-default)\n - [https://flask.palletsprojects.com/en/3.0.x/api/#flask.json.jsonify](https://flask.palletsprojects.com/en/3.0.x/api/#flask.json.jsonify)\n - [https://flask.palletsprojects.com/en/3.0.x/web-security/#security-json](https://flask.palletsprojects.com/en/3.0.x/web-security/#security-json)\n - [https://owasp.org/Top10/2025/A05_2025-Injection/](https://owasp.org/Top10/2025/A05_2025-Injection/)\n - [https://owasp.org/Top10/A03_2021-Injection](https://owasp.org/Top10/A03_2021-Injection)\n - [https://www.geeksforgeeks.org/use-jsonify-instead-of-json-dumps-in-flask/](https://www.geeksforgeeks.org/use-jsonify-instead-of-json-dumps-in-flask/)\n","text":"Untrusted input could be used to tamper with a web page rendering, which can lead to a Cross-site scripting (XSS) vulnerability. XSS vulnerabilities occur when untrusted input executes malicious JavaScript code, leading to issues such as account compromise and sensitive information leakage. To prevent this vulnerability, validate the user input, perform contextual output encoding or sanitize the input. In Flask apps, it is recommended to use the `jsonify()` function instead of the `json.dumps()` functions. It is more convenient as it converts the JSON data to a Response object, using `json.dumps()` is more error prone. Additionally, `jsonify()` sets the correct security headers and the response type for JSON responses. This means the response data will never be interpreted by browsers as HTML or JavaScript and will be secure against XSS attacks."},"helpUri":"https://semgrep.dev/r/python.flask.web.flask-use-jsonify-secure-default.flask-use-jsonify-secure-default","id":"python.flask.web.flask-use-jsonify-secure-default.flask-use-jsonify-secure-default","name":"python.flask.web.flask-use-jsonify-secure-default.flask-use-jsonify-secure-default","properties":{"precision":"very-high","tags":["CWE-79: Improper Neutralization of Input During Web Page Generation ('Cross-site Scripting')","HIGH CONFIDENCE","OWASP-A03:2021 - Injection","OWASP-A05:2025 - Injection","OWASP-A07:2017 - Cross-Site Scripting (XSS)","security"]},"shortDescription":{"text":"Semgrep Finding: python.flask.web.flask-use-jsonify-secure-default.flask-use-jsonify-secure-default"}},{"defaultConfiguration":{"level":"note"},"fullDescription":{"text":"The application does not appear to verify inbound requests which can lead to a Cross-site request forgery (CSRF) vulnerability. If the application uses cookie-based authentication, an attacker can trick users into sending authenticated HTTP requests without their knowledge from any arbitrary domain they visit. If this is intentional, remember that with `WTF_CSRF_CHECK_DEFAULT` set to `False` the CSRF tokens are still enabled and included, but the check no longer happens automatically, which weakens the security of the application. Doing the check manually requires a call to `csrf.protect()` before handling the request. An appropriate place to do this is a `@app.before_request` decorated function."},"help":{"markdown":"The application does not appear to verify inbound requests which can lead to a Cross-site request forgery (CSRF) vulnerability. If the application uses cookie-based authentication, an attacker can trick users into sending authenticated HTTP requests without their knowledge from any arbitrary domain they visit. If this is intentional, remember that with `WTF_CSRF_CHECK_DEFAULT` set to `False` the CSRF tokens are still enabled and included, but the check no longer happens automatically, which weakens the security of the application. Doing the check manually requires a call to `csrf.protect()` before handling the request. An appropriate place to do this is a `@app.before_request` decorated function.\n\n<b>References:</b>\n - [Semgrep Rule](https://semgrep.dev/r/python.flask.web.flask-wtf-csrf-check-default-false.flask-wtf-csrf-check-default-false)\n - [https://flask-wtf.readthedocs.io/en/1.2.x/config/](https://flask-wtf.readthedocs.io/en/1.2.x/config/)\n - [https://owasp.org/Top10/2025/A01_2025-Broken_Access_Control/](https://owasp.org/Top10/2025/A01_2025-Broken_Access_Control/)\n - [https://owasp.org/Top10/A01_2021-Broken_Access_Control](https://owasp.org/Top10/A01_2021-Broken_Access_Control)\n","text":"The application does not appear to verify inbound requests which can lead to a Cross-site request forgery (CSRF) vulnerability. If the application uses cookie-based authentication, an attacker can trick users into sending authenticated HTTP requests without their knowledge from any arbitrary domain they visit. If this is intentional, remember that with `WTF_CSRF_CHECK_DEFAULT` set to `False` the CSRF tokens are still enabled and included, but the check no longer happens automatically, which weakens the security of the application. Doing the check manually requires a call to `csrf.protect()` before handling the request. An appropriate place to do this is a `@app.before_request` decorated function."},"helpUri":"https://semgrep.dev/r/python.flask.web.flask-wtf-csrf-check-default-false.flask-wtf-csrf-check-default-false","id":"python.flask.web.flask-wtf-csrf-check-default-false.flask-wtf-csrf-check-default-false","name":"python.flask.web.flask-wtf-csrf-check-default-false.flask-wtf-csrf-check-default-false","properties":{"precision":"very-high","tags":["CWE-352: Cross-Site Request Forgery (CSRF)","HIGH CONFIDENCE","OWASP-A01:2021 - Broken Access Control","OWASP-A01:2025 - Broken Access Control","security"]},"shortDescription":{"text":"Semgrep Finding: python.flask.web.flask-wtf-csrf-check-default-false.flask-wtf-csrf-check-default-false"}},{"defaultConfiguration":{"level":"error"},"fullDescription":{"text":"The application is setting one or more security headers but does not set the `Cache-Control` header. Improper cache control on authenticated resources can lead to information leakage or even session hijacking depending on the application."},"help":{"markdown":"The application is setting one or more security headers but does not set the `Cache-Control` header. Improper cache control on authenticated resources can lead to information leakage or even session hijacking depending on the application.\n\n<b>References:</b>\n - [Semgrep Rule](https://semgrep.dev/r/python.flask.web.security_header.after_request.after-request-cache-control.after-request-cache-control)\n - [https://academy.semgrep.dev/courses/security-headers](https://academy.semgrep.dev/courses/security-headers)\n - [https://cheatsheetseries.owasp.org/cheatsheets/HTTP_Headers_Cheat_Sheet.html](https://cheatsheetseries.owasp.org/cheatsheets/HTTP_Headers_Cheat_Sheet.html)\n - [https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/HTTP/Headers](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/HTTP/Headers)\n - [https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/HTTP/Headers/Content-Security-Policy](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/HTTP/Headers/Content-Security-Policy)\n - [https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/HTTP/Headers/Cross-Origin-Embedder-Policy](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/HTTP/Headers/Cross-Origin-Embedder-Policy)\n - [https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/HTTP/Headers/Cross-Origin-Opener-Policy](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/HTTP/Headers/Cross-Origin-Opener-Policy)\n - [https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/HTTP/Headers/Cross-Origin-Resource-Policy](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/HTTP/Headers/Cross-Origin-Resource-Policy)\n - [https://owasp.org/Top10/A05_2021-Security_Misconfiguration](https://owasp.org/Top10/A05_2021-Security_Misconfiguration)\n - [https://owasp.org/www-community/attacks/Session_hijacking_attack](https://owasp.org/www-community/attacks/Session_hijacking_attack)\n - [https://phabricator.wikimedia.org/T55032](https://phabricator.wikimedia.org/T55032)\n","text":"The application is setting one or more security headers but does not set the `Cache-Control` header. Improper cache control on authenticated resources can lead to information leakage or even session hijacking depending on the application."},"helpUri":"https://semgrep.dev/r/python.flask.web.security_header.after_request.after-request-cache-control.after-request-cache-control","id":"python.flask.web.security_header.after_request.after-request-cache-control.after-request-cache-control","name":"python.flask.web.security_header.after_request.after-request-cache-control.after-request-cache-control","properties":{"precision":"very-high","tags":["CWE-358: Improperly Implemented Security Check for Standard","HIGH CONFIDENCE","OWASP-A05:2021-Security misconfiguration","security"]},"shortDescription":{"text":"Semgrep Finding: python.flask.web.security_header.after_request.after-request-cache-control.after-request-cache-control"}},{"defaultConfiguration":{"level":"error"},"fullDescription":{"text":"The application is setting one or more security headers but does not set the `X-Content-Type-Options` header. Without this header set to \"nosniff\", browsers may interpret and execute files as a different content-type than what was declared (MIME confusion attacks). MIME confusion attacks are commonly used for cross-site scripting attacks - if you accept user-uploaded files, you should set this header."},"help":{"markdown":"The application is setting one or more security headers but does not set the `X-Content-Type-Options` header. Without this header set to \"nosniff\", browsers may interpret and execute files as a different content-type than what was declared (MIME confusion attacks). MIME confusion attacks are commonly used for cross-site scripting attacks - if you accept user-uploaded files, you should set this header.\n\n<b>References:</b>\n - [Semgrep Rule](https://semgrep.dev/r/python.flask.web.security_header.after_request.after-request-content-type-options.after-request-content-type-options)\n - [https://academy.semgrep.dev/courses/security-headers](https://academy.semgrep.dev/courses/security-headers)\n - [https://cheatsheetseries.owasp.org/cheatsheets/HTTP_Headers_Cheat_Sheet.html](https://cheatsheetseries.owasp.org/cheatsheets/HTTP_Headers_Cheat_Sheet.html)\n - [https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/HTTP/Headers](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/HTTP/Headers)\n - [https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/HTTP/Headers/Content-Security-Policy](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/HTTP/Headers/Content-Security-Policy)\n - [https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/HTTP/Headers/Cross-Origin-Embedder-Policy](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/HTTP/Headers/Cross-Origin-Embedder-Policy)\n - [https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/HTTP/Headers/Cross-Origin-Opener-Policy](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/HTTP/Headers/Cross-Origin-Opener-Policy)\n - [https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/HTTP/Headers/Cross-Origin-Resource-Policy](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/HTTP/Headers/Cross-Origin-Resource-Policy)\n - [https://owasp.org/Top10/A05_2021-Security_Misconfiguration](https://owasp.org/Top10/A05_2021-Security_Misconfiguration)\n","text":"The application is setting one or more security headers but does not set the `X-Content-Type-Options` header. Without this header set to \"nosniff\", browsers may interpret and execute files as a different content-type than what was declared (MIME confusion attacks). MIME confusion attacks are commonly used for cross-site scripting attacks - if you accept user-uploaded files, you should set this header."},"helpUri":"https://semgrep.dev/r/python.flask.web.security_header.after_request.after-request-content-type-options.after-request-content-type-options","id":"python.flask.web.security_header.after_request.after-request-content-type-options.after-request-content-type-options","name":"python.flask.web.security_header.after_request.after-request-content-type-options.after-request-content-type-options","properties":{"precision":"very-high","tags":["CWE-358: Improperly Implemented Security Check for Standard","HIGH CONFIDENCE","OWASP-A05:2021-Security misconfiguration","security"]},"shortDescription":{"text":"Semgrep Finding: python.flask.web.security_header.after_request.after-request-content-type-options.after-request-content-type-options"}},{"defaultConfiguration":{"level":"error"},"fullDescription":{"text":"The application is setting one or more security headers but does not set the `Content-Security-Policy` header. A strong CSP configuration is an important defense-in-depth measure to mitigate the impact of successful cross-site scripting exploits."},"help":{"markdown":"The application is setting one or more security headers but does not set the `Content-Security-Policy` header. A strong CSP configuration is an important defense-in-depth measure to mitigate the impact of successful cross-site scripting exploits.\n\n<b>References:</b>\n - [Semgrep Rule](https://semgrep.dev/r/python.flask.web.security_header.after_request.after-request-csp.after-request-csp)\n - [https://academy.semgrep.dev/courses/security-headers](https://academy.semgrep.dev/courses/security-headers)\n - [https://cheatsheetseries.owasp.org/cheatsheets/Content_Security_Policy_Cheat_Sheet.html](https://cheatsheetseries.owasp.org/cheatsheets/Content_Security_Policy_Cheat_Sheet.html)\n - [https://cheatsheetseries.owasp.org/cheatsheets/HTTP_Headers_Cheat_Sheet.html](https://cheatsheetseries.owasp.org/cheatsheets/HTTP_Headers_Cheat_Sheet.html)\n - [https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/HTTP/Headers](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/HTTP/Headers)\n - [https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/HTTP/Headers/Content-Security-Policy](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/HTTP/Headers/Content-Security-Policy)\n - [https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/HTTP/Headers/Cross-Origin-Embedder-Policy](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/HTTP/Headers/Cross-Origin-Embedder-Policy)\n - [https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/HTTP/Headers/Cross-Origin-Opener-Policy](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/HTTP/Headers/Cross-Origin-Opener-Policy)\n - [https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/HTTP/Headers/Cross-Origin-Resource-Policy](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/HTTP/Headers/Cross-Origin-Resource-Policy)\n - [https://owasp.org/Top10/A05_2021-Security_Misconfiguration](https://owasp.org/Top10/A05_2021-Security_Misconfiguration)\n","text":"The application is setting one or more security headers but does not set the `Content-Security-Policy` header. A strong CSP configuration is an important defense-in-depth measure to mitigate the impact of successful cross-site scripting exploits."},"helpUri":"https://semgrep.dev/r/python.flask.web.security_header.after_request.after-request-csp.after-request-csp","id":"python.flask.web.security_header.after_request.after-request-csp.after-request-csp","name":"python.flask.web.security_header.after_request.after-request-csp.after-request-csp","properties":{"precision":"very-high","tags":["CWE-358: Improperly Implemented Security Check for Standard","HIGH CONFIDENCE","OWASP-A05:2021-Security misconfiguration","security"]},"shortDescription":{"text":"Semgrep Finding: python.flask.web.security_header.after_request.after-request-csp.after-request-csp"}},{"defaultConfiguration":{"level":"error"},"fullDescription":{"text":"The application is setting one or more security headers but does not set the `X-Frame-Options` header. This header prevents your application from being embedded in frames on untrusted domains, protecting against clickjacking attacks. Modern applications should also set a strong CSP configuration - this header is generally used for backwards compatibility with older browsers."},"help":{"markdown":"The application is setting one or more security headers but does not set the `X-Frame-Options` header. This header prevents your application from being embedded in frames on untrusted domains, protecting against clickjacking attacks. Modern applications should also set a strong CSP configuration - this header is generally used for backwards compatibility with older browsers.\n\n<b>References:</b>\n - [Semgrep Rule](https://semgrep.dev/r/python.flask.web.security_header.after_request.after-request-frame-options.after-request-frame-options)\n - [https://academy.semgrep.dev/courses/security-headers](https://academy.semgrep.dev/courses/security-headers)\n - [https://cheatsheetseries.owasp.org/cheatsheets/HTTP_Headers_Cheat_Sheet.html](https://cheatsheetseries.owasp.org/cheatsheets/HTTP_Headers_Cheat_Sheet.html)\n - [https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/HTTP/Headers](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/HTTP/Headers)\n - [https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/HTTP/Headers/Content-Security-Policy](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/HTTP/Headers/Content-Security-Policy)\n - [https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/HTTP/Headers/Cross-Origin-Embedder-Policy](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/HTTP/Headers/Cross-Origin-Embedder-Policy)\n - [https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/HTTP/Headers/Cross-Origin-Opener-Policy](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/HTTP/Headers/Cross-Origin-Opener-Policy)\n - [https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/HTTP/Headers/Cross-Origin-Resource-Policy](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/HTTP/Headers/Cross-Origin-Resource-Policy)\n - [https://owasp.org/Top10/A05_2021-Security_Misconfiguration](https://owasp.org/Top10/A05_2021-Security_Misconfiguration)\n","text":"The application is setting one or more security headers but does not set the `X-Frame-Options` header. This header prevents your application from being embedded in frames on untrusted domains, protecting against clickjacking attacks. Modern applications should also set a strong CSP configuration - this header is generally used for backwards compatibility with older browsers."},"helpUri":"https://semgrep.dev/r/python.flask.web.security_header.after_request.after-request-frame-options.after-request-frame-options","id":"python.flask.web.security_header.after_request.after-request-frame-options.after-request-frame-options","name":"python.flask.web.security_header.after_request.after-request-frame-options.after-request-frame-options","properties":{"precision":"very-high","tags":["CWE-358: Improperly Implemented Security Check for Standard","HIGH CONFIDENCE","OWASP-A05:2021-Security misconfiguration","security"]},"shortDescription":{"text":"Semgrep Finding: python.flask.web.security_header.after_request.after-request-frame-options.after-request-frame-options"}},{"defaultConfiguration":{"level":"error"},"fullDescription":{"text":"The application is setting one or more security headers but does not set the `Strict-Transport-Security` header. Failure to set this header can lead to protocol downgrade attacks. On the modern web, you should enforce HTTPS for all resources."},"help":{"markdown":"The application is setting one or more security headers but does not set the `Strict-Transport-Security` header. Failure to set this header can lead to protocol downgrade attacks. On the modern web, you should enforce HTTPS for all resources.\n\n<b>References:</b>\n - [Semgrep Rule](https://semgrep.dev/r/python.flask.web.security_header.after_request.after-request-hsts.after-request-hsts)\n - [https://academy.semgrep.dev/courses/security-headers](https://academy.semgrep.dev/courses/security-headers)\n - [https://cheatsheetseries.owasp.org/cheatsheets/HTTP_Headers_Cheat_Sheet.html](https://cheatsheetseries.owasp.org/cheatsheets/HTTP_Headers_Cheat_Sheet.html)\n - [https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/HTTP/Headers](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/HTTP/Headers)\n - [https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/HTTP/Headers/Content-Security-Policy](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/HTTP/Headers/Content-Security-Policy)\n - [https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/HTTP/Headers/Cross-Origin-Embedder-Policy](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/HTTP/Headers/Cross-Origin-Embedder-Policy)\n - [https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/HTTP/Headers/Cross-Origin-Opener-Policy](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/HTTP/Headers/Cross-Origin-Opener-Policy)\n - [https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/HTTP/Headers/Cross-Origin-Resource-Policy](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/HTTP/Headers/Cross-Origin-Resource-Policy)\n - [https://owasp.org/Top10/A05_2021-Security_Misconfiguration](https://owasp.org/Top10/A05_2021-Security_Misconfiguration)\n","text":"The application is setting one or more security headers but does not set the `Strict-Transport-Security` header. Failure to set this header can lead to protocol downgrade attacks. On the modern web, you should enforce HTTPS for all resources."},"helpUri":"https://semgrep.dev/r/python.flask.web.security_header.after_request.after-request-hsts.after-request-hsts","id":"python.flask.web.security_header.after_request.after-request-hsts.after-request-hsts","name":"python.flask.web.security_header.after_request.after-request-hsts.after-request-hsts","properties":{"precision":"very-high","tags":["CWE-358: Improperly Implemented Security Check for Standard","HIGH CONFIDENCE","OWASP-A05:2021-Security misconfiguration","security"]},"shortDescription":{"text":"Semgrep Finding: python.flask.web.security_header.after_request.after-request-hsts.after-request-hsts"}},{"defaultConfiguration":{"level":"error"},"fullDescription":{"text":"The application is setting one or more security headers but does not set the `Permissions-Policy` header. This header helps control which browser features can be used in your application. Modern browsers may access hardware features like a user's camera or microphone. To protect your users, if you do not need these features you should explicitly deny them via this header."},"help":{"markdown":"The application is setting one or more security headers but does not set the `Permissions-Policy` header. This header helps control which browser features can be used in your application. Modern browsers may access hardware features like a user's camera or microphone. To protect your users, if you do not need these features you should explicitly deny them via this header.\n\n<b>References:</b>\n - [Semgrep Rule](https://semgrep.dev/r/python.flask.web.security_header.after_request.after-request-permissions-policy.after-request-permissions-policy)\n - [https://academy.semgrep.dev/courses/security-headers](https://academy.semgrep.dev/courses/security-headers)\n - [https://cheatsheetseries.owasp.org/cheatsheets/HTTP_Headers_Cheat_Sheet.html](https://cheatsheetseries.owasp.org/cheatsheets/HTTP_Headers_Cheat_Sheet.html)\n - [https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/HTTP/Headers](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/HTTP/Headers)\n - [https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/HTTP/Headers/Content-Security-Policy](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/HTTP/Headers/Content-Security-Policy)\n - [https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/HTTP/Headers/Cross-Origin-Embedder-Policy](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/HTTP/Headers/Cross-Origin-Embedder-Policy)\n - [https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/HTTP/Headers/Cross-Origin-Opener-Policy](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/HTTP/Headers/Cross-Origin-Opener-Policy)\n - [https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/HTTP/Headers/Cross-Origin-Resource-Policy](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/HTTP/Headers/Cross-Origin-Resource-Policy)\n - [https://owasp.org/Top10/A05_2021-Security_Misconfiguration](https://owasp.org/Top10/A05_2021-Security_Misconfiguration)\n","text":"The application is setting one or more security headers but does not set the `Permissions-Policy` header. This header helps control which browser features can be used in your application. Modern browsers may access hardware features like a user's camera or microphone. To protect your users, if you do not need these features you should explicitly deny them via this header."},"helpUri":"https://semgrep.dev/r/python.flask.web.security_header.after_request.after-request-permissions-policy.after-request-permissions-policy","id":"python.flask.web.security_header.after_request.after-request-permissions-policy.after-request-permissions-policy","name":"python.flask.web.security_header.after_request.after-request-permissions-policy.after-request-permissions-policy","properties":{"precision":"very-high","tags":["CWE-358: Improperly Implemented Security Check for Standard","HIGH CONFIDENCE","OWASP-A05:2021-Security misconfiguration","security"]},"shortDescription":{"text":"Semgrep Finding: python.flask.web.security_header.after_request.after-request-permissions-policy.after-request-permissions-policy"}},{"defaultConfiguration":{"level":"error"},"fullDescription":{"text":"The application is setting one or more security headers but does not set the `X-Permitted-Cross-Domain-Policies` header. This header helps prevent untrusted Flash and Silverlight content from improperly loading information from your domain."},"help":{"markdown":"The application is setting one or more security headers but does not set the `X-Permitted-Cross-Domain-Policies` header. This header helps prevent untrusted Flash and Silverlight content from improperly loading information from your domain.\n\n<b>References:</b>\n - [Semgrep Rule](https://semgrep.dev/r/python.flask.web.security_header.after_request.after-request-permitted-cross-domain-policies.after-request-permitted-cross-domain-policies)\n - [https://academy.semgrep.dev/courses/security-headers](https://academy.semgrep.dev/courses/security-headers)\n - [https://cheatsheetseries.owasp.org/cheatsheets/HTTP_Headers_Cheat_Sheet.html](https://cheatsheetseries.owasp.org/cheatsheets/HTTP_Headers_Cheat_Sheet.html)\n - [https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/HTTP/Headers](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/HTTP/Headers)\n - [https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/HTTP/Headers/Content-Security-Policy](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/HTTP/Headers/Content-Security-Policy)\n - [https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/HTTP/Headers/Cross-Origin-Embedder-Policy](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/HTTP/Headers/Cross-Origin-Embedder-Policy)\n - [https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/HTTP/Headers/Cross-Origin-Opener-Policy](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/HTTP/Headers/Cross-Origin-Opener-Policy)\n - [https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/HTTP/Headers/Cross-Origin-Resource-Policy](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/HTTP/Headers/Cross-Origin-Resource-Policy)\n - [https://owasp.org/Top10/A05_2021-Security_Misconfiguration](https://owasp.org/Top10/A05_2021-Security_Misconfiguration)\n","text":"The application is setting one or more security headers but does not set the `X-Permitted-Cross-Domain-Policies` header. This header helps prevent untrusted Flash and Silverlight content from improperly loading information from your domain."},"helpUri":"https://semgrep.dev/r/python.flask.web.security_header.after_request.after-request-permitted-cross-domain-policies.after-request-permitted-cross-domain-policies","id":"python.flask.web.security_header.after_request.after-request-permitted-cross-domain-policies.after-request-permitted-cross-domain-policies","name":"python.flask.web.security_header.after_request.after-request-permitted-cross-domain-policies.after-request-permitted-cross-domain-policies","properties":{"precision":"very-high","tags":["CWE-358: Improperly Implemented Security Check for Standard","HIGH CONFIDENCE","OWASP-A05:2021-Security misconfiguration","security"]},"shortDescription":{"text":"Semgrep Finding: python.flask.web.security_header.after_request.after-request-permitted-cross-domain-policies.after-request-permitted-cross-domain-policies"}},{"defaultConfiguration":{"level":"error"},"fullDescription":{"text":"The application is setting one or more security headers but does not set the `Referrer-Policy` header. If your application makes use of sensitive query parameters (such as in oauth flows) or redirects users to other domains, you should set this header to prevent leaking sensitive information to third parties."},"help":{"markdown":"The application is setting one or more security headers but does not set the `Referrer-Policy` header. If your application makes use of sensitive query parameters (such as in oauth flows) or redirects users to other domains, you should set this header to prevent leaking sensitive information to third parties.\n\n<b>References:</b>\n - [Semgrep Rule](https://semgrep.dev/r/python.flask.web.security_header.after_request.after-request-referrer-policy.after-request-referrer-policy)\n - [https://academy.semgrep.dev/courses/security-headers](https://academy.semgrep.dev/courses/security-headers)\n - [https://cheatsheetseries.owasp.org/cheatsheets/HTTP_Headers_Cheat_Sheet.html](https://cheatsheetseries.owasp.org/cheatsheets/HTTP_Headers_Cheat_Sheet.html)\n - [https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/HTTP/Headers](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/HTTP/Headers)\n - [https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/HTTP/Headers/Content-Security-Policy](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/HTTP/Headers/Content-Security-Policy)\n - [https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/HTTP/Headers/Cross-Origin-Embedder-Policy](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/HTTP/Headers/Cross-Origin-Embedder-Policy)\n - [https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/HTTP/Headers/Cross-Origin-Opener-Policy](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/HTTP/Headers/Cross-Origin-Opener-Policy)\n - [https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/HTTP/Headers/Cross-Origin-Resource-Policy](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/HTTP/Headers/Cross-Origin-Resource-Policy)\n - [https://owasp.org/Top10/A05_2021-Security_Misconfiguration](https://owasp.org/Top10/A05_2021-Security_Misconfiguration)\n","text":"The application is setting one or more security headers but does not set the `Referrer-Policy` header. If your application makes use of sensitive query parameters (such as in oauth flows) or redirects users to other domains, you should set this header to prevent leaking sensitive information to third parties."},"helpUri":"https://semgrep.dev/r/python.flask.web.security_header.after_request.after-request-referrer-policy.after-request-referrer-policy","id":"python.flask.web.security_header.after_request.after-request-referrer-policy.after-request-referrer-policy","name":"python.flask.web.security_header.after_request.after-request-referrer-policy.after-request-referrer-policy","properties":{"precision":"very-high","tags":["CWE-358: Improperly Implemented Security Check for Standard","HIGH CONFIDENCE","OWASP-A05:2021-Security misconfiguration","security"]},"shortDescription":{"text":"Semgrep Finding: python.flask.web.security_header.after_request.after-request-referrer-policy.after-request-referrer-policy"}},{"defaultConfiguration":{"level":"error"},"fullDescription":{"text":"An after_request handler is setting one or more cross-origin resource sharing (CORS) headers but does not set the `Access-Control-Allow-Origin` header. Missing or weak values for this header allow arbitrary origins to read responses from your application. Setting a strong value for this header is especially recommended if your application's threat model includes 'straw purchasing' or reselling of paywalled content."},"help":{"markdown":"An after_request handler is setting one or more cross-origin resource sharing (CORS) headers but does not set the `Access-Control-Allow-Origin` header. Missing or weak values for this header allow arbitrary origins to read responses from your application. Setting a strong value for this header is especially recommended if your application's threat model includes 'straw purchasing' or reselling of paywalled content.\n\n<b>References:</b>\n - [Semgrep Rule](https://semgrep.dev/r/python.flask.web.security_header.after_request.cors.after-request-acao.after-request-acao)\n - [https://academy.semgrep.dev/courses/security-headers](https://academy.semgrep.dev/courses/security-headers)\n - [https://cheatsheetseries.owasp.org/cheatsheets/HTTP_Headers_Cheat_Sheet.html](https://cheatsheetseries.owasp.org/cheatsheets/HTTP_Headers_Cheat_Sheet.html)\n - [https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/HTTP/Headers](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/HTTP/Headers)\n - [https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/HTTP/Headers/Content-Security-Policy](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/HTTP/Headers/Content-Security-Policy)\n - [https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/HTTP/Headers/Cross-Origin-Embedder-Policy](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/HTTP/Headers/Cross-Origin-Embedder-Policy)\n - [https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/HTTP/Headers/Cross-Origin-Opener-Policy](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/HTTP/Headers/Cross-Origin-Opener-Policy)\n - [https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/HTTP/Headers/Cross-Origin-Resource-Policy](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/HTTP/Headers/Cross-Origin-Resource-Policy)\n - [https://owasp.org/Top10/A05_2021-Security_Misconfiguration](https://owasp.org/Top10/A05_2021-Security_Misconfiguration)\n - [https://xsleaks.dev/](https://xsleaks.dev/)\n","text":"An after_request handler is setting one or more cross-origin resource sharing (CORS) headers but does not set the `Access-Control-Allow-Origin` header. Missing or weak values for this header allow arbitrary origins to read responses from your application. Setting a strong value for this header is especially recommended if your application's threat model includes 'straw purchasing' or reselling of paywalled content."},"helpUri":"https://semgrep.dev/r/python.flask.web.security_header.after_request.cors.after-request-acao.after-request-acao","id":"python.flask.web.security_header.after_request.cors.after-request-acao.after-request-acao","name":"python.flask.web.security_header.after_request.cors.after-request-acao.after-request-acao","properties":{"precision":"very-high","tags":["CWE-358: Improperly Implemented Security Check for Standard","HIGH CONFIDENCE","OWASP-A05:2021-Security misconfiguration","security"]},"shortDescription":{"text":"Semgrep Finding: python.flask.web.security_header.after_request.cors.after-request-acao.after-request-acao"}},{"defaultConfiguration":{"level":"error"},"fullDescription":{"text":"An after_request handler is setting one or more cross-origin resource sharing (CORS) headers but does not set the `Cross-Origin-Embedder-Policy` header. Strict values for this header prevent the document from loading untrusted resources which can seriously hamper an attacker's ability to exploit weaknesses like cross-site scripting by preventing the loading of remote malicious scripts."},"help":{"markdown":"An after_request handler is setting one or more cross-origin resource sharing (CORS) headers but does not set the `Cross-Origin-Embedder-Policy` header. Strict values for this header prevent the document from loading untrusted resources which can seriously hamper an attacker's ability to exploit weaknesses like cross-site scripting by preventing the loading of remote malicious scripts.\n\n<b>References:</b>\n - [Semgrep Rule](https://semgrep.dev/r/python.flask.web.security_header.after_request.cors.after-request-coep.after-request-coep)\n - [https://academy.semgrep.dev/courses/security-headers](https://academy.semgrep.dev/courses/security-headers)\n - [https://cheatsheetseries.owasp.org/cheatsheets/HTTP_Headers_Cheat_Sheet.html](https://cheatsheetseries.owasp.org/cheatsheets/HTTP_Headers_Cheat_Sheet.html)\n - [https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/HTTP/Headers](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/HTTP/Headers)\n - [https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/HTTP/Headers/Content-Security-Policy](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/HTTP/Headers/Content-Security-Policy)\n - [https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/HTTP/Headers/Cross-Origin-Embedder-Policy](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/HTTP/Headers/Cross-Origin-Embedder-Policy)\n - [https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/HTTP/Headers/Cross-Origin-Opener-Policy](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/HTTP/Headers/Cross-Origin-Opener-Policy)\n - [https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/HTTP/Headers/Cross-Origin-Resource-Policy](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/HTTP/Headers/Cross-Origin-Resource-Policy)\n - [https://owasp.org/Top10/A05_2021-Security_Misconfiguration](https://owasp.org/Top10/A05_2021-Security_Misconfiguration)\n - [https://xsleaks.dev/](https://xsleaks.dev/)\n","text":"An after_request handler is setting one or more cross-origin resource sharing (CORS) headers but does not set the `Cross-Origin-Embedder-Policy` header. Strict values for this header prevent the document from loading untrusted resources which can seriously hamper an attacker's ability to exploit weaknesses like cross-site scripting by preventing the loading of remote malicious scripts."},"helpUri":"https://semgrep.dev/r/python.flask.web.security_header.after_request.cors.after-request-coep.after-request-coep","id":"python.flask.web.security_header.after_request.cors.after-request-coep.after-request-coep","name":"python.flask.web.security_header.after_request.cors.after-request-coep.after-request-coep","properties":{"precision":"very-high","tags":["CWE-358: Improperly Implemented Security Check for Standard","HIGH CONFIDENCE","OWASP-A05:2021-Security misconfiguration","security"]},"shortDescription":{"text":"Semgrep Finding: python.flask.web.security_header.after_request.cors.after-request-coep.after-request-coep"}},{"defaultConfiguration":{"level":"error"},"fullDescription":{"text":"An after_request handler is setting one or more cross-origin resource sharing (CORS) headers but does not set the `Cross-Origin-Opener-Policy` header. This header prevents attacks that use `window.opener` and the resulting `window` object to leak data from your application."},"help":{"markdown":"An after_request handler is setting one or more cross-origin resource sharing (CORS) headers but does not set the `Cross-Origin-Opener-Policy` header. This header prevents attacks that use `window.opener` and the resulting `window` object to leak data from your application.\n\n<b>References:</b>\n - [Semgrep Rule](https://semgrep.dev/r/python.flask.web.security_header.after_request.cors.after-request-coop.after-request-coop)\n - [https://academy.semgrep.dev/courses/security-headers](https://academy.semgrep.dev/courses/security-headers)\n - [https://cheatsheetseries.owasp.org/cheatsheets/HTTP_Headers_Cheat_Sheet.html](https://cheatsheetseries.owasp.org/cheatsheets/HTTP_Headers_Cheat_Sheet.html)\n - [https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/HTTP/Headers](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-U