ut does not set the `Cross-Origin-Resource-Policy` header. This header prevents untrusted origins from loading subresources - this behavior is commonly abused by phishing kits to quickly copy \"look and feel\" of your IP without having to host assets themselves."},"help":{"markdown":"An after_request handler is setting one or more cross-origin resource sharing (CORS) headers but does not set the `Cross-Origin-Resource-Policy` header. This header prevents untrusted origins from loading subresources - this behavior is commonly abused by phishing kits to quickly copy \"look and feel\" of your IP without having to host assets themselves.\n\n<b>References:</b>\n - [Semgrep Rule](https://semgrep.dev/r/python.flask.web.security_header.after_request.cors.after-request-corp.after-request-corp)\n - [https://academy.semgrep.dev/courses/security-headers](https://academy.semgrep.dev/courses/security-headers)\n - [https://cheatsheetseries.owasp.org/cheatsheets/HTTP_Headers_Cheat_Sheet.html](https://cheatsheetseries.owasp.org/cheatsheets/HTTP_Headers_Cheat_Sheet.html)\n - [https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/HTTP/Headers](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/HTTP/Headers)\n - [https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/HTTP/Headers/Content-Security-Policy](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/HTTP/Headers/Content-Security-Policy)\n - [https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/HTTP/Headers/Cross-Origin-Embedder-Policy](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/HTTP/Headers/Cross-Origin-Embedder-Policy)\n - [https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/HTTP/Headers/Cross-Origin-Opener-Policy](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/HTTP/Headers/Cross-Origin-Opener-Policy)\n - [https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/HTTP/Headers/Cross-Origin-Resource-Policy](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/HTTP/Headers/Cross-Origin-Resource-Policy)\n - [https://owasp.org/Top10/A05_2021-Security_Misconfiguration](https://owasp.org/Top10/A05_2021-Security_Misconfiguration)\n - [https://xsleaks.dev/](https://xsleaks.dev/)\n","text":"An after_request handler is setting one or more cross-origin resource sharing (CORS) headers but does not set the `Cross-Origin-Resource-Policy` header. This header prevents untrusted origins from loading subresources - this behavior is commonly abused by phishing kits to quickly copy \"look and feel\" of your IP without having to host assets themselves."},"helpUri":"https://semgrep.dev/r/python.flask.web.security_header.after_request.cors.after-request-corp.after-request-corp","id":"python.flask.web.security_header.after_request.cors.after-request-corp.after-request-corp","name":"python.flask.web.security_header.after_request.cors.after-request-corp.after-request-corp","properties":{"precision":"very-high","tags":["CWE-358: Improperly Implemented Security Check for Standard","HIGH CONFIDENCE","OWASP-A05:2021-Security misconfiguration","security"]},"shortDescription":{"text":"Semgrep Finding: python.flask.web.security_header.after_request.cors.after-request-corp.after-request-corp"}},{"defaultConfiguration":{"level":"note"},"fullDescription":{"text":"Found a `flask-cors` decorator with the default configuration. This will allow all origins to access the resource.If your application needs to support cross-origin requests, you should explicitly specify the origins you trust, even if that ends up being the wildcard origin. Being explicit about behavior makes it easier for future developers and security personnel to understand and review your source code."},"help":{"markdown":"Found a `flask-cors` decorator with the default configuration. This will allow all origins to access the resource.If your application needs to support cross-origin requests, you should explicitly specify the origins you trust, even if that ends up being the wildcard origin. Being explicit about behavior makes it easier for future developers and security personnel to understand and review your source code.\n\n<b>References:</b>\n - [Semgrep Rule](https://semgrep.dev/r/python.flask.web.security_header.flask-cors.flask-cors-unsafe-default.flask-cors-unsafe-default)\n - [https://academy.semgrep.dev/courses/security-headers](https://academy.semgrep.dev/courses/security-headers)\n - [https://cheatsheetseries.owasp.org/cheatsheets/HTTP_Headers_Cheat_Sheet.html](https://cheatsheetseries.owasp.org/cheatsheets/HTTP_Headers_Cheat_Sheet.html)\n - [https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/HTTP/Headers](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/HTTP/Headers)\n - [https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/HTTP/Headers/Content-Security-Policy](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/HTTP/Headers/Content-Security-Policy)\n - [https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/HTTP/Headers/Cross-Origin-Embedder-Policy](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/HTTP/Headers/Cross-Origin-Embedder-Policy)\n - [https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/HTTP/Headers/Cross-Origin-Opener-Policy](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/HTTP/Headers/Cross-Origin-Opener-Policy)\n - [https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/HTTP/Headers/Cross-Origin-Resource-Policy](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/HTTP/Headers/Cross-Origin-Resource-Policy)\n - [https://flask-cors.readthedocs.io/en/latest/configuration.html#default-values](https://flask-cors.readthedocs.io/en/latest/configuration.html#default-values)\n - [https://owasp.org/Top10/2025/A02_2025-Security_Misconfiguration/](https://owasp.org/Top10/2025/A02_2025-Security_Misconfiguration/)\n - [https://owasp.org/Top10/A05_2021-Security_Misconfiguration](https://owasp.org/Top10/A05_2021-Security_Misconfiguration)\n","text":"Found a `flask-cors` decorator with the default configuration. This will allow all origins to access the resource.If your application needs to support cross-origin requests, you should explicitly specify the origins you trust, even if that ends up being the wildcard origin. Being explicit about behavior makes it easier for future developers and security personnel to understand and review your source code."},"helpUri":"https://semgrep.dev/r/python.flask.web.security_header.flask-cors.flask-cors-unsafe-default.flask-cors-unsafe-default","id":"python.flask.web.security_header.flask-cors.flask-cors-unsafe-default.flask-cors-unsafe-default","name":"python.flask.web.security_header.flask-cors.flask-cors-unsafe-default.flask-cors-unsafe-default","properties":{"precision":"very-high","tags":["CWE-942: Permissive Cross-domain Policy with Untrusted Domains","HIGH CONFIDENCE","OWASP-A02:2025 - Security Misconfiguration","OWASP-A05:2021 - Security Misconfiguration","security"]},"shortDescription":{"text":"Semgrep Finding: python.flask.web.security_header.flask-cors.flask-cors-unsafe-default.flask-cors-unsafe-default"}},{"defaultConfiguration":{"level":"error"},"fullDescription":{"text":"Security middleware is setting one or more cross-origin resource sharing (CORS) headers but does not set the `Access-Control-Allow-Origin` header. Missing or weak values for this header allow arbitrary origins to read responses from your application. Setting a strong value for this header is especially recommended if your application's threat model includes 'straw purchasing' or reselling of paywalled content."},"help":{"markdown":"Security middleware is setting one or more cross-origin resource sharing (CORS) headers but does not set the `Access-Control-Allow-Origin` header. Missing or weak values for this header allow arbitrary origins to read responses from your application. Setting a strong value for this header is especially recommended if your application's threat model includes 'straw purchasing' or reselling of paywalled content.\n\n<b>References:</b>\n - [Semgrep Rule](https://semgrep.dev/r/python.flask.web.security_header.middleware.cors.middleware-acao.middleware-acao)\n - [https://academy.semgrep.dev/courses/security-headers](https://academy.semgrep.dev/courses/security-headers)\