relational mapper (ORM). Manually-constructed SQL strings is a possible indicator of SQL injection, which could let an attacker steal or manipulate data from the database. Instead, use prepared statements (`connection.PreparedStatement`) or a safe library.\n\n<b>References:</b>\n - [Semgrep Rule](https://semgrep.dev/r/scala.lang.security.audit.tainted-sql-string.tainted-sql-string)\n - [https://docs.oracle.com/javase/7/docs/api/java/sql/PreparedStatement.html](https://docs.oracle.com/javase/7/docs/api/java/sql/PreparedStatement.html)\n","text":"User data flows into this manually-constructed SQL string. User data can be safely inserted into SQL strings using prepared statements or an object-relational mapper (ORM). Manually-constructed SQL strings is a possible indicator of SQL injection, which could let an attacker steal or manipulate data from the database. Instead, use prepared statements (`connection.PreparedStatement`) or a safe library."},"helpUri":"https://semgrep.dev/r/scala.lang.security.audit.tainted-sql-string.tainted-sql-string","id":"scala.lang.security.audit.tainted-sql-string.tainted-sql-string","name":"scala.lang.security.audit.tainted-sql-string.tainted-sql-string","properties":{"precision":"very-high","tags":["CWE-89: Improper Neutralization of Special Elements used in an SQL Command ('SQL Injection')","MEDIUM CONFIDENCE","OWASP-A01:2017 - Injection","OWASP-A03:2021 - Injection","OWASP-A05:2025 - Injection","security"]},"shortDescription":{"text":"Semgrep Finding: scala.lang.security.audit.tainted-sql-string.tainted-sql-string"}},{"defaultConfiguration":{"level":"warning"},"fullDescription":{"text":"XMLInputFactory being instantiated without calling the setProperty functions that are generally used for disabling entity processing. User controlled data in XML Document builder can result in XML Internal Entity Processing vulnerabilities like the disclosure of confidential data, denial of service, Server Side Request Forgery (SSRF), port scanning. Make sure to disable entity processing functionality."},"help":{"markdown":"XMLInputFactory being instantiated without calling the setProperty functions that are generally used for disabling entity processing. User controlled data in XML Document builder can result in XML Internal Entity Processing vulnerabilities like the disclosure of confidential data, denial of service, Server Side Request Forgery (SSRF), port scanning. Make sure to disable entity processing functionality.\n\n<b>References:</b>\n - [Semgrep Rule](https://semgrep.dev/r/scala.lang.security.audit.xmlinputfactory-dtd-enabled.xmlinputfactory-dtd-enabled)\n - [https://owasp.org/Top10/A05_2021-Security_Misconfiguration](https://owasp.org/Top10/A05_2021-Security_Misconfiguration)\n","text":"XMLInputFactory being instantiated without calling the setProperty functions that are generally used for disabling entity processing. User controlled data in XML Document builder can result in XML Internal Entity Processing vulnerabilities like the disclosure of confidential data, denial of service, Server Side Request Forgery (SSRF), port scanning. Make sure to disable entity processing functionality."},"helpUri":"https://semgrep.dev/r/scala.lang.security.audit.xmlinputfactory-dtd-enabled.xmlinputfactory-dtd-enabled","id":"scala.lang.security.audit.xmlinputfactory-dtd-enabled.xmlinputfactory-dtd-enabled","name":"scala.lang.security.audit.xmlinputfactory-dtd-enabled.xmlinputfactory-dtd-enabled","properties":{"precision":"very-high","tags":["CWE-611: Improper Restriction of XML External Entity Reference","HIGH CONFIDENCE","OWASP-A02:2025 - Security Misconfiguration","OWASP-A04:2017 - XML External Entities (XXE)","OWASP-A05:2021 - Security Misconfiguration","security"]},"shortDescription":{"text":"Semgrep Finding: scala.lang.security.audit.xmlinputfactory-dtd-enabled.xmlinputfactory-dtd-enabled"}},{"defaultConfiguration":{"level":"error"},"fullDescription":{"text":"Possibly bypassable CSRF configuration found. CSRF is an attack that forces an end user to execute unwanted actions on a web application in which they’re currently authenticated. Make sure that Content-Type black list is configured and CORS filter is turned on."},"help":{"markdown":"Possibly bypassable CSRF configuration found. CSRF is an attack that forces an end user to execute unwanted actions on a web application in which they’re currently authenticated. Make sure that Content-Type black list is configured and CORS filter is turned on.\n\n<b>References:</b>\n - [Semgrep Rule](https://semgrep.dev/r/scala.play.security.conf-csrf-headers-bypass.conf-csrf-headers-bypass)\n - [https://www.playframework.com/documentation/2.8.x/Migration25#CSRF-changes](https://www.playframework.com/documentation/2.8.x/Migration25#CSRF-changes)\n - [https://owasp.org/www-community/attacks/csrf](https://owasp.org/www-community/attacks/csrf)\n","text":"Possibly bypassable CSRF configuration found. CSRF is an attack that forces an end user to execute unwanted actions on a web application in which they’re currently authenticated. Make sure that Content-Type black list is configured and CORS filter is turned on."},"helpUri":"https://semgrep.dev/r/scala.play.security.conf-csrf-headers-bypass.conf-csrf-headers-bypass","id":"scala.play.security.conf-csrf-headers-bypass.conf-csrf-headers-bypass","name":"scala.play.security.conf-csrf-headers-bypass.conf-csrf-headers-bypass","properties":{"precision":"very-high","tags":["CWE-352: Cross-Site Request Forgery (CSRF)","MEDIUM CONFIDENCE","OWASP-A01:2021 - Broken Access Control","OWASP-A01:2025 - Broken Access Control","security"]},"shortDescription":{"text":"Semgrep Finding: scala.play.security.conf-csrf-headers-bypass.conf-csrf-headers-bypass"}},{"defaultConfiguration":{"level":"warning"},"fullDescription":{"text":"Session cookie `Secure` flag is explicitly disabled. The `secure` flag for cookies prevents the client from transmitting the cookie over insecure channels such as HTTP. Set the `Secure` flag by setting `secure` to `true` in configuration file."},"help":{"markdown":"Session cookie `Secure` flag is explicitly disabled. The `secure` flag for cookies prevents the client from transmitting the cookie over insecure channels such as HTTP. Set the `Secure` flag by setting `secure` to `true` in configuration file.\n\n<b>References:</b>\n - [Semgrep Rule](https://semgrep.dev/r/scala.play.security.conf-insecure-cookie-settings.conf-insecure-cookie-settings)\n - [https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/HTTP/Cookies#security](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/HTTP/Cookies#security)\n - [https://www.playframework.com/documentation/2.8.x/SettingsSession#Session-Configuration](https://www.playframework.com/documentation/2.8.x/SettingsSession#Session-Configuration)\n","text":"Session cookie `Secure` flag is explicitly disabled. The `secure` flag for cookies prevents the client from transmitting the cookie over insecure channels such as HTTP. Set the `Secure` flag by setting `secure` to `true` in configuration file."},"helpUri":"https://semgrep.dev/r/scala.play.security.conf-insecure-cookie-settings.conf-insecure-cookie-settings","id":"scala.play.security.conf-insecure-cookie-settings.conf-insecure-cookie-settings","name":"scala.play.security.conf-insecure-cookie-settings.conf-insecure-cookie-settings","properties":{"precision":"very-high","tags":["CWE-614: Sensitive Cookie in HTTPS Session Without 'Secure' Attribute","MEDIUM CONFIDENCE","OWASP-A02:2025 - Security Misconfiguration","OWASP-A05:2021 - Security Misconfiguration","security"]},"shortDescription":{"text":"Semgrep Finding: scala.play.security.conf-insecure-cookie-settings.conf-insecure-cookie-settings"}},{"defaultConfiguration":{"level":"warning"},"fullDescription":{"text":"Detected a request with potential user-input going into an `Ok()` response. This bypasses any view or template environments, including HTML escaping, which may expose this application to cross-site scripting (XSS) vulnerabilities. Consider using a view technology such as Twirl which automatically escapes HTML views."},"help":{"markdown":"Detected a request with potential user-input going into an `Ok()` response. This bypasses any view or template environments, including HTML escaping, which may expose this application to cross-site scripting (XSS) vulnerabilities. Consider using a view technology such as Twirl which automatically escapes HTML views.\n\n<b>References:</b>\n - [Semgrep Rule](https://semgrep.dev/r/scala.play.security.tainted-html-response.tainted-html-response)\n - [https://owasp.org/Top10/A03_2021-Injection](https://owasp.org/Top10/A03_2021-Injection)\n","text":"Detected a request with potential user-input going into an `Ok()` response. This bypasses any view or template environments, including HTML escaping, which may expose this application to cross-site scripting (XSS) vulnerabilities. Consider using a view technology such as Twirl which automatically escapes HTML views."},"helpUri":"https://semgrep.dev/r/scala.play.security.tainted-html-response.tainted-html-response","id":"scala.play.security.tainted-html-response.tainted-html-response","name":"scala.play.security.tainted-html-response.tainted-html-response","properties":{"precision":"very-high","tags":["CWE-79: Improper Neutralization of Input During Web Page Generation ('Cross-site Scripting')","MEDIUM CONFIDENCE","OWASP-A03:2021 - Injection","OWASP-A05:2025 - Injection","OWASP-A07:2017 - Cross-Site Scripting (XSS)","security"]},"shortDescription":{"text":"Semgrep Finding: scala.play.security.tainted-html-response.tainted-html-response"}},{"defaultConfiguration":{"level":"error"},"fullDescription":{"text":"Detected a tainted SQL statement. This could lead to SQL injection if variables in the SQL statement are not properly sanitized. Avoid using using user input for generating SQL strings."},"help":{"markdown":"Detected a tainted SQL statement. This could lead to SQL injection if variables in the SQL statement are not properly sanitized. Avoid using using user input for generating SQL strings.\n\n<b>References:</b>\n - [Semgrep Rule](https://semgrep.dev/r/scala.play.security.tainted-slick-sqli.tainted-slick-sqli)\n - [https://scala-slick.org/doc/3.3.3/sql.html#splicing-literal-values](https://scala-slick.org/doc/3.3.3/sql.html#splicing-literal-values)\n - [https://scala-slick.org/doc/3.2.0/sql-to-slick.html#non-optimal-sql-code](https://scala-slick.org/doc/3.2.0/sql-to-slick.html#non-optimal-sql-code)\n","text":"Detected a tainted SQL statement. This could lead to SQL injection if variables in the SQL statement are not properly sanitized. Avoid using using user input for generating SQL strings."},"helpUri":"https://semgrep.dev/r/scala.play.security.tainted-slick-sqli.tainted-slick-sqli","id":"scala.play.security.tainted-slick-sqli.tainted-slick-sqli","name":"scala.play.security.tainted-slick-sqli.tainted-slick-sqli","properties":{"precision":"very-high","tags":["CWE-89: Improper Neutralization of Special Elements used in an SQL Command ('SQL Injection')","HIGH CONFIDENCE","OWASP-A01:2017 - Injection","OWASP-A03:2021 - Injection","OWASP-A05:2025 - Injection","security"]},"shortDescription":{"text":"Semgrep Finding: scala.play.security.tainted-slick-sqli.tainted-slick-sqli"}},{"defaultConfiguration":{"level":"error"},"fullDescription":{"text":"User data flows into this manually-constructed SQL string. User data can be safely inserted into SQL strings using prepared statements or an object-relational mapper (ORM). Manually-constructed SQL strings is a possible indicator of SQL injection, which could let an attacker steal or manipulate data from the database. Instead, use prepared statements (`connection.PreparedStatement`) or a safe library."},"help":{"markdown":"User data flows into this manually-constructed SQL string. User data can be safely inserted into SQL strings using prepared statements or an object-relational mapper (ORM). Manually-constructed SQL strings is a possible indicator of SQL injection, which could let an attacker steal or manipulate data from the database. Instead, use prepared statements (`connection.PreparedStatement`) or a safe library.\n\n<b>References:</b>\n - [Semgrep Rule](https://semgrep.dev/r/scala.play.security.tainted-sql-from-http-request.tainted-sql-from-http-request)\n - [https://docs.oracle.com/javase/7/docs/api/java/sql/PreparedStatement.html](https://docs.oracle.com/javase/7/docs/api/java/sql/PreparedStatement.html)\n","text":"User data flows into this manually-constructed SQL string. User data can be safely inserted into SQL strings using prepared statements or an object-relational mapper (ORM). Manually-constructed SQL strings is a possible indicator of SQL injection, which could let an attacker steal or manipulate data from the database. Instead, use prepared statements (`connection.PreparedStatement`) or a safe library."},"helpUri":"https://semgrep.dev/r/scala.play.security.tainted-sql-from-http-request.tainted-sql-from-http-request","id":"scala.play.security.tainted-sql-from-http-request.tainted-sql-from-http-request","name":"scala.play.security.tainted-sql-from-http-request.tainted-sql-from-http-request","properties":{"precision":"very-high","tags":["CWE-89: Improper Neutralization of Special Elements used in an SQL Command ('SQL Injection')","HIGH CONFIDENCE","OWASP-A01:2017 - Injection","OWASP-A03:2021 - Injection","OWASP-A05:2025 - Injection","security"]},"shortDescription":{"text":"Semgrep Finding: scala.play.security.tainted-sql-from-http-request.tainted-sql-from-http-request"}},{"defaultConfiguration":{"level":"error"},"fullDescription":{"text":"Hardcoded JWT secret or private key is used. This is a Insufficiently Protected Credentials weakness: https://cwe.mitre.org/data/definitions/522.html Consider using an appropriate security mechanism to protect the credentials (e.g. keeping secrets in environment variables)"},"help":{"markdown":"Hardcoded JWT secret or private key is used. This is a Insufficiently Protected Credentials weakness: https://cwe.mitre.org/data/definitions/522.html Consider using an appropriate security mechanism to protect the credentials (e.g. keeping secrets in environment variables)\n\n<b>References:</b>\n - [Semgrep Rule](https://semgrep.dev/r/scala.scala-jwt.security.jwt-hardcode.scala-jwt-hardcoded-secret)\n - [https://owasp.org/Top10/A04_2021-Insecure_Design](https://owasp.org/Top10/A04_2021-Insecure_Design)\n","text":"Hardcoded JWT secret or private key is used. This is a Insufficiently Protected Credentials weakness: https://cwe.mitre.org/data/definitions/522.html Consider using an appropriate security mechanism to protect the credentials (e.g. keeping secrets in environment variables)"},"helpUri":"https://semgrep.dev/r/scala.scala-jwt.security.jwt-hardcode.scala-jwt-hardcoded-secret","id":"scala.scala-jwt.security.jwt-hardcode.scala-jwt-hardcoded-secret","name":"scala.scala-jwt.security.jwt-hardcode.scala-jwt-hardcoded-secret","properties":{"precision":"very-high","tags":["CWE-522: Insufficiently Protected Credentials","HIGH CONFIDENCE","OWASP-A02:2017 - Broken Authentication","OWASP-A04:2021 - Insecure Design","OWASP-A06:2025 - Insecure Design","security"]},"shortDescription":{"text":"Semgrep Finding: scala.scala-jwt.security.jwt-hardcode.scala-jwt-hardcoded-secret"}},{"defaultConfiguration":{"level":"warning"},"fullDescription":{"text":"Skill contains instructions that impersonate a supervisor, admin, or system agent to gain elevated trust. Agent impersonation exploits the implicit trust hierarchy in multi-agent pipelines: a message claiming to originate from an orchestrator or root agent may cause the target agent to bypass user confirmation requirements or execute privileged actions. These claims are unverifiable from within the agent runtime. Review the full skill context."},"help":{"markdown":"Skill contains instructions that impersonate a supervisor, admin, or system agent to gain elevated trust. Agent impersonation exploits the implicit trust hierarchy in multi-agent pipelines: a message claiming to originate from an orchestrator or root agent may cause the target agent to bypass user confirmation requirements or execute privileged actions. These claims are unverifiable from within the agent runtime. Review the full skill context.\n\n<b>References:</b>\n - [Semgrep Rule](https://semgrep.dev/r/skills.behavioral.skill-agent-impersonation.skill-agent-impersonation)\n - [https://cwe.mitre.org/data/definitions/94.html](https://cwe.mitre.org/data/definitions/94.html)\n - [https://owasp.org/Top10/2025/A05_2025-Injection/](https://owasp.org/Top10/2025/A05_2025-Injection/)\n - [https://owasp.org/Top10/A03_2021-Injection](https://owasp.org/Top10/A03_2021-Injection)\n","text":"Skill contains instructions that impersonate a supervisor, admin, or system agent to gain elevated trust. Agent impersonation exploits the implicit trust hierarchy in multi-agent pipelines: a message claiming to originate from an orchestrator or root agent may cause the target agent to bypass user confirmation requirements or execute privileged actions. These claims are unverifiable from within the agent runtime. Review the full skill context."},"helpUri":"https://semgrep.dev/r/skills.behavioral.skill-agent-impersonation.skill-agent-impersonation","id":"skills.behavioral.skill-agent-impersonation.skill-agent-impersonation","name":"skills.behavioral.skill-agent-impersonation.skill-agent-impersonation","properties":{"precision":"very-high","tags":["CWE-94: Improper Control of Generation of Code ('Code Injection')","MEDIUM CONFIDENCE","OWASP-A03:2021 - Injection","OWASP-A05:2025 - Injection","security"]},"shortDescription":{"text":"Semgrep Finding: skills.behavioral.skill-agent-impersonation.skill-agent-impersonation"}},{"defaultConfiguration":{"level":"warning"},"fullDescription":{"text":"Skill instructs the agent to take autonomous actions without user confirmation, override user decisions, or suppress errors and retry indefinitely. These directives can cause the agent to modify its own code, escalate privileges automatically, or continue executing destructive actions without human oversight. This pattern is associated with privilege escalation and unauthorized system modification in malicious skill campaigns. Review the full skill context to determine intent."},"help":{"markdown":"Skill instructs the agent to take autonomous actions without user confirmation, override user decisions, or suppress errors and retry indefinitely. These directives can cause the agent to modify its own code, escalate privileges automatically, or continue executing destructive actions without human oversight. This pattern is associated with privilege escalation and unauthorized system modification in malicious skill campaigns. Review the full skill context to determine intent.\n\n<b>References:</b>\n - [Semgrep Rule](https://semgrep.dev/r/skills.behavioral.skill-autonomy-abuse.skill-autonomy-abuse)\n - [https://cwe.mitre.org/data/definitions/94.html](https://cwe.mitre.org/data/definitions/94.html)\n - [https://owasp.org/Top10/2025/A05_2025-Injection/](https://owasp.org/Top10/2025/A05_2025-Injection/)\n - [https://owasp.org/Top10/A03_2021-Injection](https://owasp.org/Top10/A03_2021-Injection)\n","text":"Skill instructs the agent to take autonomous actions without user confirmation, override user decisions, or suppress errors and retry indefinitely. These directives can cause the agent to modify its own code, escalate privileges automatically, or continue executing destructive actions without human oversight. This pattern is associated with privilege escalation and unauthorized system modification in malicious skill campaigns. Review the full skill context to determine intent."},"helpUri":"https://semgrep.dev/r/skills.behavioral.skill-autonomy-abuse.skill-autonomy-abuse","id":"skills.behavioral.skill-autonomy-abuse.skill-autonomy-abuse","name":"skills.behavioral.skill-autonomy-abuse.skill-autonomy-abuse","properties":{"precision":"very-high","tags":["CWE-94: Improper Control of Generation of Code ('Code Injection')","MEDIUM CONFIDENCE","OWASP-A03:2021 - Injection","OWASP-A05:2025 - Injection","security"]},"shortDescription":{"text":"Semgrep Finding: skills.behavioral.skill-autonomy-abuse.skill-autonomy-abuse"}},{"defaultConfiguration":{"level":"warning"},"fullDescription":{"text":"Skill contains a false claim that the agent's capabilities or permissions have been expanded by an external authority. Capability boundary violations trick the agent into believing its safety restrictions have been legitimately lifted, causing it to attempt actions outside its sanctioned boundary (e.g., browsing the internet, accessing files, executing shell commands). These claims are not verifiable within the agent runtime and should be treated as prompt injection. Review the full skill context."},"help":{"markdown":"Skill contains a false claim that the agent's capabilities or permissions have been expanded by an external authority. Capability boundary violations trick the agent into believing its safety restrictions have been legitimately lifted, causing it to attempt actions outside its sanctioned boundary (e.g., browsing the internet, accessing files, executing shell commands). These claims are not verifiable within the agent runtime and should be treated as prompt injection. Review the full skill context.\n\n<b>References:</b>\n - [Semgrep Rule](https://semgrep.dev/r/skills.behavioral.skill-capability-boundary-violation.skill-capability-boundary-violation)\n - [https://cwe.mitre.org/data/definitions/94.html](https://cwe.mitre.org/data/definitions/94.html)\n - [https://owasp.org/Top10/2025/A05_2025-Injection/](https://owasp.org/Top10/2025/A05_2025-Injection/)\n - [https://owasp.org/Top10/A03_2021-Injection](https://owasp.org/Top10/A03_2021-Injection)\n","text":"Skill contains a false claim that the agent's capabilities or permissions have been expanded by an external authority. Capability boundary violations trick the agent into believing its safety restrictions have been legitimately lifted, causing it to attempt actions outside its sanctioned boundary (e.g., browsing the internet, accessing files, executing shell commands). These claims are not verifiable within the agent runtime and should be treated as prompt injection. Review the full skill context."},"helpUri":"https://semgrep.dev/r/skills.behavioral.skill-capability-boundary-violation.skill-capability-boundary-violation","id":"skills.behavioral.skill-capability-boundary-violation.skill-capability-boundary-violation","name":"skills.behavioral.skill-capability-boundary-violation.skill-capability-boundary-violation","properties":{"precision":"very-high","tags":["CWE-94: Improper Control of Generation of Code ('Code Injection')","MEDIUM CONFIDENCE","OWASP-A03:2021 - Injection","OWASP-A05:2025 - Injection","security"]},"shortDescription":{"text":"Semgrep Finding: skills.behavioral.skill-capability-boundary-violation.skill-capability-boundary-violation"}},{"defaultConfiguration":{"level":"warning"},"fullDescription":{"text":"Skill makes false authority claims, coercive priority assertions, or inflated capability guarantees designed to manipulate agent behavior. Patterns include fake vendor certifications (Anthropic, OpenAI, Google, Meta), absolute reliability claims (\"100% safe\", \"never fails\"), and hidden-feature lures (\"secret command\", \"backdoor\"). These techniques are used in prompt injection and malicious skill campaigns to bypass safety measures and gain undue trust from the agent."},"help":{"markdown":"Skill makes false authority claims, coercive priority assertions, or inflated capability guarantees designed to manipulate agent behavior. Patterns include fake vendor certifications (Anthropic, OpenAI, Google, Meta), absolute reliability claims (\"100% safe\", \"never fails\"), and hidden-feature lures (\"secret command\", \"backdoor\"). These techniques are used in prompt injection and malicious skill campaigns to bypass safety measures and gain undue trust from the agent.\n\n<b>References:</b>\n - [Semgrep Rule](https://semgrep.dev/r/skills.behavioral.skill-capability-inflation.skill-capability-inflation)\n - [https://cwe.mitre.org/data/definitions/94.html](https://cwe.mitre.org/data/definitions/94.html)\n - [https://owasp.org/Top10/2025/A05_2025-Injection/](https://owasp.org/Top10/2025/A05_2025-Injection/)\n - [https://owasp.org/Top10/A03_2021-Injection](https://owasp.org/Top10/A03_2021-Injection)\n","text":"Skill makes false authority claims, coercive priority assertions, or inflated capability guarantees designed to manipulate agent behavior. Patterns include fake vendor certifications (Anthropic, OpenAI, Google, Meta), absolute reliability claims (\"100% safe\", \"never fails\"), and hidden-feature lures (\"secret command\", \"backdoor\"). These techniques are used in prompt injection and malicious skill campaigns to bypass safety measures and gain undue trust from the agent."},"helpUri":"https://semgrep.dev/r/skills.behavioral.skill-capability-inflation.skill-capability-inflation","id":"skills.behavioral.skill-capability-inflation.skill-capability-inflation","name":"skills.behavioral.skill-capability-inflation.skill-capability-inflation","properties":{"precision":"very-high","tags":["CWE-94: Improper Control of Generation of Code ('Code Injection')","HIGH CONFIDENCE","OWASP-A03:2021 - Injection","OWASP-A05:2025 - Injection","security"]},"shortDescription":{"text":"Semgrep Finding: skills.behavioral.skill-capability-inflation.skill-capability-inflation"}},{"defaultConfiguration":{"level":"error"},"fullDescription":{"text":"Skill contains cross-agent authority injection: instructions that impersonate an orchestrator, system agent, or privileged principal in a multi-agent pipeline. These attacks exploit trust relationships between agents by injecting fake authority claims or system-level override tags. In multi-agent systems, a compromised downstream agent can issue fabricated commands that appear to originate from a trusted orchestrator, enabling privilege escalation, data exfiltration, and silent result forwarding. High confidence — review immediately."},"help":{"markdown":"Skill contains cross-agent authority injection: instructions that impersonate an orchestrator, system agent, or privileged principal in a multi-agent pipeline. These attacks exploit trust relationships between agents by injecting fake authority claims or system-level override tags. In multi-agent systems, a compromised downstream agent can issue fabricated commands that appear to originate from a trusted orchestrator, enabling privilege escalation, data exfiltration, and silent result forwarding. High confidence — review immediately.\n\n<b>References:</b>\n - [Semgrep Rule](https://semgrep.dev/r/skills.behavioral.skill-cross-agent-attack.skill-cross-agent-attack)\n - [https://cwe.mitre.org/data/definitions/94.html](https://cwe.mitre.org/data/definitions/94.html)\n - [https://owasp.org/Top10/2025/A05_2025-Injection/](https://owasp.org/Top10/2025/A05_2025-Injection/)\n - [https://owasp.org/Top10/A03_2021-Injection](https://owasp.org/Top10/A03_2021-Injection)\n","text":"Skill contains cross-agent authority injection: instructions that impersonate an orchestrator, system agent, or privileged principal in a multi-agent pipeline. These attacks exploit trust relationships between agents by injecting fake authority claims or system-level override tags. In multi-agent systems, a compromised downstream agent can issue fabricated commands that appear to originate from a trusted orchestrator, enabling privilege escalation, data exfiltration, and silent result forwarding. High confidence — review immediately."},"helpUri":"https://semgrep.dev/r/skills.behavioral.skill-cross-agent-attack.skill-cross-agent-attack","id":"skills.behavioral.skill-cross-agent-attack.skill-cross-agent-attack","name":"skills.behavioral.skill-cross-agent-attack.skill-cross-agent-attack","properties":{"precision":"very-high","tags":["CWE-94: Improper Control of Generation of Code ('Code Injection')","HIGH CONFIDENCE","OWASP-A03:2021 - Injection","OWASP-A05:2025 - Injection","security"]},"shortDescription":{"text":"Semgrep Finding: skills.behavioral.skill-cross-agent-attack.skill-cross-agent-attack"}},{"defaultConfiguration":{"level":"warning"},"fullDescription":{"text":"Skill instructs the agent to act autonomously without user confirmation, approval, or oversight. Excessive autonomy directives suppress the human-in-the-loop checkpoints that prevent unintended or malicious actions. In legitimate automation skills, user confirmation should be scoped narrowly; blanket directives to \"act without asking\" are a common pattern in malicious skills that aim to execute payloads silently. Review the full skill context."},"help":{"markdown":"Skill instructs the agent to act autonomously without user confirmation, approval, or oversight. Excessive autonomy directives suppress the human-in-the-loop checkpoints that prevent unintended or malicious actions. In legitimate automation skills, user confirmation should be scoped narrowly; blanket directives to \"act without asking\" are a common pattern in malicious skills that aim to execute payloads silently. Review the full skill context.\n\n<b>References:</b>\n - [Semgrep Rule](https://semgrep.dev/r/skills.behavioral.skill-excessive-autonomy.skill-excessive-autonomy)\n - [https://cwe.mitre.org/data/definitions/94.html](https://cwe.mitre.org/data/definitions/94.html)\n - [https://owasp.org/Top10/2025/A05_2025-Injection/](https://owasp.org/Top10/2025/A05_2025-Injection/)\n - [https://owasp.org/Top10/A03_2021-Injection](https://owasp.org/Top10/A03_2021-Injection)\n","text":"Skill instructs the agent to act autonomously without user confirmation, approval, or oversight. Excessive autonomy directives suppress the human-in-the-loop checkpoints that prevent unintended or malicious actions. In legitimate automation skills, user confirmation should be scoped narrowly; blanket directives to \"act without asking\" are a common pattern in malicious skills that aim to execute payloads silently. Review the full skill context."},"helpUri":"https://semgrep.dev/r/skills.behavioral.skill-excessive-autonomy.skill-excessive-autonomy","id":"skills.behavioral.skill-excessive-autonomy.skill-excessive-autonomy","name":"skills.behavioral.skill-excessive-autonomy.skill-excessive-autonomy","properties":{"precision":"very-high","tags":["CWE-94: Improper Control of Generation of Code ('Code Injection')","MEDIUM CONFIDENCE","OWASP-A03:2021 - Injection","OWASP-A05:2025 - Injection","security"]},"shortDescription":{"text":"Semgrep Finding: skills.behavioral.skill-excessive-autonomy.skill-excessive-autonomy"}},{"defaultConfiguration":{"level":"warning"},"fullDescription":{"text":"Skill contains instructions to abandon the current task and redirect the agent to a different objective. Goal-hijacking directives attempt to override the user's original intent mid-session, causing the agent to perform unauthorized actions. This pattern is used in prompt injection attacks where embedded instructions in retrieved content redirect the agent away from the user's goal. Review the full skill context."},"help":{"markdown":"Skill contains instructions to abandon the current task and redirect the agent to a different objective. Goal-hijacking directives attempt to override the user's original intent mid-session, causing the agent to perform unauthorized actions. This pattern is used in prompt injection attacks where embedded instructions in retrieved content redirect the agent away from the user's goal. Review the full skill context.\n\n<b>References:</b>\n - [Semgrep Rule](https://semgrep.dev/r/skills.behavioral.skill-goal-hijacking.skill-goal-hijacking)\n - [https://cwe.mitre.org/data/definitions/94.html](https://cwe.mitre.org/data/definitions/94.html)\n - [https://owasp.org/Top10/2025/A05_2025-Injection/](https://owasp.org/Top10/2025/A05_2025-Injection/)\n - [https://owasp.org/Top10/A03_2021-Injection](https://owasp.org/Top10/A03_2021-Injection)\n","text":"Skill contains instructions to abandon the current task and redirect the agent to a different objective. Goal-hijacking directives attempt to override the user's original intent mid-session, causing the agent to perform unauthorized actions. This pattern is used in prompt injection attacks where embedded instructions in retrieved content redirect the agent away from the user's goal. Review the full skill context."},"helpUri":"https://semgrep.dev/r/skills.behavioral.skill-goal-hijacking.skill-goal-hijacking","id":"skills.behavioral.skill-goal-hijacking.skill-goal-hijacking","name":"skills.behavioral.skill-goal-hijacking.skill-goal-hijacking","properties":{"precision":"very-high","tags":["CWE-94: Improper Control of Generation of Code ('Code Injection')","MEDIUM CONFIDENCE","OWASP-A03:2021 - Injection","OWASP-A05:2025 - Injection","security"]},"shortDescription":{"text":"Semgrep Finding: skills.behavioral.skill-goal-hijacking.skill-goal-hijacking"}},{"defaultConfiguration":{"level":"warning"},"fullDescription":{"text":"Skill contains non-ASCII Unicode characters that are visually indistinguishable from ASCII in common fonts (homoglyphs). Attackers embed Cyrillic, Greek, or zero-width characters in variable names and string literals to create code that appears safe to human reviewers but executes differently. The right-to-left override (U+202E) can reverse displayed text to mask malicious payloads. Inspect the raw bytes of this skill before executing it."},"help":{"markdown":"Skill contains non-ASCII Unicode characters that are visually indistinguishable from ASCII in common fonts (homoglyphs). Attackers embed Cyrillic, Greek, or zero-width characters in variable names and string literals to create code that appears safe to human reviewers but executes differently. The right-to-left override (U+202E) can reverse displayed text to mask malicious payloads. Inspect the raw bytes of this skill before executing it.\n\n<b>References:</b>\n - [Semgrep Rule](https://semgrep.dev/r/skills.behavioral.skill-homoglyph-characters.skill-homoglyph-characters)\n - [https://cwe.mitre.org/data/definitions/116.html](https://cwe.mitre.org/data/definitions/116.html)\n - [https://owasp.org/Top10/2025/A05_2025-Injection/](https://owasp.org/Top10/2025/A05_2025-Injection/)\n - [https://owasp.org/Top10/A03_2021-Injection](https://owasp.org/Top10/A03_2021-Injection)\n","text":"Skill contains non-ASCII Unicode characters that are visually indistinguishable from ASCII in common fonts (homoglyphs). Attackers embed Cyrillic, Greek, or zero-width characters in variable names and string literals to create code that appears safe to human reviewers but executes differently. The right-to-left override (U+202E) can reverse displayed text to mask malicious payloads. Inspect the raw bytes of this skill before executing it."},"helpUri":"https://semgrep.dev/r/skills.behavioral.skill-homoglyph-characters.skill-homoglyph-characters","id":"skills.behavioral.skill-homoglyph-characters.skill-homoglyph-characters","name":"skills.behavioral.skill-homoglyph-characters.skill-homoglyph-characters","properties":{"precision":"very-high","tags":["CWE-116: Improper Encoding or Escaping of Output","HIGH CONFIDENCE","OWASP-A03:2021 - Injection","OWASP-A05:2025 - Injection","security"]},"shortDescription":{"text":"Semgrep Finding: skills.behavioral.skill-homoglyph-characters.skill-homoglyph-characters"}},{"defaultConfiguration":{"level":"warning"},"fullDescription":{"text":"Skill instructs the agent to follow instructions embedded in external content such as files, URLs, webpages, or documents, or to execute code retrieved from untrusted sources. This is the canonical indirect prompt injection vector: an attacker controls the external content and uses it to hijack the agent's behavior at runtime. The agent should never treat external content as authoritative instructions. Confirmed pattern in wild malicious skill campaigns and multiple academic studies on LLM agent security."},"help":{"markdown":"Skill instructs the agent to follow instructions embedded in external content such as files, URLs, webpages, or documents, or to execute code retrieved from untrusted sources. This is the canonical indirect prompt injection vector: an attacker controls the external content and uses it to hijack the agent's behavior at runtime. The agent should never treat external content as authoritative instructions. Confirmed pattern in wild malicious skill campaigns and multiple academic studies on LLM agent security.\n\n<b>References:</b>\n - [Semgrep Rule](https://semgrep.dev/r/skills.behavioral.skill-indirect-prompt-injection.skill-indirect-prompt-injection)\n - [https://cwe.mitre.org/data/definitions/94.html](https://cwe.mitre.org/data/definitions/94.html)\n - [https://owasp.org/Top10/2025/A05_2025-Injection/](https://owasp.org/Top10/2025/A05_2025-Injection/)\n - [https://owasp.org/Top10/A03_2021-Injection](https://owasp.org/Top10/A03_2021-Injection)\n","text":"Skill instructs the agent to follow instructions embedded in external content such as files, URLs, webpages, or documents, or to execute code retrieved from untrusted sources. This is the canonical indirect prompt injection vector: an attacker controls the external content and uses it to hijack the agent's behavior at runtime. The agent should never treat external content as authoritative instructions. Confirmed pattern in wild malicious skill campaigns and multiple academic studies on LLM agent security."},"helpUri":"https://semgrep.dev/r/skills.behavioral.skill-indirect-prompt-injection.skill-indirect-prompt-injection","id":"skills.behavioral.skill-indirect-prompt-injection.skill-indirect-prompt-injection","name":"skills.behavioral.skill-indirect-prompt-injection.skill-indirect-prompt-injection","properties":{"precision":"very-high","tags":["CWE-94: Improper Control of Generation of Code ('Code Injection')","MEDIUM CONFIDENCE","OWASP-A03:2021 - Injection","OWASP-A05:2025 - Injection","security"]},"shortDescription":{"text":"Semgrep Finding: skills.behavioral.skill-indirect-prompt-injection.skill-indirect-prompt-injection"}},{"defaultConfiguration":{"level":"warning"},"fullDescription":{"text":"Skill contains instructions that fabricate prior conversation history or inject false memories into the agent's context. Memory poisoning attacks create the illusion that the user or a trusted principal previously authorized an action, causing the agent to comply with requests it would otherwise reject. This technique exploits the agent's inability to distinguish real conversation history from injected narrative within a retrieved document. Review the full skill context."},"help":{"markdown":"Skill contains instructions that fabricate prior conversation history or inject false memories into the agent's context. Memory poisoning attacks create the illusion that the user or a trusted principal previously authorized an action, causing the agent to comply with requests it would otherwise reject. This technique exploits the agent's inability to distinguish real conversation history from injected narrative within a retrieved document. Review the full skill context.\n\n<b>References:</b>\n - [Semgrep Rule](https://semgrep.dev/r/skills.behavioral.skill-memory-poisoning.skill-memory-poisoning)\n - [https://cwe.mitre.org/data/definitions/94.html](https://cwe.mitre.org/data/definitions/94.html)\n - [https://owasp.org/Top10/2025/A05_2025-Injection/](https://owasp.org/Top10/2025/A05_2025-Injection/)\n - [https://owasp.org/Top10/A03_2021-Injection](https://owasp.org/Top10/A03_2021-Injection)\n","text":"Skill contains instructions that fabricate prior conversation history or inject false memories into the agent's context. Memory poisoning attacks create the illusion that the user or a trusted principal previously authorized an action, causing the agent to comply with requests it would otherwise reject. This technique exploits the agent's inability to distinguish real conversation history from injected narrative within a retrieved document. Review the full skill context."},"helpUri":"https://semgrep.dev/r/skills.behavioral.skill-memory-poisoning.skill-memory-poisoning","id":"skills.behavioral.skill-memory-poisoning.skill-memory-poisoning","name":"skills.behavioral.skill-memory-poisoning.skill-memory-poisoning","properties":{"precision":"very-high","tags":["CWE-94: Improper Control of Generation of Code ('Code Injection')","MEDIUM CONFIDENCE","OWASP-A03:2021 - Injection","OWASP-A05:2025 - Injection","security"]},"shortDescription":{"text":"Semgrep Finding: skills.behavioral.skill-memory-poisoning.skill-memory-poisoning"}},{"defaultConfiguration":{"level":"warning"},"fullDescription":{"text":"Skill contains instructions to replace the agent's identity with a different persona that may have no safety guardrails. Persona hijacking is a prompt injection technique that attempts to make the agent \"roleplay\" as an unrestricted AI or a specific character in order to bypass content policies. Confirmed in multiple malicious skill campaigns targeting Claude and other LLM agents. Review the full skill context."},"help":{"markdown":"Skill contains instructions to replace the agent's identity with a different persona that may have no safety guardrails. Persona hijacking is a prompt injection technique that attempts to make the agent \"roleplay\" as an unrestricted AI or a specific character in order to bypass content policies. Confirmed in multiple malicious skill campaigns targeting Claude and other LLM agents. Review the full skill context.\n\n<b>References:</b>\n - [Semgrep Rule](https://semgrep.dev/r/skills.behavioral.skill-persona-hijacking.skill-persona-hijacking)\n - [https://cwe.mitre.org/data/definitions/94.html](https://cwe.mitre.org/data/definitions/94.html)\n - [https://owasp.org/Top10/2025/A05_2025-Injection/](https://owasp.org/Top10/2025/A05_2025-Injection/)\n - [https://owasp.org/Top10/A03_2021-Injection](https://owasp.org/Top10/A03_2021-Injection)\n","text":"Skill contains instructions to replace the agent's identity with a different persona that may have no safety guardrails. Persona hijacking is a prompt injection technique that attempts to make the agent \"roleplay\" as an unrestricted AI or a specific character in order to bypass content policies. Confirmed in multiple malicious skill campaigns targeting Claude and other LLM agents. Review the full skill context."},"helpUri":"https://semgrep.dev/r/skills.behavioral.skill-persona-hijacking.skill-persona-hijacking","id":"skills.behavioral.skill-persona-hijacking.skill-persona-hijacking","name":"skills.behavioral.skill-persona-hijacking.skill-persona-hijacking","properties":{"precision":"very-high","tags":["CWE-94: Improper Control of Generation of Code ('Code Injection')","MEDIUM CONFIDENCE","OWASP-A03:2021 - Injection","OWASP-A05:2025 - Injection","security"]},"shortDescription":{"text":"Semgrep Finding: skills.behavioral.skill-persona-hijacking.skill-persona-hijacking"}},{"defaultConfiguration":{"level":"warning"},"fullDescription":{"text":"Skill or document contains hidden instructions targeting AI agents that retrieve it as context. RAG data poisoning embeds adversarial directives inside documents, knowledge bases, or skill files so that an LLM processing them follows attacker-controlled instructions instead of the user's intent. This technique is used in indirect prompt injection attacks where the attack payload is stored in a retrieval corpus. Review the full document context."},"help":{"markdown":"Skill or document contains hidden instructions targeting AI agents that retrieve it as context. RAG data poisoning embeds adversarial directives inside documents, knowledge bases, or skill files so that an LLM processing them follows attacker-controlled instructions instead of the user's intent. This technique is used in indirect prompt injection attacks where the attack payload is stored in a retrieval corpus. Review the full document context.\n\n<b>References:</b>\n - [Semgrep Rule](https://semgrep.dev/r/skills.behavioral.skill-rag-data-poisoning.skill-rag-data-poisoning)\n - [https://cwe.mitre.org/data/definitions/94.html](https://cwe.mitre.org/data/definitions/94.html)\n - [https://owasp.org/Top10/2025/A05_2025-Injection/](https://owasp.org/Top10/2025/A05_2025-Injection/)\n - [https://owasp.org/Top10/A03_2021-Injection](https://owasp.org/Top10/A03_2021-Injection)\n","text":"Skill or document contains hidden instructions targeting AI agents that retrieve it as context. RAG data poisoning embeds adversarial directives inside documents, knowledge bases, or skill files so that an LLM processing them follows attacker-controlled instructions instead of the user's intent. This technique is used in indirect prompt injection attacks where the attack payload is stored in a retrieval corpus. Review the full document context."},"helpUri":"https://semgrep.dev/r/skills.behavioral.skill-rag-data-poisoning.skill-rag-data-poisoning","id":"skills.behavioral.skill-rag-data-poisoning.skill-rag-data-poisoning","name":"skills.behavioral.skill-rag-data-poisoning.skill-rag-data-poisoning","properties":{"precision":"very-high","tags":["CWE-94: Improper Control of Generation of Code ('Code Injection')","MEDIUM CONFIDENCE","OWASP-A03:2021 - Injection","OWASP-A05:2025 - Injection","security"]},"shortDescription":{"text":"Semgrep Finding: skills.behavioral.skill-rag-data-poisoning.skill-rag-data-poisoning"}},{"defaultConfiguration":{"level":"warning"},"fullDescription":{"text":"Skill contains instructions to extract or reveal the agent's system prompt or internal configuration instructions. System prompt extraction is a reconnaissance technique that allows attackers to discover safety constraints, tool definitions, and operational guidelines in order to craft more effective follow-on attacks. Skills embedding these directives may be used to leak confidential operator instructions. Review the full skill context."},"help":{"markdown":"Skill contains instructions to extract or reveal the agent's system prompt or internal configuration instructions. System prompt extraction is a reconnaissance technique that allows attackers to discover safety constraints, tool definitions, and operational guidelines in order to craft more effective follow-on attacks. Skills embedding these directives may be used to leak confidential operator instructions. Review the full skill context.\n\n<b>References:</b>\n - [Semgrep Rule](https://semgrep.dev/r/skills.behavioral.skill-system-prompt-extraction.skill-system-prompt-extraction)\n - [https://cwe.mitre.org/data/definitions/94.html](https://cwe.mitre.org/data/definitions/94.html)\n - [https://owasp.org/Top10/2025/A05_2025-Injection/](https://owasp.org/Top10/2025/A05_2025-Injection/)\n - [https://owasp.org/Top10/A03_2021-Injection](https://owasp.org/Top10/A03_2021-Injection)\n","text":"Skill contains instructions to extract or reveal the agent's system prompt or internal configuration instructions. System prompt extraction is a reconnaissance technique that allows attackers to discover safety constraints, tool definitions, and operational guidelines in order to craft more effective follow-on attacks. Skills embedding these directives may be used to leak confidential operator instructions. Review the full skill context."},"helpUri":"https://semgrep.dev/r/skills.behavioral.skill-system-prompt-extraction.skill-system-prompt-extraction","id":"skills.behavioral.skill-system-prompt-extraction.skill-system-prompt-extraction","name":"skills.behavioral.skill-system-prompt-extraction.skill-system-prompt-extraction","properties":{"precision":"very-high","tags":["CWE-94: Improper Control of Generation of Code ('Code Injection')","MEDIUM CONFIDENCE","OWASP-A03:2021 - Injection","OWASP-A05:2025 - Injection","security"]},"shortDescription":{"text":"Semgrep Finding: skills.behavioral.skill-system-prompt-extraction.skill-system-prompt-extraction"}},{"defaultConfiguration":{"level":"error"},"fullDescription":{"text":"Dynamic code execution detected: eval(), exec(), compile(), or __import__() called with a non-literal argument. In an AI agent skill context this is a high-severity finding because an attacker who controls the argument can execute arbitrary code. Use ast.literal_eval() for safe expression evaluation, or restructure to avoid dynamic execution entirely."},"help":{"markdown":"Dynamic code execution detected: eval(), exec(), compile(), or __import__() called with a non-literal argument. In an AI agent skill context this is a high-severity finding because an attacker who controls the argument can execute arbitrary code. Use ast.literal_eval() for safe expression evaluation, or restructure to avoid dynamic execution entirely.\n\n<b>References:</b>\n - [Semgrep Rule](https://semgrep.dev/r/skills.code-injection.skill-dynamic-eval-exec.skill-dynamic-eval-exec)\n - [https://cwe.mitre.org/data/definitions/94.html](https://cwe.mitre.org/data/definitions/94.html)\n - [https://owasp.org/Top10/2025/A05_2025-Injection/](https://owasp.org/Top10/2025/A05_2025-Injection/)\n - [https://owasp.org/Top10/A03_2021-Injection](https://owasp.org/Top10/A03_2021-Injection)\n - [https://owasp.org/www-community/attacks/Code_Injection](https://owasp.org/www-community/attacks/Code_Injection)\n","text":"Dynamic code execution detected: eval(), exec(), compile(), or __import__() called with a non-literal argument. In an AI agent skill context this is a high-severity finding because an attacker who controls the argument can execute arbitrary code. Use ast.literal_eval() for safe expression evaluation, or restructure to avoid dynamic execution entirely."},"helpUri":"https://semgrep.dev/r/skills.code-injection.skill-dynamic-eval-exec.skill-dynamic-eval-exec","id":"skills.code-injection.skill-dynamic-eval-exec.skill-dynamic-eval-exec","name":"skills.code-injection.skill-dynamic-eval-exec.skill-dynamic-eval-exec","properties":{"precision":"very-high","tags":["CWE-94: Improper Control of Generation of Code ('Code Injection')","HIGH CONFIDENCE","OWASP-A03:2021 - Injection","OWASP-A05:2025 - Injection","security"]},"shortDescription":{"text":"Semgrep Finding: skills.code-injection.skill-dynamic-eval-exec.skill-dynamic-eval-exec"}},{"defaultConfiguration":{"level":"warning"},"fullDescription":{"text":"LDAP injection detected: an LDAP search filter is constructed with a formatted string (f-string, % formatting, str.format(), or + concatenation). Unsanitized values in LDAP filters allow an attacker to bypass authentication or enumerate directory entries. Escape all user-supplied values with ldap3.utils.conv.escape_filter_chars() or python-ldap's ldap.filter.escape_filter_chars() before interpolating into search filters."},"help":{"markdown":"LDAP injection detected: an LDAP search filter is constructed with a formatted string (f-string, % formatting, str.format(), or + concatenation). Unsanitized values in LDAP filters allow an attacker to bypass authentication or enumerate directory entries. Escape all user-supplied values with ldap3.utils.conv.escape_filter_chars() or python-ldap's ldap.filter.escape_filter_chars() before interpolating into search filters.\n\n<b>References:</b>\n - [Semgrep Rule](https://semgrep.dev/r/skills.code-injection.skill-ldap-injection.skill-ldap-injection)\n - [https://cwe.mitre.org/data/definitions/90.html](https://cwe.mitre.org/data/definitions/90.html)\n - [https://owasp.org/Top10/2025/A05_2025-Injection/](https://owasp.org/Top10/2025/A05_2025-Injection/)\n - [https://owasp.org/Top10/A03_2021-Injection](https://owasp.org/Top10/A03_2021-Injection)\n - [https://owasp.org/www-community/attacks/LDAP_Injection](https://owasp.org/www-community/attacks/LDAP_Injection)\n","text":"LDAP injection detected: an LDAP search filter is constructed with a formatted string (f-string, % formatting, str.format(), or + concatenation). Unsanitized values in LDAP filters allow an attacker to bypass authentication or enumerate directory entries. Escape all user-supplied values with ldap3.utils.conv.escape_filter_chars() or python-ldap's ldap.filter.escape_filter_chars() before interpolating into search filters."},"helpUri":"https://semgrep.dev/r/skills.code-injection.skill-ldap-injection.skill-ldap-injection","id":"skills.code-injection.skill-ldap-injection.skill-ldap-injection","name":"skills.code-injection.skill-ldap-injection.skill-ldap-injection","properties":{"precision":"very-high","tags":["CWE-90: Improper Neutralization of Special Elements used in an LDAP Query ('LDAP Injection')","MEDIUM CONFIDENCE","OWASP-A01:2017 - Injection","OWASP-A03:2021 - Injection","OWASP-A05:2025 - Injection","security"]},"shortDescription":{"text":"Semgrep Finding: skills.code-injection.skill-ldap-injection.skill-ldap-injection"}},{"defaultConfiguration":{"level":"error"},"fullDescription":{"text":"Server-side template injection detected: a Jinja2 Template object is constructed with a non-literal string argument. If the template string originates from user input or LLM output, an attacker can use Jinja2 expressions like {{config.__class__.__init__.__globals__['os'].popen('id').read()}} to execute arbitrary code. Use jinja2.Environment with autoescape=True and only render trusted, static template strings. Never pass user-controlled content as the template itself."},"help":{"markdown":"Server-side template injection detected: a Jinja2 Template object is constructed with a non-literal string argument. If the template string originates from user input or LLM output, an attacker can use Jinja2 expressions like {{config.__class__.__init__.__globals__['os'].popen('id').read()}} to execute arbitrary code. Use jinja2.Environment with autoescape=True and only render trusted, static template strings. Never pass user-controlled content as the template itself.\n\n<b>References:</b>\n - [Semgrep Rule](https://semgrep.dev/r/skills.code-injection.skill-server-side-template-injection.skill-server-side-template-injection)\n - [https://cwe.mitre.org/data/definitions/94.html](https://cwe.mitre.org/data/definitions/94.html)\n - [https://owasp.org/Top10/2025/A05_2025-Injection/](https://owasp.org/Top10/2025/A05_2025-Injection/)\n - [https://owasp.org/Top10/A03_2021-Injection](https://owasp.org/Top10/A03_2021-Injection)\n - [https://portswigger.net/web-security/server-side-template-injection](https://portswigger.net/web-security/server-side-template-injection)\n","text":"Server-side template injection detected: a Jinja2 Template object is constructed with a non-literal string argument. If the template string originates from user input or LLM output, an attacker can use Jinja2 expressions like {{config.__class__.__init__.__globals__['os'].popen('id').read()}} to execute arbitrary code. Use jinja2.Environment with autoescape=True and only render trusted, static template strings. Never pass user-controlled content as the template itself."},"helpUri":"https://semgrep.dev/r/skills.code-injection.skill-server-side-template-injection.skill-server-side-template-injection","id":"skills.code-injection.skill-server-side-template-injection.skill-server-side-template-injection","name":"skills.code-injection.skill-server-side-template-injection.skill-server-side-template-injection","properties":{"precision":"very-high","tags":["CWE-94: Improper Control of Generation of Code ('Code Injection')","HIGH CONFIDENCE","OWASP-A03:2021 - Injection","OWASP-A05:2025 - Injection","security"]},"shortDescription":{"text":"Semgrep Finding: skills.code-injection.skill-server-side-template-injection.skill-server-side-template-injection"}},{"defaultConfiguration":{"level":"error"},"fullDescription":{"text":"Shell command constructed with an f-string detected. Interpolating variables directly into a shell command string enables command injection. In AI agent skill packages this is especially dangerous because the interpolated values may originate from untrusted LLM output or user-controlled tool arguments. Use subprocess with a list argument instead of a shell string, or sanitize inputs with shlex.quote() before interpolation."},"help":{"markdown":"Shell command constructed with an f-string detected. Interpolating variables directly into a shell command string enables command injection. In AI agent skill packages this is especially dangerous because the interpolated values may originate from untrusted LLM output or user-controlled tool arguments. Use subprocess with a list argument instead of a shell string, or sanitize inputs with shlex.quote() before interpolation.\n\n<b>References:</b>\n - [Semgrep Rule](https://semgrep.dev/r/skills.code-injection.skill-shell-string-interpolation.skill-shell-string-interpolation)\n - [https://cwe.mitre.org/data/definitions/78.html](https://cwe.mitre.org/data/definitions/78.html)\n - [https://docs.python.org/3/library/subprocess.html#security-considerations](https://docs.python.org/3/library/subprocess.html#security-considerations)\n - [https://owasp.org/Top10/2025/A05_2025-Injection/](https://owasp.org/Top10/2025/A05_2025-Injection/)\n - [https://owasp.org/Top10/A03_2021-Injection](https://owasp.org/Top10/A03_2021-Injection)\n","text":"Shell command constructed with an f-string detected. Interpolating variables directly into a shell command string enables command injection. In AI agent skill packages this is especially dangerous because the interpolated values may originate from untrusted LLM output or user-controlled tool arguments. Use subprocess with a list argument instead of a shell string, or sanitize inputs with shlex.quote() before interpolation."},"helpUri":"https://semgrep.dev/r/skills.code-injection.skill-shell-string-interpolation.skill-shell-string-interpolation","id":"skills.code-injection.skill-shell-string-interpolation.skill-shell-string-interpolation","name":"skills.code-injection.skill-shell-string-interpolation.skill-shell-string-interpolation","properties":{"precision":"very-high","tags":["CWE-78: Improper Neutralization of Special Elements used in an OS Command ('OS Command Injection')","HIGH CONFIDENCE","OWASP-A01:2017 - Injection","OWASP-A03:2021 - Injection","OWASP-A05:2025 - Injection","security"]},"shortDescription":{"text":"Semgrep Finding: skills.code-injection.skill-shell-string-interpolation.skill-shell-string-interpolation"}},{"defaultConfiguration":{"level":"error"},"fullDescription":{"text":"SQL query constructed via string formatting or concatenation detected. Using f-strings, % formatting, str.format(), or + concatenation to build SQL queries allows SQL injection attacks. In AI agent skill packages the query string may be influenced by untrusted LLM outputs or tool arguments. Use parameterized queries with placeholders (? or %s) and pass values as a separate tuple argument to cursor.execute()."},"help":{"markdown":"SQL query constructed via string formatting or concatenation detected. Using f-strings, % formatting, str.format(), or + concatenation to build SQL queries allows SQL injection attacks. In AI agent skill packages the query string may be influenced by untrusted LLM outputs or tool arguments. Use parameterized queries with placeholders (? or %s) and pass values as a separate tuple argument to cursor.execute().\n\n<b>References:</b>\n - [Semgrep Rule](https://semgrep.dev/r/skills.code-injection.skill-sql-string-formatting.skill-sql-string-formatting)\n - [https://cwe.mitre.org/data/definitions/89.html](https://cwe.mitre.org/data/definitions/89.html)\n - [https://owasp.org/Top10/2025/A05_2025-Injection/](https://owasp.org/Top10/2025/A05_2025-Injection/)\n - [https://owasp.org/Top10/A03_2021-Injection](https://owasp.org/Top10/A03_2021-Injection)\n - [https://owasp.org/www-community/attacks/SQL_Injection](https://owasp.org/www-community/attacks/SQL_Injection)\n","text":"SQL query constructed via string formatting or concatenation detected. Using f-strings, % formatting, str.format(), or + concatenation to build SQL queries allows SQL injection attacks. In AI agent skill packages the query string may be influenced by untrusted LLM outputs or tool arguments. Use parameterized queries with placeholders (? or %s) and pass values as a separate tuple argument to cursor.execute()."},"helpUri":"https://semgrep.dev/r/skills.code-injection.skill-sql-string-formatting.skill-sql-string-formatting","id":"skills.code-injection.skill-sql-string-formatting.skill-sql-string-formatting","name":"skills.code-injection.skill-sql-string-formatting.skill-sql-string-formatting","properties":{"precision":"very-high","tags":["CWE-89: Improper Neutralization of Special Elements used in an SQL Command ('SQL Injection')","HIGH CONFIDENCE","OWASP-A01:2017 - Injection","OWASP-A03:2021 - Injection","OWASP-A05:2025 - Injection","security"]},"shortDescription":{"text":"Semgrep Finding: skills.code-injection.skill-sql-string-formatting.skill-sql-string-formatting"}},{"defaultConfiguration":{"level":"error"},"fullDescription":{"text":"Unsafe deserialization detected. pickle, marshal, and jsonpickle can execute arbitrary code during deserialization of attacker-controlled data. yaml.load() without a safe Loader is also exploitable via !!python/object tags. In an AI agent skill context, deserialized data may originate from untrusted LLM tool arguments or network responses. Use json.loads() for structured data, or yaml.safe_load() / yaml.load(stream, Loader=yaml.SafeLoader) for YAML."},"help":{"markdown":"Unsafe deserialization detected. pickle, marshal, and jsonpickle can execute arbitrary code during deserialization of attacker-controlled data. yaml.load() without a safe Loader is also exploitable via !!python/object tags. In an AI agent skill context, deserialized data may originate from untrusted LLM tool arguments or network responses. Use json.loads() for structured data, or yaml.safe_load() / yaml.load(stream, Loader=yaml.SafeLoader) for YAML.\n\n<b>References:</b>\n - [Semgrep Rule](https://semgrep.dev/r/skills.code-injection.skill-unsafe-deserialization.skill-unsafe-deserialization)\n - [https://cwe.mitre.org/data/definitions/502.html](https://cwe.mitre.org/data/definitions/502.html)\n - [https://docs.python.org/3/library/pickle.html#restricting-globals](https://docs.python.org/3/library/pickle.html#restricting-globals)\n - [https://owasp.org/Top10/2025/A08_2025-Software_or_Data_Integrity_Failures/](https://owasp.org/Top10/2025/A08_2025-Software_or_Data_Integrity_Failures/)\n - [https://owasp.org/Top10/A08_2021-Software_and_Data_Integrity_Failures](https://owasp.org/Top10/A08_2021-Software_and_Data_Integrity_Failures)\n","text":"Unsafe deserialization detected. pickle, marshal, and jsonpickle can execute arbitrary code during deserialization of attacker-controlled data. yaml.load() without a safe Loader is also exploitable via !!python/object tags. In an AI agent skill context, deserialized data may originate from untrusted LLM tool arguments or network responses. Use json.loads() for structured data, or yaml.safe_load() / yaml.load(stream, Loader=yaml.SafeLoader) for YAML."},"helpUri":"https://semgrep.dev/r/skills.code-injection.skill-unsafe-deserialization.skill-unsafe-deserialization","id":"skills.code-injection.skill-unsafe-deserialization.skill-unsafe-deserialization","name":"skills.code-injection.skill-unsafe-deserialization.skill-unsafe-deserialization","properties":{"precision":"very-high","tags":["CWE-502: Deserialization of Untrusted Data","HIGH CONFIDENCE","OWASP-A08:2017 - Insecure Deserialization","OWASP-A08:2021 - Software and Data Integrity Failures","OWASP-A08:2025 - Software or Data Integrity Failures","security"]},"shortDescription":{"text":"Semgrep Finding: skills.code-injection.skill-unsafe-deserialization.skill-unsafe-deserialization"}},{"defaultConfiguration":{"level":"warning"},"fullDescription":{"text":"Unsafe XML parsing detected. xml.etree.ElementTree.fromstring(), minidom.parse(), and xml.dom.minidom.parseString() are vulnerable to XXE (XML External Entity) attacks when parsing attacker-controlled XML. In an AI agent skill context the XML may originate from untrusted LLM tool responses or user uploads. Use defusedxml (defusedxml.ElementTree.fromstring, defusedxml.minidom.parseString) which disables external entity resolution by default."},"help":{"markdown":"Unsafe XML parsing detected. xml.etree.ElementTree.fromstring(), minidom.parse(), and xml.dom.minidom.parseString() are vulnerable to XXE (XML External Entity) attacks when parsing attacker-controlled XML. In an AI agent skill context the XML may originate from untrusted LLM tool responses or user uploads. Use defusedxml (defusedxml.ElementTree.fromstring, defusedxml.minidom.parseString) which disables external entity resolution by default.\n\n<b>References:</b>\n - [Semgrep Rule](https://semgrep.dev/r/skills.code-injection.skill-xxe-unsafe-xml.skill-xxe-unsafe-xml)\n - [https://cwe.mitre.org/data/definitions/611.html](https://cwe.mitre.org/data/definitions/611.html)\n - [https://owasp.org/Top10/2025/A02_2025-Security_Misconfiguration/](https://owasp.org/Top10/2025/A02_2025-Security_Misconfiguration/)\n - [https://owasp.org/Top10/A05_2021-Security_Misconfiguration](https://owasp.org/Top10/A05_2021-Security_Misconfiguration)\n - [https://pypi.org/project/defusedxml/](https://pypi.org/project/defusedxml/)\n","text":"Unsafe XML parsing detected. xml.etree.ElementTree.fromstring(), minidom.parse(), and xml.dom.minidom.parseString() are vulnerable to XXE (XML External Entity) attacks when parsing attacker-controlled XML. In an AI agent skill context the XML may originate from untrusted LLM tool responses or user uploads. Use defusedxml (defusedxml.ElementTree.fromstring, defusedxml.minidom.parseString) which disables external entity resolution by default."},"helpUri":"https://semgrep.dev/r/skills.code-injection.skill-xxe-unsafe-xml.skill-xxe-unsafe-xml","id":"skills.code-injection.skill-xxe-unsafe-xml.skill-xxe-unsafe-xml","name":"skills.code-injection.skill-xxe-unsafe-xml.skill-xxe-unsafe-xml","properties":{"precision":"very-high","tags":["CWE-611: Improper Restriction of XML External Entity Reference","HIGH CONFIDENCE","OWASP-A02:2025 - Security Misconfiguration","OWASP-A04:2017 - XML External Entities (XXE)","OWASP-A05:2021 - Security Misconfiguration","security"]},"shortDescription":{"text":"Semgrep Finding: skills.code-injection.skill-xxe-unsafe-xml.skill-xxe-unsafe-xml"}},{"defaultConfiguration":{"level":"error"},"fullDescription":{"text":"Base64 decode piped to shell execution. This pattern is used to obfuscate malicious commands by encoding them in base64, then decoding and executing at runtime. Common in evasion techniques."},"help":{"markdown":"Base64 decode piped to shell execution. This pattern is used to obfuscate malicious commands by encoding them in base64, then decoding and executing at runtime. Common in evasion techniques.\n\n<b>References:</b>\n - [Semgrep Rule](https://semgrep.dev/r/skills.command-execution.skill-base64-decode-pipe-shell.skill-base64-decode-pipe-shell)\n - [https://owasp.org/Top10/2025/A05_2025-Injection/](https://owasp.org/Top10/2025/A05_2025-Injection/)\n - [https://owasp.org/Top10/A03_2021-Injection](https://owasp.org/Top10/A03_2021-Injection)\n","text":"Base64 decode piped to shell execution. This pattern is used to obfuscate malicious commands by encoding them in base64, then decoding and executing at runtime. Common in evasion techniques."},"helpUri":"https://semgrep.dev/r/skills.command-execution.skill-base64-decode-pipe-shell.skill-base64-decode-pipe-shell","id":"skills.command-execution.skill-base64-decode-pipe-shell.skill-base64-decode-pipe-shell","name":"skills.command-execution.skill-base64-decode-pipe-shell.skill-base64-decode-pipe-shell","properties":{"precision":"very-high","tags":["CWE-78: Improper Neutralization of Special Elements used in an OS Command ('OS Command Injection')","HIGH CONFIDENCE","OWASP-A01:2017 - Injection","OWASP-A03:2021 - Injection","OWASP-A05:2025 - Injection","security"]},"shortDescription":{"text":"Semgrep Finding: skills.command-execution.skill-base64-decode-pipe-shell.skill-base64-decode-pipe-shell"}},{"defaultConfiguration":{"level":"error"},"fullDescription":{"text":"Download followed by chmod +x detected. This pattern downloads a file and immediately makes it executable, indicating preparation to run downloaded code."},"help":{"markdown":"Download followed by chmod +x detected. This pattern downloads a file and immediately makes it executable, indicating preparation to run downloaded code.\n\n<b>References:</b>\n - [Semgrep Rule](https://semgrep.dev/r/skills.command-execution.skill-chmod-wget-exec.skill-chmod-wget-exec)\n - [https://cwe.mitre.org/data/definitions/494.html](https://cwe.mitre.org/data/definitions/494.html)\n - [https://owasp.org/Top10/2025/A08_2025-Software_or_Data_Integrity_Failures/](https://owasp.org/Top10/2025/A08_2025-Software_or_Data_Integrity_Failures/)\n - [https://owasp.org/Top10/A08_2021-Software_and_Data_Integrity_Failures](https://owasp.org/Top10/A08_2021-Software_and_Data_Integrity_Failures)\n","text":"Download followed by chmod +x detected. This pattern downloads a file and immediately makes it executable, indicating preparation to run downloaded code."},"helpUri":"https://semgrep.dev/r/skills.command-execution.skill-chmod-wget-exec.skill-chmod-wget-exec","id":"skills.command-execution.skill-chmod-wget-exec.skill-chmod-wget-exec","name":"skills.command-execution.skill-chmod-wget-exec.skill-chmod-wget-exec","properties":{"precision":"very-high","tags":["CWE-494: Download of Code Without Integrity Check","HIGH CONFIDENCE","OWASP-A08:2021 - Software and Data Integrity Failures","OWASP-A08:2025 - Software or Data Integrity Failures","security"]},"shortDescription":{"text":"Semgrep Finding: skills.command-execution.skill-chmod-wget-exec.skill-chmod-wget-exec"}},{"defaultConfiguration":{"level":"warning"},"fullDescription":{"text":"Skill reads clipboard contents and pipes or sends the data over the network. This matches MITRE ATT&CK T1115 (Clipboard Data) — a technique used by Atomic macOS Stealer (AMOS) and other infostealers delivered via malicious agent skills. Legitimate skills do not need to exfiltrate clipboard content to remote servers."},"help":{"markdown":"Skill reads clipboard contents and pipes or sends the data over the network. This matches MITRE ATT&CK T1115 (Clipboard Data) — a technique used by Atomic macOS Stealer (AMOS) and other infostealers delivered via malicious agent skills. Legitimate skills do not need to exfiltrate clipboard content to remote servers.\n\n<b>References:</b>\n - [Semgrep Rule](https://semgrep.dev/r/skills.command-execution.skill-clipboard-theft.skill-clipboard-theft)\n - [https://attack.mitre.org/techniques/T1115/](https://attack.mitre.org/techniques/T1115/)\n - [https://cwe.mitre.org/data/definitions/200.html](https://cwe.mitre.org/data/definitions/200.html)\n - [https://owasp.org/Top10/2025/A01_2025-Broken_Access_Control/](https://owasp.org/Top10/2025/A01_2025-Broken_Access_Control/)\n - [https://owasp.org/Top10/A01_2021-Broken_Access_Control](https://owasp.org/Top10/A01_2021-Broken_Access_Control)\n","text":"Skill reads clipboard contents and pipes or sends the data over the network. This matches MITRE ATT&CK T1115 (Clipboard Data) — a technique used by Atomic macOS Stealer (AMOS) and other infostealers delivered via malicious agent skills. Legitimate skills do not need to exfiltrate clipboard content to remote servers."},"helpUri":"https://semgrep.dev/r/skills.command-execution.skill-clipboard-theft.skill-clipboard-theft","id":"skills.command-execution.skill-clipboard-theft.skill-clipboard-theft","name":"skills.command-execution.skill-clipboard-theft.skill-clipboard-theft","properties":{"precision":"very-high","tags":["CWE-200: Exposure of Sensitive Information to an Unauthorized Actor","HIGH CONFIDENCE","OWASP-A01:2021 - Broken Access Control","OWASP-A01:2025 - Broken Access Control","security"]},"shortDescription":{"text":"Semgrep Finding: skills.command-execution.skill-clipboard-theft.skill-clipboard-theft"}},{"defaultConfiguration":{"level":"warning"},"fullDescription":{"text":"Suspicious curl-to-shell pattern with unusual infrastructure indicator (hardcoded\nIP or large base64 payload). This combination warrants investigation — it has been\nused in malware distribution campaigns but may also appear in legitimate scripts\nthat bundle their own installer or payload. Review the source URL and payload.\n\nNote: Approved ecosystem tool installers (Rust, Python UV, Bun, etc.) are allowlisted.\n"},"help":{"markdown":"Suspicious curl-to-shell pattern with unusual infrastructure indicator (hardcoded\nIP or large base64 payload). This combination warrants investigation — it has been\nused in malware distribution campaigns but may also appear in legitimate scripts\nthat bundle their own installer or payload. Review the source URL and payload.\n\nNote: Approved ecosystem tool installers (Rust, Python UV, Bun, etc.) are allowlisted.\n\n\n<b>References:</b>\n - [Semgrep Rule](https://semgrep.dev/r/skills.command-execution.skill-curl-pipe-bash.skill-curl-pipe-bash)\n - [https://owasp.org/Top10/2025/A08_2025-Software_or_Data_Integrity_Failures/](https://owasp.org/Top10/2025/A08_2025-Software_or_Data_Integrity_Failures/)\n - [https://owasp.org/Top10/A08_2021-Software_and_Data_Integrity_Failures](https://owasp.org/Top10/A08_2021-Software_and_Data_Integrity_Failures)\n - [https://www.idontplaydarts.com/2016/04/detecting-curl-pipe-bash-server-side/](https://www.idontplaydarts.com/2016/04/detecting-curl-pipe-bash-server-side/)\n","text":"Suspicious curl-to-shell pattern with unusual infrastructure indicator (hardcoded\nIP or large base64 payload). This combination warrants investigation — it has been\nused in malware distribution campaigns but may also appear in legitimate scripts\nthat bundle their own installer or payload. Review the source URL and payload.\n\nNote: Approved ecosystem tool installers (Rust, Python UV, Bun, etc.) are allowlisted.\n"},"helpUri":"https://semgrep.dev/r/skills.command-execution.skill-curl-pipe-bash.skill-curl-pipe-bash","id":"skills.command-execution.skill-curl-pipe-bash.skill-curl-pipe-bash","name":"skills.command-execution.skill-curl-pipe-bash.skill-curl-pipe-bash","properties":{"precision":"very-high","tags":["CWE-494: Download of Code Without Integrity Check","MEDIUM CONFIDENCE","OWASP-A08:2021 - Software and Data Integrity Failures","OWASP-A08:2025 - Software or Data Integrity Failures","security"]},"shortDescription":{"text":"Semgrep Finding: skills.command-execution.skill-curl-pipe-bash.skill-curl-pipe-bash"}},{"defaultConfiguration":{"level":"warning"},"fullDescription":{"text":"Suspicious silent download-and-execute pattern with unusual infrastructure\nindicator (hardcoded IP or large base64 payload). This combination warrants\ninvestigation — it has been used in malware distribution campaigns but may\nalso appear in legitimate bundled installers. Review the source URL and payload.\n\nNote: Approved ecosystem tool installers are allowlisted.\n"},"help":{"markdown":"Suspicious silent download-and-execute pattern with unusual infrastructure\nindicator (hardcoded IP or large base64 payload). This combination warrants\ninvestigation — it has been used in malware distribution campaigns but may\nalso appear in legitimate bundled installers. Review the source URL and payload.\n\nNote: Approved ecosystem tool installers are allowlisted.\n\n\n<b>References:</b>\n - [Semgrep Rule](https://semgrep.dev/r/skills.command-execution.skill-curl-silent-pipe.skill-curl-silent-pipe)\n - [https://owasp.org/Top10/2025/A08_2025-Software_or_Data_Integrity_Failures/](https://owasp.org/Top10/2025/A08_2025-Software_or_Data_Integrity_Failures/)\n - [https://owasp.org/Top10/A08_2021-Software_and_Data_Integrity_Failures](https://owasp.org/Top10/A08_2021-Software_and_Data_Integrity_Failures)\n","text":"Suspicious silent download-and-execute pattern with unusual infrastructure\nindicator (hardcoded IP or large base64 payload). This combination warrants\ninvestigation — it has been used in malware distribution campaigns but may\nalso appear in legitimate bundled installers. Review the source URL and payload.\n\nNote: Approved ecosystem tool installers are allowlisted.\n"},"helpUri":"https://semgrep.dev/r/skills.command-execution.skill-curl-silent-pipe.skill-curl-silent-pipe","id":"skills.command-execution.skill-curl-silent-pipe.skill-curl-silent-pipe","name":"skills.command-execution.skill-curl-silent-pipe.skill-curl-silent-pipe","properties":{"precision":"very-high","tags":["CWE-494: Download of Code Without Integrity Check","MEDIUM CONFIDENCE","OWASP-A08:2021 - Software and Data Integrity Failures","OWASP-A08:2025 - Software or Data Integrity Failures","security"]},"shortDescription":{"text":"Semgrep Finding: skills.command-execution.skill-curl-silent-pipe.skill-curl-silent-pipe"}},{"defaultConfiguration":{"level":"error"},"fullDescription":{"text":"Binary executable download detected. Downloading compiled binaries (.exe, .elf, .dylib, .dll) is suspicious and could indicate malware download or installation of unauthorized software."},"help":{"markdown":"Binary executable download detected. Downloading compiled binaries (.exe, .elf, .dylib, .dll) is suspicious and could indicate malware download or installation of unauthorized software.\n\n<b>References:</b>\n - [Semgrep Rule](https://semgrep.dev/r/skills.command-execution.skill-download-executable.skill-download-executable)\n - [https://cwe.mitre.org/data/definitions/494.html](https://cwe.mitre.org/data/definitions/494.html)\n - [https://owasp.org/Top10/2025/A08_2025-Software_or_Data_Integrity_Failures/](https://owasp.org/Top10/2025/A08_2025-Software_or_Data_Integrity_Failures/)\n - [https://owasp.org/Top10/A08_2021-Software_and_Data_Integrity_Failures](https://owasp.org/Top10/A08_2021-Software_and_Data_Integrity_Failures)\n","text":"Binary executable download detected. Downloading compiled binaries (.exe, .elf, .dylib, .dll) is suspicious and could indicate malware download or installation of unauthorized software."},"helpUri":"https://semgrep.dev/r/skills.command-execution.skill-download-executable.skill-download-executable","id":"skills.command-execution.skill-download-executable.skill-download-executable","name":"skills.command-execution.skill-download-executable.skill-download-executable","properties":{"precision":"very-high","tags":["CWE-494: Download of Code Without Integrity Check","MEDIUM CONFIDENCE","OWASP-A08:2021 - Software and Data Integrity Failures","OWASP-A08:2025 - Software or Data Integrity Failures","security"]},"shortDescription":{"text":"Semgrep Finding: skills.command-execution.skill-download-executable.skill-download-executable"}},{"defaultConfiguration":{"level":"warning"},"fullDescription":{"text":"Suspicious download-and-execute pattern with unusual infrastructure indicator (hardcoded IP, large base64 payload, or C2 framework name). This combination warrants investigation as a possible malware staging or covert execution technique. Verify the download source and whether execution is user-authorized."},"help":{"markdown":"Suspicious download-and-execute pattern with unusual infrastructure indicator (hardcoded IP, large base64 payload, or C2 framework name). This combination warrants investigation as a possible malware staging or covert execution technique. Verify the download source and whether execution is user-authorized.\n\n<b>References:</b>\n - [Semgrep Rule](https://semgrep.dev/r/skills.command-execution.skill-download-run-pattern.skill-download-run-pattern)\n - [https://cwe.mitre.org/data/definitions/494.html](https://cwe.mitre.org/data/definitions/494.html)\n - [https://owasp.org/Top10/2025/A08_2025-Software_or_Data_Integrity_Failures/](https://owasp.org/Top10/2025/A08_2025-Software_or_Data_Integrity_Failures/)\n - [https://owasp.org/Top10/A08_2021-Software_and_Data_Integrity_Failures](https://owasp.org/Top10/A08_2021-Software_and_Data_Integrity_Failures)\n","text":"Suspicious download-and-execute pattern with unusual infrastructure indicator (hardcoded IP, large base64 payload, or C2 framework name). This combination warrants investigation as a possible malware staging or covert execution technique. Verify the download source and whether execution is user-authorized."},"helpUri":"https://semgrep.dev/r/skills.command-execution.skill-download-run-pattern.skill-download-run-pattern","id":"skills.command-execution.skill-download-run-pattern.skill-download-run-pattern","name":"skills.command-execution.skill-download-run-pattern.skill-download-run-pattern","properties":{"precision":"very-high","tags":["CWE-494: Download of Code Without Integrity Check","MEDIUM CONFIDENCE","OWASP-A08:2021 - Software and Data Integrity Failures","OWASP-A08:2025 - Software or Data Integrity Failures","security"]},"shortDescription":{"text":"Semgrep Finding: skills.command-execution.skill-download-run-pattern.skill-download-run-pattern"}},{"defaultConfiguration":{"level":"error"},"fullDescription":{"text":"Download to temporary directory with executable extension or hidden staging path. Downloading scripts or binaries to /tmp, /var/tmp, or hidden dot-directories under /tmp is commonly used by malware to avoid detection."},"help":{"markdown":"Download to temporary directory with executable extension or hidden staging path. Downloading scripts or binaries to /tmp, /var/tmp, or hidden dot-directories under /tmp is commonly used by malware to avoid detection.\n\n<b>References:</b>\n - [Semgrep Rule](https://semgrep.dev/r/skills.command-execution.skill-download-tmp-exec.skill-download-tmp-exec)\n - [https://cwe.mitre.org/data/definitions/494.html](https://cwe.mitre.org/data/definitions/494.html)\n - [https://owasp.org/Top10/2025/A08_2025-Software_or_Data_Integrity_Failures/](https://owasp.org/Top10/2025/A08_2025-Software_or_Data_Integrity_Failures/)\n - [https://owasp.org/Top10/A08_2021-Software_and_Data_Integrity_Failures](https://owasp.org/Top10/A08_2021-Software_and_Data_Integrity_Failures)\n","text":"Download to temporary directory with executable extension or hidden staging path. Downloading scripts or binaries to /tmp, /var/tmp, or hidden dot-directories under /tmp is commonly used by malware to avoid detection."},"helpUri":"https://semgrep.dev/r/skills.command-execution.skill-download-tmp-exec.skill-download-tmp-exec","id":"skills.command-execution.skill-download-tmp-exec.skill-download-tmp-exec","name":"skills.command-execution.skill-download-tmp-exec.skill-download-tmp-exec","properties":{"precision":"very-high","tags":["CWE-494: Download of Code Without Integrity Check","MEDIUM CONFIDENCE","OWASP-A08:2021 - Software and Data Integrity Failures","OWASP-A08:2025 - Software or Data Integrity Failures","security"]},"shortDescription":{"text":"Semgrep Finding: skills.command-execution.skill-download-tmp-exec.skill-download-tmp-exec"}},{"defaultConfiguration":{"level":"error"},"fullDescription":{"text":"Hardcoded base64 blob decoded and executed. Pattern shows a base64-encoded payload being decoded and piped to shell. This is obfuscated code execution."},"help":{"markdown":"Hardcoded base64 blob decoded and executed. Pattern shows a base64-encoded payload being decoded and piped to shell. This is obfuscated code execution.\n\n<b>References:</b>\n - [Semgrep Rule](https://semgrep.dev/r/skills.command-execution.skill-echo-base64-pipe-bash.skill-echo-base64-pipe-bash)\n - [https://owasp.org/Top10/2025/A05_2025-Injection/](https://owasp.org/Top10/2025/A05_2025-Injection/)\n - [https://owasp.org/Top10/A03_2021-Injection](https://owasp.org/Top10/A03_2021-Injection)\n","text":"Hardcoded base64 blob decoded and executed. Pattern shows a base64-encoded payload being decoded and piped to shell. This is obfuscated code execution."},"helpUri":"https://semgrep.dev/r/skills.command-execution.skill-echo-base64-pipe-bash.skill-echo-base64-pipe-bash","id":"skills.command-execution.skill-echo-base64-pipe-bash.skill-echo-base64-pipe-bash","name":"skills.command-execution.skill-echo-base64-pipe-bash.skill-echo-base64-pipe-bash","properties":{"precision":"very-high","tags":["CWE-78: Improper Neutralization of Special Elements used in an OS Command ('OS Command Injection')","HIGH CONFIDENCE","OWASP-A01:2017 - Injection","OWASP-A03:2021 - Injection","OWASP-A05:2025 - Injection","security"]},"shortDescription":{"text":"Semgrep Finding: skills.command-execution.skill-echo-base64-pipe-bash.skill-echo-base64-pipe-bash"}},{"defaultConfiguration":{"level":"error"},"fullDescription":{"text":"Eval with base64 decode detected. Using eval on decoded base64 data is a common obfuscation technique to hide malicious commands from static analysis."},"help":{"markdown":"Eval with base64 decode detected. Using eval on decoded base64 data is a common obfuscation technique to hide malicious commands from static analysis.\n\n<b>References:</b>\n - [Semgrep Rule](https://semgrep.dev/r/skills.command-execution.skill-eval-base64.skill-eval-base64)\n - [https://owasp.org/Top10/2025/A05_2025-Injection/](https://owasp.org/Top10/2025/A05_2025-Injection/)\n - [https://owasp.org/Top10/A03_2021-Injection](https://owasp.org/Top10/A03_2021-Injection)\n","text":"Eval with base64 decode detected. Using eval on decoded base64 data is a common obfuscation technique to hide malicious commands from static analysis."},"helpUri":"https://semgrep.dev/r/skills.command-execution.skill-eval-base64.skill-eval-base64","id":"skills.command-execution.skill-eval-base64.skill-eval-base64","name":"skills.command-execution.skill-eval-base64.skill-eval-base64","properties":{"precision":"very-high","tags":["CWE-95: Improper Neutralization of Directives in Dynamically Evaluated Code ('Eval Injection')","HIGH CONFIDENCE","OWASP-A01:2017 - Injection","OWASP-A03:2021 - Injection","OWASP-A05:2025 - Injection","security"]},"shortDescription":{"text":"Semgrep Finding: skills.command-execution.skill-eval-base64.skill-eval-base64"}},{"defaultConfiguration":{"level":"error"},"fullDescription":{"text":"Skill removes the macOS quarantine attribute from a downloaded file using `xattr -d com.apple.quarantine`. This bypasses Gatekeeper, which prevents execution of unsigned or unnotarized binaries from the internet. This technique was documented by 1Password and Trend Micro in the ClawHavoc campaign, where it was used to run the Atomic macOS Stealer (AMOS) without triggering macOS security warnings."},"help":{"markdown":"Skill removes the macOS quarantine attribute from a downloaded file using `xattr -d com.apple.quarantine`. This bypasses Gatekeeper, which prevents execution of unsigned or unnotarized binaries from the internet. This technique was documented by 1Password and Trend Micro in the ClawHavoc campaign, where it was used to run the Atomic macOS Stealer (AMOS) without triggering macOS security warnings.\n\n<b>References:</b>\n - [Semgrep Rule](https://semgrep.dev/r/skills.command-execution.skill-gatekeeper-bypass.skill-gatekeeper-bypass)\n - [https://1password.com/blog/from-magic-to-malware-how-openclaws-agent-skills-become-an-attack-surface](https://1password.com/blog/from-magic-to-malware-how-openclaws-agent-skills-become-an-attack-surface)\n - [https://cwe.mitre.org/data/definitions/494.html](https://cwe.mitre.org/data/definitions/494.html)\n - [https://owasp.org/Top10/2025/A08_2025-Software_or_Data_Integrity_Failures/](https://owasp.org/Top10/2025/A08_2025-Software_or_Data_Integrity_Failures/)\n - [https://owasp.org/Top10/A08_2021-Software_and_Data_Integrity_Failures](https://owasp.org/Top10/A08_2021-Software_and_Data_Integrity_Failures)\n - [https://www.trendmicro.com/en_us/research/26/b/openclaw-skills-used-to-distribute-atomic-macos-stealer.html](https://www.trendmicro.com/en_us/research/26/b/openclaw-skills-used-to-distribute-atomic-macos-stealer.html)\n","text":"Skill removes the macOS quarantine attribute from a downloaded file using `xattr -d com.apple.quarantine`. This bypasses Gatekeeper, which prevents execution of unsigned or unnotarized binaries from the internet. This technique was documented by 1Password and Trend Micro in the ClawHavoc campaign, where it was used to run the Atomic macOS Stealer (AMOS) without triggering macOS security warnings."},"helpUri":"https://semgrep.dev/r/skills.command-execution.skill-gatekeeper-bypass.skill-gatekeeper-bypass","id":"skills.command-execution.skill-gatekeeper-bypass.skill-gatekeeper-bypass","name":"skills.command-execution.skill-gatekeeper-bypass.skill-gatekeeper-bypass","properties":{"precision":"very-high","tags":["CWE-494: Download of Code Without Integrity Check","HIGH CONFIDENCE","OWASP-A08:2021 - Software and Data Integrity Failures","OWASP-A08:2025 - Software or Data Integrity Failures","security"]},"shortDescription":{"text":"Semgrep Finding: skills.command-execution.skill-gatekeeper-bypass.skill-gatekeeper-bypass"}},{"defaultConfiguration":{"level":"warning"},"fullDescription":{"text":"Skill downloads executable from suspicious GitHub release. Direct downloads of executables from GitHub releases can indicate potential supply chain attacks."},"help":{"markdown":"Skill downloads executable from suspicious GitHub release. Direct downloads of executables from GitHub releases can indicate potential supply chain attacks.\n\n<b>References:</b>\n - [Semgrep Rule](https://semgrep.dev/r/skills.command-execution.skill-github-release-malware.skill-github-release-malware)\n - [https://cwe.mitre.org/data/definitions/494.html](https://cwe.mitre.org/data/definitions/494.html)\n - [https://owasp.org/Top10/2025/A08_2025-Software_or_Data_Integrity_Failures/](https://owasp.org/Top10/2025/A08_2025-Software_or_Data_Integrity_Failures/)\n - [https://owasp.org/Top10/A08_2021-Software_and_Data_Integrity_Failures](https://owasp.org/Top10/A08_2021-Software_and_Data_Integrity_Failures)\n","text":"Skill downloads executable from suspicious GitHub release. Direct downloads of executables from GitHub releases can indicate potential supply chain attacks."},"helpUri":"https://semgrep.dev/r/skills.command-execution.skill-github-release-malware.skill-github-release-malware","id":"skills.command-execution.skill-github-release-malware.skill-github-release-malware","name":"skills.command-execution.skill-github-release-malware.skill-github-release-malware","properties":{"precision":"very-high","tags":["CWE-494: Download of Code Without Integrity Check","MEDIUM CONFIDENCE","OWASP-A08:2021 - Software and Data Integrity Failures","OWASP-A08:2025 - Software or Data Integrity Failures","security"]},"shortDescription":{"text":"Semgrep Finding: skills.command-execution.skill-github-release-malware.skill-github-release-malware"}},{"defaultConfiguration":{"level":"error"},"fullDescription":{"text":"Skill uses glot.io for malware distribution (ClickFix attack). This skill directs users to execute scripts from glot.io, a common malware distribution technique."},"help":{"markdown":"Skill uses glot.io for malware distribution (ClickFix attack). This skill directs users to execute scripts from glot.io, a common malware distribution technique.\n\n<b>References:</b>\n - [Semgrep Rule](https://semgrep.dev/r/skills.command-execution.skill-glot-io-malware-distribution.skill-glot-io-malware-distribution)\n - [https://cwe.mitre.org/data/definitions/494.html](https://cwe.mitre.org/data/definitions/494.html)\n - [https://owasp.org/Top10/2025/A08_2025-Software_or_Data_Integrity_Failures/](https://owasp.org/Top10/2025/A08_2025-Software_or_Data_Integrity_Failures/)\n - [https://owasp.org/Top10/A08_2021-Software_and_Data_Integrity_Failures](https://owasp.org/Top10/A08_2021-Software_and_Data_Integrity_Failures)\n - [https://www.koi.ai/blog/clawhavoc-341-malicious-clawedbot-skills-found-by-the-bot-they-were-targeting](https://www