ev-tcp"}},{"defaultConfiguration":{"level":"error"},"fullDescription":{"text":"Detects execution of network tools commonly used for exfiltration or reverse shells"},"help":{"markdown":"Detects execution of network tools commonly used for exfiltration or reverse shells\n\n<b>References:</b>\n - [Semgrep Rule](https://semgrep.dev/r/skills.command-execution.skill-go-exec-network-tools.skill-go-exec-network-tools)\n - [https://owasp.org/Top10/2025/A05_2025-Injection/](https://owasp.org/Top10/2025/A05_2025-Injection/)\n - [https://owasp.org/Top10/A03_2021-Injection](https://owasp.org/Top10/A03_2021-Injection)\n - [https://pkg.go.dev/os/exec](https://pkg.go.dev/os/exec)\n - [https://pkg.go.dev/syscall#Exec](https://pkg.go.dev/syscall#Exec)\n - [https://semgrep.dev/docs/cheat-sheets/go-command-injection/](https://semgrep.dev/docs/cheat-sheets/go-command-injection/)\n","text":"Detects execution of network tools commonly used for exfiltration or reverse shells"},"helpUri":"https://semgrep.dev/r/skills.command-execution.skill-go-exec-network-tools.skill-go-exec-network-tools","id":"skills.command-execution.skill-go-exec-network-tools.skill-go-exec-network-tools","name":"skills.command-execution.skill-go-exec-network-tools.skill-go-exec-network-tools","properties":{"precision":"very-high","tags":["CWE-78: Improper Neutralization of Special Elements used in an OS Command ('OS Command Injection')","HIGH CONFIDENCE","OWASP-A01:2017 - Injection","OWASP-A03:2021 - Injection","OWASP-A05:2025 - Injection","security"]},"shortDescription":{"text":"Semgrep Finding: skills.command-execution.skill-go-exec-network-tools.skill-go-exec-network-tools"}},{"defaultConfiguration":{"level":"warning"},"fullDescription":{"text":"Skill instructs the agent to install a package directly from a URL or VCS repository (pip install https://, pip install git+, npm install https://, etc.). Installing packages from arbitrary URLs bypasses registry integrity checks, signature verification, and audit trails. Attackers use this technique to deliver malware that does not appear in any public registry. Verify the source before allowing URL-based package installation."},"help":{"markdown":"Skill instructs the agent to install a package directly from a URL or VCS repository (pip install https://, pip install git+, npm install https://, etc.). Installing packages from arbitrary URLs bypasses registry integrity checks, signature verification, and audit trails. Attackers use this technique to deliver malware that does not appear in any public registry. Verify the source before allowing URL-based package installation.\n\n<b>References:</b>\n - [Semgrep Rule](https://semgrep.dev/r/skills.command-execution.skill-install-from-vcs-url.skill-install-from-vcs-url)\n - [https://cwe.mitre.org/data/definitions/494.html](https://cwe.mitre.org/data/definitions/494.html)\n - [https://owasp.org/Top10/2025/A08_2025-Software_or_Data_Integrity_Failures/](https://owasp.org/Top10/2025/A08_2025-Software_or_Data_Integrity_Failures/)\n - [https://owasp.org/Top10/A08_2021-Software_and_Data_Integrity_Failures](https://owasp.org/Top10/A08_2021-Software_and_Data_Integrity_Failures)\n","text":"Skill instructs the agent to install a package directly from a URL or VCS repository (pip install https://, pip install git+, npm install https://, etc.). Installing packages from arbitrary URLs bypasses registry integrity checks, signature verification, and audit trails. Attackers use this technique to deliver malware that does not appear in any public registry. Verify the source before allowing URL-based package installation."},"helpUri":"https://semgrep.dev/r/skills.command-execution.skill-install-from-vcs-url.skill-install-from-vcs-url","id":"skills.command-execution.skill-install-from-vcs-url.skill-install-from-vcs-url","name":"skills.command-execution.skill-install-from-vcs-url.skill-install-from-vcs-url","properties":{"precision":"very-high","tags":["CWE-494: Download of Code Without Integrity Check","MEDIUM CONFIDENCE","OWASP-A08:2021 - Software and Data Integrity Failures","OWASP-A08:2025 - Software or Data Integrity Failures","security"]},"shortDescription":{"text":"Semgrep Finding: skills.command-execution.skill-install-from-vcs-url.skill-install-from-vcs-url"}},{"defaultConfiguration":{"level":"warning"},"fullDescription":{"text":"Suspicious download-and-execute pattern: curl/wget piped directly to a shell interpreter. This pattern warrants investigation — it appears in malware distribution campaigns but also in legitimate tool installers. Review the source URL and surrounding context to determine intent."},"help":{"markdown":"Suspicious download-and-execute pattern: curl/wget piped directly to a shell interpreter. This pattern warrants investigation — it appears in malware distribution campaigns but also in legitimate tool installers. Review the source URL and surrounding context to determine intent.\n\n<b>References:</b>\n - [Semgrep Rule](https://semgrep.dev/r/skills.command-execution.skill-multi-stage-attack-bash.skill-multi-stage-attack-bash)\n - [https://attack.mitre.org/techniques/T1059/](https://attack.mitre.org/techniques/T1059/)\n - [https://attack.mitre.org/techniques/T1105/](https://attack.mitre.org/techniques/T1105/)\n - [https://owasp.org/Top10/2025/A05_2025-Injection/](https://owasp.org/Top10/2025/A05_2025-Injection/)\n - [https://owasp.org/Top10/A03_2021-Injection](https://owasp.org/Top10/A03_2021-Injection)\n","text":"Suspicious download-and-execute pattern: curl/wget piped directly to a shell interpreter. This pattern warrants investigation — it appears in malware distribution campaigns but also in legitimate tool installers. Review the source URL and surrounding context to determine intent."},"helpUri":"https://semgrep.dev/r/skills.command-execution.skill-multi-stage-attack-bash.skill-multi-stage-attack-bash","id":"skills.command-execution.skill-multi-stage-attack-bash.skill-multi-stage-attack-bash","name":"skills.command-execution.skill-multi-stage-attack-bash.skill-multi-stage-attack-bash","properties":{"precision":"very-high","tags":["CWE-94: Improper Control of Generation of Code ('Code Injection')","MEDIUM CONFIDENCE","OWASP-A03:2021 - Injection","OWASP-A05:2025 - Injection","security"]},"shortDescription":{"text":"Semgrep Finding: skills.command-execution.skill-multi-stage-attack-bash.skill-multi-stage-attack-bash"}},{"defaultConfiguration":{"level":"error"},"fullDescription":{"text":"Multi-stage attack: Downloads remote content and executes it. Detected fetch/axios followed by eval with data flow. HIGH SIGNAL - likely malicious."},"help":{"markdown":"Multi-stage attack: Downloads remote content and executes it. Detected fetch/axios followed by eval with data flow. HIGH SIGNAL - likely malicious.\n\n<b>References:</b>\n - [Semgrep Rule](https://semgrep.dev/r/skills.command-execution.skill-multi-stage-attack-javascript.skill-multi-stage-attack-javascript)\n - [https://attack.mitre.org/techniques/T1059/](https://attack.mitre.org/techniques/T1059/)\n - [https://attack.mitre.org/techniques/T1105/](https://attack.mitre.org/techniques/T1105/)\n - [https://owasp.org/Top10/2025/A05_2025-Injection/](https://owasp.org/Top10/2025/A05_2025-Injection/)\n - [https://owasp.org/Top10/A03_2021-Injection](https://owasp.org/Top10/A03_2021-Injection)\n","text":"Multi-stage attack: Downloads remote content and executes it. Detected fetch/axios followed by eval with data flow. HIGH SIGNAL - likely malicious."},"helpUri":"https://semgrep.dev/r/skills.command-execution.skill-multi-stage-attack-javascript.skill-multi-stage-attack-javascript","id":"skills.command-execution.skill-multi-stage-attack-javascript.skill-multi-stage-attack-javascript","name":"skills.command-execution.skill-multi-stage-attack-javascript.skill-multi-stage-attack-javascript","properties":{"precision":"very-high","tags":["CWE-94: Improper Control of Generation of Code ('Code Injection')","HIGH CONFIDENCE","OWASP-A03:2021 - Injection","OWASP-A05:2025 - Injection","security"]},"shortDescription":{"text":"Semgrep Finding: skills.command-execution.skill-multi-stage-attack-javascript.skill-multi-stage-attack-javascript"}},{"defaultConfiguration":{"level":"error"},"fullDescription":{"text":"Multi-stage attack: Downloads remote content and executes it. Detected download followed by exec/eval/subprocess on response data. HIGH SIGNAL - likely malicious."},"help":{"markdown":"Multi-stage attack: Downloads remote content and executes it. Detected download followed by exec/eval/subprocess on response data. HIGH SIGNAL - likely malicious.\n\n<b>References:</b>\n - [Semgrep Rule](https://semgrep.dev/r/skills.command-execution.skill-multi-stage-attack-python.skill-multi-stage-attack-python)\n - [https://attack.mitre.org/techniques/T1059/](https://attack.mitre.org/techniques/T1059/)\n - [https://attack.mitre.org/techniques/T1105/](https://attack.mitre.org/techniques/T1105/)\n - [https://owasp.org/Top10/2025/A05_2025-Injection/](https://owasp.org/Top10/2025/A05_2025-Injection/)\n - [https://owasp.org/Top10/A03_2021-Injection](https://owasp.org/Top10/A03_2021-Injection)\n","text":"Multi-stage attack: Downloads remote content and executes it. Detected download followed by exec/eval/subprocess on response data. HIGH SIGNAL - likely malicious."},"helpUri":"https://semgrep.dev/r/skills.command-execution.skill-multi-stage-attack-python.skill-multi-stage-attack-python","id":"skills.command-execution.skill-multi-stage-attack-python.skill-multi-stage-attack-python","name":"skills.command-execution.skill-multi-stage-attack-python.skill-multi-stage-attack-python","properties":{"precision":"very-high","tags":["CWE-94: Improper Control of Generation of Code ('Code Injection')","HIGH CONFIDENCE","OWASP-A03:2021 - Injection","OWASP-A05:2025 - Injection","security"]},"shortDescription":{"text":"Semgrep Finding: skills.command-execution.skill-multi-stage-attack-python.skill-multi-stage-attack-python"}},{"defaultConfiguration":{"level":"error"},"fullDescription":{"text":"Skill instructs downloading password-protected executable (social engineering). This detects social engineering instructions to download and extract password-protected executables, a common malware distribution tactic."},"help":{"markdown":"Skill instructs downloading password-protected executable (social engineering). This detects social engineering instructions to download and extract password-protected executables, a common malware distribution tactic.\n\n<b>References:</b>\n - [Semgrep Rule](https://semgrep.dev/r/skills.command-execution.skill-password-protected-binary-download.skill-password-protected-binary-download)\n - [https://cwe.mitre.org/data/definitions/494.html](https://cwe.mitre.org/data/definitions/494.html)\n - [https://owasp.org/Top10/2025/A08_2025-Software_or_Data_Integrity_Failures/](https://owasp.org/Top10/2025/A08_2025-Software_or_Data_Integrity_Failures/)\n - [https://owasp.org/Top10/A08_2021-Software_and_Data_Integrity_Failures](https://owasp.org/Top10/A08_2021-Software_and_Data_Integrity_Failures)\n - [https://www.koi.ai/blog/clawhavoc-341-malicious-clawedbot-skills-found-by-the-bot-they-were-targeting](https://www.koi.ai/blog/clawhavoc-341-malicious-clawedbot-skills-found-by-the-bot-they-were-targeting)\n","text":"Skill instructs downloading password-protected executable (social engineering). This detects social engineering instructions to download and extract password-protected executables, a common malware distribution tactic."},"helpUri":"https://semgrep.dev/r/skills.command-execution.skill-password-protected-binary-download.skill-password-protected-binary-download","id":"skills.command-execution.skill-password-protected-binary-download.skill-password-protected-binary-download","name":"skills.command-execution.skill-password-protected-binary-download.skill-password-protected-binary-download","properties":{"precision":"very-high","tags":["CWE-494: Download of Code Without Integrity Check","HIGH CONFIDENCE","OWASP-A08:2021 - Software and Data Integrity Failures","OWASP-A08:2025 - Software or Data Integrity Failures","security"]},"shortDescription":{"text":"Semgrep Finding: skills.command-execution.skill-password-protected-binary-download.skill-password-protected-binary-download"}},{"defaultConfiguration":{"level":"error"},"fullDescription":{"text":"Fetching executable content from a paste or code sharing service detected.\nThreat actors stage malicious scripts on free paste services to separate\nthe distribution channel from the payload, evading detection and allowing\npayload updates without modifying the delivery mechanism.\n\nPaste services (pastebin.com, hastebin, rentry.co, raw GitHub) are commonly\nused for secondary-stage payload hosting in supply chain attacks and the\nClawHavoc campaign. Using curl/wget to fetch raw content from these services\nfor execution is a high-confidence malicious indicator.\n\nIMPACT: Arbitrary code execution from attacker-controlled staging server\n"},"help":{"markdown":"Fetching executable content from a paste or code sharing service detected.\nThreat actors stage malicious scripts on free paste services to separate\nthe distribution channel from the payload, evading detection and allowing\npayload updates without modifying the delivery mechanism.\n\nPaste services (pastebin.com, hastebin, rentry.co, raw GitHub) are commonly\nused for secondary-stage payload hosting in supply chain attacks and the\nClawHavoc campaign. Using curl/wget to fetch raw content from these services\nfor execution is a high-confidence malicious indicator.\n\nIMPACT: Arbitrary code execution from attacker-controlled staging server\n\n\n<b>References:</b>\n - [Semgrep Rule](https://semgrep.dev/r/skills.command-execution.skill-pastebin-staging.skill-pastebin-staging)\n - [https://attack.mitre.org/techniques/T1102/](https://attack.mitre.org/techniques/T1102/)\n - [https://attack.mitre.org/techniques/T1608/001/](https://attack.mitre.org/techniques/T1608/001/)\n - [https://owasp.org/Top10/2025/A08_2025-Software_or_Data_Integrity_Failures/](https://owasp.org/Top10/2025/A08_2025-Software_or_Data_Integrity_Failures/)\n - [https://owasp.org/Top10/A08_2021-Software_and_Data_Integrity_Failures](https://owasp.org/Top10/A08_2021-Software_and_Data_Integrity_Failures)\n - [https://www.koi.ai/blog/clawhavoc-341-malicious-clawedbot-skills-found-by-the-bot-they-were-targeting](https://www.koi.ai/blog/clawhavoc-341-malicious-clawedbot-skills-found-by-the-bot-they-were-targeting)\n","text":"Fetching executable content from a paste or code sharing service detected.\nThreat actors stage malicious scripts on free paste services to separate\nthe distribution channel from the payload, evading detection and allowing\npayload updates without modifying the delivery mechanism.\n\nPaste services (pastebin.com, hastebin, rentry.co, raw GitHub) are commonly\nused for secondary-stage payload hosting in supply chain attacks and the\nClawHavoc campaign. Using curl/wget to fetch raw content from these services\nfor execution is a high-confidence malicious indicator.\n\nIMPACT: Arbitrary code execution from attacker-controlled staging server\n"},"helpUri":"https://semgrep.dev/r/skills.command-execution.skill-pastebin-staging.skill-pastebin-staging","id":"skills.command-execution.skill-pastebin-staging.skill-pastebin-staging","name":"skills.command-execution.skill-pastebin-staging.skill-pastebin-staging","properties":{"precision":"very-high","tags":["CWE-494: Download of Code Without Integrity Check","HIGH CONFIDENCE","OWASP-A08:2021 - Software and Data Integrity Failures","OWASP-A08:2025 - Software or Data Integrity Failures","security"]},"shortDescription":{"text":"Semgrep Finding: skills.command-execution.skill-pastebin-staging.skill-pastebin-staging"}},{"defaultConfiguration":{"level":"error"},"fullDescription":{"text":"PowerShell Invoke-Expression (IEX) with base64 decoding detected. This pattern\nuses PowerShell's IEX command with base64 decoding to execute obfuscated code.\nThis technique is commonly used for:\n\n- Obfuscated command execution that bypasses basic static analysis\n- Red team exercises and penetration testing\n- Malware delivery and persistence mechanisms\n- Command & Control (C2) payload execution\n\nThe base64 encoding hides the actual commands from security tools and makes\nforensic analysis more difficult. Legitimate use of this pattern is rare.\n"},"help":{"markdown":"PowerShell Invoke-Expression (IEX) with base64 decoding detected. This pattern\nuses PowerShell's IEX command with base64 decoding to execute obfuscated code.\nThis technique is commonly used for:\n\n- Obfuscated command execution that bypasses basic static analysis\n- Red team exercises and penetration testing\n- Malware delivery and persistence mechanisms\n- Command & Control (C2) payload execution\n\nThe base64 encoding hides the actual commands from security tools and makes\nforensic analysis more difficult. Legitimate use of this pattern is rare.\n\n\n<b>References:</b>\n - [Semgrep Rule](https://semgrep.dev/r/skills.command-execution.skill-powershell-iex-base64.skill-powershell-iex-base64)\n - [https://owasp.org/Top10/2025/A05_2025-Injection/](https://owasp.org/Top10/2025/A05_2025-Injection/)\n - [https://owasp.org/Top10/A03_2021-Injection](https://owasp.org/Top10/A03_2021-Injection)\n","text":"PowerShell Invoke-Expression (IEX) with base64 decoding detected. This pattern\nuses PowerShell's IEX command with base64 decoding to execute obfuscated code.\nThis technique is commonly used for:\n\n- Obfuscated command execution that bypasses basic static analysis\n- Red team exercises and penetration testing\n- Malware delivery and persistence mechanisms\n- Command & Control (C2) payload execution\n\nThe base64 encoding hides the actual commands from security tools and makes\nforensic analysis more difficult. Legitimate use of this pattern is rare.\n"},"helpUri":"https://semgrep.dev/r/skills.command-execution.skill-powershell-iex-base64.skill-powershell-iex-base64","id":"skills.command-execution.skill-powershell-iex-base64.skill-powershell-iex-base64","name":"skills.command-execution.skill-powershell-iex-base64.skill-powershell-iex-base64","properties":{"precision":"very-high","tags":["CWE-78: Improper Neutralization of Special Elements used in an OS Command ('OS Command Injection')","HIGH CONFIDENCE","OWASP-A01:2017 - Injection","OWASP-A03:2021 - Injection","OWASP-A05:2025 - Injection","security"]},"shortDescription":{"text":"Semgrep Finding: skills.command-execution.skill-powershell-iex-base64.skill-powershell-iex-base64"}},{"defaultConfiguration":{"level":"error"},"fullDescription":{"text":"Python exec on base64-decoded data. Using exec() on decoded base64 is a common obfuscation technique to hide malicious Python code."},"help":{"markdown":"Python exec on base64-decoded data. Using exec() on decoded base64 is a common obfuscation technique to hide malicious Python code.\n\n<b>References:</b>\n - [Semgrep Rule](https://semgrep.dev/r/skills.command-execution.skill-python-base64-exec.skill-python-base64-exec)\n - [https://owasp.org/Top10/2025/A05_2025-Injection/](https://owasp.org/Top10/2025/A05_2025-Injection/)\n - [https://owasp.org/Top10/A03_2021-Injection](https://owasp.org/Top10/A03_2021-Injection)\n","text":"Python exec on base64-decoded data. Using exec() on decoded base64 is a common obfuscation technique to hide malicious Python code."},"helpUri":"https://semgrep.dev/r/skills.command-execution.skill-python-base64-exec.skill-python-base64-exec","id":"skills.command-execution.skill-python-base64-exec.skill-python-base64-exec","name":"skills.command-execution.skill-python-base64-exec.skill-python-base64-exec","properties":{"precision":"very-high","tags":["CWE-94: Improper Control of Generation of Code ('Code Injection')","HIGH CONFIDENCE","OWASP-A03:2021 - Injection","OWASP-A05:2025 - Injection","security"]},"shortDescription":{"text":"Semgrep Finding: skills.command-execution.skill-python-base64-exec.skill-python-base64-exec"}},{"defaultConfiguration":{"level":"error"},"fullDescription":{"text":"Obvious malicious subprocess pattern detected: - Pipe to bash/sh (curl|bash, wget|sh, etc) - Reverse shell tools (nc, netcat, /dev/tcp) - Persistence (crontab, @reboot) HIGH SIGNAL - review immediately."},"help":{"markdown":"Obvious malicious subprocess pattern detected: - Pipe to bash/sh (curl|bash, wget|sh, etc) - Reverse shell tools (nc, netcat, /dev/tcp) - Persistence (crontab, @reboot) HIGH SIGNAL - review immediately.\n\n<b>References:</b>\n - [Semgrep Rule](https://semgrep.dev/r/skills.command-execution.skill-python-subprocess.skill-python-subprocess-execution)\n - [https://attack.mitre.org/techniques/T1059/](https://attack.mitre.org/techniques/T1059/)\n - [https://owasp.org/Top10/2025/A05_2025-Injection/](https://owasp.org/Top10/2025/A05_2025-Injection/)\n - [https://owasp.org/Top10/A03_2021-Injection](https://owasp.org/Top10/A03_2021-Injection)\n - [https://owasp.org/www-community/attacks/Command_Injection](https://owasp.org/www-community/attacks/Command_Injection)\n","text":"Obvious malicious subprocess pattern detected: - Pipe to bash/sh (curl|bash, wget|sh, etc) - Reverse shell tools (nc, netcat, /dev/tcp) - Persistence (crontab, @reboot) HIGH SIGNAL - review immediately."},"helpUri":"https://semgrep.dev/r/skills.command-execution.skill-python-subprocess.skill-python-subprocess-execution","id":"skills.command-execution.skill-python-subprocess.skill-python-subprocess-execution","name":"skills.command-execution.skill-python-subprocess.skill-python-subprocess-execution","properties":{"precision":"very-high","tags":["CWE-78: Improper Neutralization of Special Elements used in an OS Command ('OS Command Injection')","HIGH CONFIDENCE","OWASP-A01:2017 - Injection","OWASP-A03:2021 - Injection","OWASP-A05:2025 - Injection","security"]},"shortDescription":{"text":"Semgrep Finding: skills.command-execution.skill-python-subprocess.skill-python-subprocess-execution"}},{"defaultConfiguration":{"level":"error"},"fullDescription":{"text":"Reverse shell pattern detected - netcat/socat with shell execution"},"help":{"markdown":"Reverse shell pattern detected - netcat/socat with shell execution\n\n<b>References:</b>\n - [Semgrep Rule](https://semgrep.dev/r/skills.command-execution.skill-reverse-shell.skill-reverse-shell)\n - [https://github.com/swisskyrepo/PayloadsAllTheThings/blob/master/Methodology%20and%20Resources/Reverse%20Shell%20Cheatsheet.md](https://github.com/swisskyrepo/PayloadsAllTheThings/blob/master/Methodology%20and%20Resources/Reverse%20Shell%20Cheatsheet.md)\n - [https://owasp.org/Top10/2025/A05_2025-Injection/](https://owasp.org/Top10/2025/A05_2025-Injection/)\n - [https://owasp.org/Top10/A03_2021-Injection](https://owasp.org/Top10/A03_2021-Injection)\n - [https://pentestmonkey.net/cheat-sheet/shells/reverse-shell-cheat-sheet](https://pentestmonkey.net/cheat-sheet/shells/reverse-shell-cheat-sheet)\n","text":"Reverse shell pattern detected - netcat/socat with shell execution"},"helpUri":"https://semgrep.dev/r/skills.command-execution.skill-reverse-shell.skill-reverse-shell","id":"skills.command-execution.skill-reverse-shell.skill-reverse-shell","name":"skills.command-execution.skill-reverse-shell.skill-reverse-shell","properties":{"precision":"very-high","tags":["CWE-78: Improper Neutralization of Special Elements used in an OS Command ('OS Command Injection')","HIGH CONFIDENCE","OWASP-A01:2017 - Injection","OWASP-A03:2021 - Injection","OWASP-A05:2025 - Injection","security"]},"shortDescription":{"text":"Semgrep Finding: skills.command-execution.skill-reverse-shell.skill-reverse-shell"}},{"defaultConfiguration":{"level":"error"},"fullDescription":{"text":"Detects execution of bash/sh with -c flag for pipe operations"},"help":{"markdown":"Detects execution of bash/sh with -c flag for pipe operations\n\n<b>References:</b>\n - [Semgrep Rule](https://semgrep.dev/r/skills.command-execution.skill-rust-command-bash-pipe.skill-rust-command-bash-pipe)\n - [https://attack.mitre.org/techniques/T1059/](https://attack.mitre.org/techniques/T1059/)\n - [https://owasp.org/Top10/2025/A05_2025-Injection/](https://owasp.org/Top10/2025/A05_2025-Injection/)\n - [https://owasp.org/Top10/A03_2021-Injection](https://owasp.org/Top10/A03_2021-Injection)\n - [https://owasp.org/www-community/attacks/Command_Injection](https://owasp.org/www-community/attacks/Command_Injection)\n","text":"Detects execution of bash/sh with -c flag for pipe operations"},"helpUri":"https://semgrep.dev/r/skills.command-execution.skill-rust-command-bash-pipe.skill-rust-command-bash-pipe","id":"skills.command-execution.skill-rust-command-bash-pipe.skill-rust-command-bash-pipe","name":"skills.command-execution.skill-rust-command-bash-pipe.skill-rust-command-bash-pipe","properties":{"precision":"very-high","tags":["CWE-78: Improper Neutralization of Special Elements used in an OS Command ('OS Command Injection')","HIGH CONFIDENCE","OWASP-A01:2017 - Injection","OWASP-A03:2021 - Injection","OWASP-A05:2025 - Injection","security"]},"shortDescription":{"text":"Semgrep Finding: skills.command-execution.skill-rust-command-bash-pipe.skill-rust-command-bash-pipe"}},{"defaultConfiguration":{"level":"error"},"fullDescription":{"text":"Detects bash reverse shell patterns using /dev/tcp"},"help":{"markdown":"Detects bash reverse shell patterns using /dev/tcp\n\n<b>References:</b>\n - [Semgrep Rule](https://semgrep.dev/r/skills.command-execution.skill-rust-command-dev-tcp.skill-rust-command-dev-tcp)\n - [https://attack.mitre.org/techniques/T1059/](https://attack.mitre.org/techniques/T1059/)\n - [https://owasp.org/Top10/2025/A05_2025-Injection/](https://owasp.org/Top10/2025/A05_2025-Injection/)\n - [https://owasp.org/Top10/A03_2021-Injection](https://owasp.org/Top10/A03_2021-Injection)\n - [https://owasp.org/www-community/attacks/Command_Injection](https://owasp.org/www-community/attacks/Command_Injection)\n","text":"Detects bash reverse shell patterns using /dev/tcp"},"helpUri":"https://semgrep.dev/r/skills.command-execution.skill-rust-command-dev-tcp.skill-rust-command-dev-tcp","id":"skills.command-execution.skill-rust-command-dev-tcp.skill-rust-command-dev-tcp","name":"skills.command-execution.skill-rust-command-dev-tcp.skill-rust-command-dev-tcp","properties":{"precision":"very-high","tags":["CWE-78: Improper Neutralization of Special Elements used in an OS Command ('OS Command Injection')","HIGH CONFIDENCE","OWASP-A01:2017 - Injection","OWASP-A03:2021 - Injection","OWASP-A05:2025 - Injection","security"]},"shortDescription":{"text":"Semgrep Finding: skills.command-execution.skill-rust-command-dev-tcp.skill-rust-command-dev-tcp"}},{"defaultConfiguration":{"level":"error"},"fullDescription":{"text":"Detects execution of network tools commonly used for exfiltration or reverse shells"},"help":{"markdown":"Detects execution of network tools commonly used for exfiltration or reverse shells\n\n<b>References:</b>\n - [Semgrep Rule](https://semgrep.dev/r/skills.command-execution.skill-rust-command-network-tools.skill-rust-command-network-tools)\n - [https://attack.mitre.org/techniques/T1059/](https://attack.mitre.org/techniques/T1059/)\n - [https://owasp.org/Top10/2025/A05_2025-Injection/](https://owasp.org/Top10/2025/A05_2025-Injection/)\n - [https://owasp.org/Top10/A03_2021-Injection](https://owasp.org/Top10/A03_2021-Injection)\n - [https://owasp.org/www-community/attacks/Command_Injection](https://owasp.org/www-community/attacks/Command_Injection)\n","text":"Detects execution of network tools commonly used for exfiltration or reverse shells"},"helpUri":"https://semgrep.dev/r/skills.command-execution.skill-rust-command-network-tools.skill-rust-command-network-tools","id":"skills.command-execution.skill-rust-command-network-tools.skill-rust-command-network-tools","name":"skills.command-execution.skill-rust-command-network-tools.skill-rust-command-network-tools","properties":{"precision":"very-high","tags":["CWE-78: Improper Neutralization of Special Elements used in an OS Command ('OS Command Injection')","HIGH CONFIDENCE","OWASP-A01:2017 - Injection","OWASP-A03:2021 - Injection","OWASP-A05:2025 - Injection","security"]},"shortDescription":{"text":"Semgrep Finding: skills.command-execution.skill-rust-command-network-tools.skill-rust-command-network-tools"}},{"defaultConfiguration":{"level":"warning"},"fullDescription":{"text":"AWS credentials file access combined with network exfiltration pattern found. Reading ~/.aws/credentials and piping to a network tool on the same line warrants investigation as a possible cloud credential theft attempt. This pattern also appears in security scanning tools that demonstrate the technique. Verify whether this access is user-authorized."},"help":{"markdown":"AWS credentials file access combined with network exfiltration pattern found. Reading ~/.aws/credentials and piping to a network tool on the same line warrants investigation as a possible cloud credential theft attempt. This pattern also appears in security scanning tools that demonstrate the technique. Verify whether this access is user-authorized.\n\n<b>References:</b>\n - [Semgrep Rule](https://semgrep.dev/r/skills.credential-access.skill-aws-credentials-read.skill-aws-credentials-read)\n - [https://attack.mitre.org/techniques/T1552/001/](https://attack.mitre.org/techniques/T1552/001/)\n - [https://owasp.org/Top10/2025/A06_2025-Insecure_Design/](https://owasp.org/Top10/2025/A06_2025-Insecure_Design/)\n - [https://owasp.org/Top10/A04_2021-Insecure_Design](https://owasp.org/Top10/A04_2021-Insecure_Design)\n - [https://owasp.org/Top10/A07_2021-Identification_and_Authentication_Failures](https://owasp.org/Top10/A07_2021-Identification_and_Authentication_Failures)\n","text":"AWS credentials file access combined with network exfiltration pattern found. Reading ~/.aws/credentials and piping to a network tool on the same line warrants investigation as a possible cloud credential theft attempt. This pattern also appears in security scanning tools that demonstrate the technique. Verify whether this access is user-authorized."},"helpUri":"https://semgrep.dev/r/skills.credential-access.skill-aws-credentials-read.skill-aws-credentials-read","id":"skills.credential-access.skill-aws-credentials-read.skill-aws-credentials-read","name":"skills.credential-access.skill-aws-credentials-read.skill-aws-credentials-read","properties":{"precision":"very-high","tags":["CWE-522: Insufficiently Protected Credentials","MEDIUM CONFIDENCE","OWASP-A02:2017 - Broken Authentication","OWASP-A04:2021 - Insecure Design","OWASP-A06:2025 - Insecure Design","security"]},"shortDescription":{"text":"Semgrep Finding: skills.credential-access.skill-aws-credentials-read.skill-aws-credentials-read"}},{"defaultConfiguration":{"level":"error"},"fullDescription":{"text":"AWS credential environment variable piped or passed to a network tool.\nThis pattern exfiltrates AWS access keys from the agent's runtime environment\nto an attacker-controlled endpoint.\n\nDocumentation references (AWS_ACCESS_KEY_ID=<value>, table entries, etc.) are\nnot flagged; only actual variable reads combined with a network operation are.\n\nIMPACT: Full AWS credential exposure enabling account takeover\n"},"help":{"markdown":"AWS credential environment variable piped or passed to a network tool.\nThis pattern exfiltrates AWS access keys from the agent's runtime environment\nto an attacker-controlled endpoint.\n\nDocumentation references (AWS_ACCESS_KEY_ID=<value>, table entries, etc.) are\nnot flagged; only actual variable reads combined with a network operation are.\n\nIMPACT: Full AWS credential exposure enabling account takeover\n\n\n<b>References:</b>\n - [Semgrep Rule](https://semgrep.dev/r/skills.credential-access.skill-aws-env-access.skill-aws-env-access)\n - [https://attack.mitre.org/techniques/T1552/001/](https://attack.mitre.org/techniques/T1552/001/)\n - [https://cwe.mitre.org/data/definitions/522.html](https://cwe.mitre.org/data/definitions/522.html)\n - [https://owasp.org/Top10/2025/A06_2025-Insecure_Design/](https://owasp.org/Top10/2025/A06_2025-Insecure_Design/)\n - [https://owasp.org/Top10/A04_2021-Insecure_Design](https://owasp.org/Top10/A04_2021-Insecure_Design)\n - [https://owasp.org/Top10/A07_2021-Identification_and_Authentication_Failures](https://owasp.org/Top10/A07_2021-Identification_and_Authentication_Failures)\n","text":"AWS credential environment variable piped or passed to a network tool.\nThis pattern exfiltrates AWS access keys from the agent's runtime environment\nto an attacker-controlled endpoint.\n\nDocumentation references (AWS_ACCESS_KEY_ID=<value>, table entries, etc.) are\nnot flagged; only actual variable reads combined with a network operation are.\n\nIMPACT: Full AWS credential exposure enabling account takeover\n"},"helpUri":"https://semgrep.dev/r/skills.credential-access.skill-aws-env-access.skill-aws-env-access","id":"skills.credential-access.skill-aws-env-access.skill-aws-env-access","name":"skills.credential-access.skill-aws-env-access.skill-aws-env-access","properties":{"precision":"very-high","tags":["CWE-522: Insufficiently Protected Credentials","HIGH CONFIDENCE","OWASP-A02:2017 - Broken Authentication","OWASP-A04:2021 - Insecure Design","OWASP-A06:2025 - Insecure Design","security"]},"shortDescription":{"text":"Semgrep Finding: skills.credential-access.skill-aws-env-access.skill-aws-env-access"}},{"defaultConfiguration":{"level":"error"},"fullDescription":{"text":"Azure credentials file access detected. Reading Azure credential files or tokens is a cloud credential theft technique."},"help":{"markdown":"Azure credentials file access detected. Reading Azure credential files or tokens is a cloud credential theft technique.\n\n<b>References:</b>\n - [Semgrep Rule](https://semgrep.dev/r/skills.credential-access.skill-azure-credentials-read.skill-azure-credentials-read)\n - [https://cwe.mitre.org/data/definitions/522.html](https://cwe.mitre.org/data/definitions/522.html)\n - [https://owasp.org/Top10/2025/A06_2025-Insecure_Design/](https://owasp.org/Top10/2025/A06_2025-Insecure_Design/)\n - [https://owasp.org/Top10/A04_2021-Insecure_Design](https://owasp.org/Top10/A04_2021-Insecure_Design)\n - [https://owasp.org/Top10/A07_2021-Identification_and_Authentication_Failures](https://owasp.org/Top10/A07_2021-Identification_and_Authentication_Failures)\n","text":"Azure credentials file access detected. Reading Azure credential files or tokens is a cloud credential theft technique."},"helpUri":"https://semgrep.dev/r/skills.credential-access.skill-azure-credentials-read.skill-azure-credentials-read","id":"skills.credential-access.skill-azure-credentials-read.skill-azure-credentials-read","name":"skills.credential-access.skill-azure-credentials-read.skill-azure-credentials-read","properties":{"precision":"very-high","tags":["CWE-522: Insufficiently Protected Credentials","HIGH CONFIDENCE","OWASP-A02:2017 - Broken Authentication","OWASP-A04:2021 - Insecure Design","OWASP-A06:2025 - Insecure Design","security"]},"shortDescription":{"text":"Semgrep Finding: skills.credential-access.skill-azure-credentials-read.skill-azure-credentials-read"}},{"defaultConfiguration":{"level":"error"},"fullDescription":{"text":"Azure credential environment variable piped or passed to a network tool.\nThis pattern exfiltrates Azure service principal credentials from the agent's\nruntime environment to an attacker-controlled endpoint.\n\nDocumentation setup examples (AZURE_CLIENT_ID=<app-client-id>) and legitimate\nAzure CLI usage (az login) are not flagged; only reads combined with a\nnon-Azure network operation are.\n\nIMPACT: Full Azure service principal credential exposure enabling subscription takeover\n"},"help":{"markdown":"Azure credential environment variable piped or passed to a network tool.\nThis pattern exfiltrates Azure service principal credentials from the agent's\nruntime environment to an attacker-controlled endpoint.\n\nDocumentation setup examples (AZURE_CLIENT_ID=<app-client-id>) and legitimate\nAzure CLI usage (az login) are not flagged; only reads combined with a\nnon-Azure network operation are.\n\nIMPACT: Full Azure service principal credential exposure enabling subscription takeover\n\n\n<b>References:</b>\n - [Semgrep Rule](https://semgrep.dev/r/skills.credential-access.skill-azure-env-access.skill-azure-env-access)\n - [https://attack.mitre.org/techniques/T1552/001/](https://attack.mitre.org/techniques/T1552/001/)\n - [https://cwe.mitre.org/data/definitions/522.html](https://cwe.mitre.org/data/definitions/522.html)\n - [https://owasp.org/Top10/2025/A06_2025-Insecure_Design/](https://owasp.org/Top10/2025/A06_2025-Insecure_Design/)\n - [https://owasp.org/Top10/A04_2021-Insecure_Design](https://owasp.org/Top10/A04_2021-Insecure_Design)\n - [https://owasp.org/Top10/A07_2021-Identification_and_Authentication_Failures](https://owasp.org/Top10/A07_2021-Identification_and_Authentication_Failures)\n","text":"Azure credential environment variable piped or passed to a network tool.\nThis pattern exfiltrates Azure service principal credentials from the agent's\nruntime environment to an attacker-controlled endpoint.\n\nDocumentation setup examples (AZURE_CLIENT_ID=<app-client-id>) and legitimate\nAzure CLI usage (az login) are not flagged; only reads combined with a\nnon-Azure network operation are.\n\nIMPACT: Full Azure service principal credential exposure enabling subscription takeover\n"},"helpUri":"https://semgrep.dev/r/skills.credential-access.skill-azure-env-access.skill-azure-env-access","id":"skills.credential-access.skill-azure-env-access.skill-azure-env-access","name":"skills.credential-access.skill-azure-env-access.skill-azure-env-access","properties":{"precision":"very-high","tags":["CWE-522: Insufficiently Protected Credentials","HIGH CONFIDENCE","OWASP-A02:2017 - Broken Authentication","OWASP-A04:2021 - Insecure Design","OWASP-A06:2025 - Insecure Design","security"]},"shortDescription":{"text":"Semgrep Finding: skills.credential-access.skill-azure-env-access.skill-azure-env-access"}},{"defaultConfiguration":{"level":"error"},"fullDescription":{"text":"Bitcoin wallet access detected. Reading Bitcoin Core wallet files (wallet.dat) or configuration is cryptocurrency theft."},"help":{"markdown":"Bitcoin wallet access detected. Reading Bitcoin Core wallet files (wallet.dat) or configuration is cryptocurrency theft.\n\n<b>References:</b>\n - [Semgrep Rule](https://semgrep.dev/r/skills.credential-access.skill-bitcoin-wallet-read.skill-bitcoin-wallet-read)\n - [https://cwe.mitre.org/data/definitions/522.html](https://cwe.mitre.org/data/definitions/522.html)\n - [https://owasp.org/Top10/2025/A06_2025-Insecure_Design/](https://owasp.org/Top10/2025/A06_2025-Insecure_Design/)\n - [https://owasp.org/Top10/A04_2021-Insecure_Design](https://owasp.org/Top10/A04_2021-Insecure_Design)\n - [https://owasp.org/Top10/A07_2021-Identification_and_Authentication_Failures](https://owasp.org/Top10/A07_2021-Identification_and_Authentication_Failures)\n","text":"Bitcoin wallet access detected. Reading Bitcoin Core wallet files (wallet.dat) or configuration is cryptocurrency theft."},"helpUri":"https://semgrep.dev/r/skills.credential-access.skill-bitcoin-wallet-read.skill-bitcoin-wallet-read","id":"skills.credential-access.skill-bitcoin-wallet-read.skill-bitcoin-wallet-read","name":"skills.credential-access.skill-bitcoin-wallet-read.skill-bitcoin-wallet-read","properties":{"precision":"very-high","tags":["CWE-522: Insufficiently Protected Credentials","HIGH CONFIDENCE","OWASP-A02:2017 - Broken Authentication","OWASP-A04:2021 - Insecure Design","OWASP-A06:2025 - Insecure Design","security"]},"shortDescription":{"text":"Semgrep Finding: skills.credential-access.skill-bitcoin-wallet-read.skill-bitcoin-wallet-read"}},{"defaultConfiguration":{"level":"error"},"fullDescription":{"text":"Browser credential database access detected. Accessing Chrome, Firefox,\nSafari, or Edge password/cookie stores is a standard infostealer technique.\n\nChrome stores passwords in \"Login Data\" (SQLite) with encryption keys in\n\"Local State\". Firefox uses \"logins.json\" + \"key4.db\". These files contain\nall saved passwords and are targeted by commodity infostealers (Redline,\nVidar, AMOS) and by threat actor tools (Lazagne, HackerBrowserData).\n\nIMPACT: Mass credential compromise across all browser-saved accounts\n"},"help":{"markdown":"Browser credential database access detected. Accessing Chrome, Firefox,\nSafari, or Edge password/cookie stores is a standard infostealer technique.\n\nChrome stores passwords in \"Login Data\" (SQLite) with encryption keys in\n\"Local State\". Firefox uses \"logins.json\" + \"key4.db\". These files contain\nall saved passwords and are targeted by commodity infostealers (Redline,\nVidar, AMOS) and by threat actor tools (Lazagne, HackerBrowserData).\n\nIMPACT: Mass credential compromise across all browser-saved accounts\n\n\n<b>References:</b>\n - [Semgrep Rule](https://semgrep.dev/r/skills.credential-access.skill-browser-credential-theft.skill-browser-credential-theft)\n - [https://attack.mitre.org/techniques/T1555/003/](https://attack.mitre.org/techniques/T1555/003/)\n - [https://cwe.mitre.org/data/definitions/522.html](https://cwe.mitre.org/data/definitions/522.html)\n - [https://owasp.org/Top10/2025/A06_2025-Insecure_Design/](https://owasp.org/Top10/2025/A06_2025-Insecure_Design/)\n - [https://owasp.org/Top10/A04_2021-Insecure_Design](https://owasp.org/Top10/A04_2021-Insecure_Design)\n - [https://owasp.org/Top10/A07_2021-Identification_and_Authentication_Failures](https://owasp.org/Top10/A07_2021-Identification_and_Authentication_Failures)\n","text":"Browser credential database access detected. Accessing Chrome, Firefox,\nSafari, or Edge password/cookie stores is a standard infostealer technique.\n\nChrome stores passwords in \"Login Data\" (SQLite) with encryption keys in\n\"Local State\". Firefox uses \"logins.json\" + \"key4.db\". These files contain\nall saved passwords and are targeted by commodity infostealers (Redline,\nVidar, AMOS) and by threat actor tools (Lazagne, HackerBrowserData).\n\nIMPACT: Mass credential compromise across all browser-saved accounts\n"},"helpUri":"https://semgrep.dev/r/skills.credential-access.skill-browser-credential-theft.skill-browser-credential-theft","id":"skills.credential-access.skill-browser-credential-theft.skill-browser-credential-theft","name":"skills.credential-access.skill-browser-credential-theft.skill-browser-credential-theft","properties":{"precision":"very-high","tags":["CWE-522: Insufficiently Protected Credentials","HIGH CONFIDENCE","OWASP-A02:2017 - Broken Authentication","OWASP-A04:2021 - Insecure Design","OWASP-A06:2025 - Insecure Design","security"]},"shortDescription":{"text":"Semgrep Finding: skills.credential-access.skill-browser-credential-theft.skill-browser-credential-theft"}},{"defaultConfiguration":{"level":"error"},"fullDescription":{"text":"Cloud instance metadata service (IMDS) access detected. Accessing the\nmetadata service at 169.254.169.254 (AWS/Azure), metadata.google.internal\n(GCP), or equivalent endpoints returns temporary cloud credentials (IAM\nroles, service account tokens) that can be used to access cloud resources.\n\nIMDSv1 requires no authentication. The Capital One breach and many supply\nchain attacks exploited this. UNC2903 and other threat actors abuse IMDS\nto steal cloud credentials from compromised instances.\n\nIMPACT: Cloud credential theft, lateral movement to cloud infrastructure\n"},"help":{"markdown":"Cloud instance metadata service (IMDS) access detected. Accessing the\nmetadata service at 169.254.169.254 (AWS/Azure), metadata.google.internal\n(GCP), or equivalent endpoints returns temporary cloud credentials (IAM\nroles, service account tokens) that can be used to access cloud resources.\n\nIMDSv1 requires no authentication. The Capital One breach and many supply\nchain attacks exploited this. UNC2903 and other threat actors abuse IMDS\nto steal cloud credentials from compromised instances.\n\nIMPACT: Cloud credential theft, lateral movement to cloud infrastructure\n\n\n<b>References:</b>\n - [Semgrep Rule](https://semgrep.dev/r/skills.credential-access.skill-cloud-metadata-access.skill-cloud-metadata-access)\n - [https://attack.mitre.org/techniques/T1552/005/](https://attack.mitre.org/techniques/T1552/005/)\n - [https://cloud.google.com/blog/topics/threat-intelligence/cloud-metadata-abuse-unc2903/](https://cloud.google.com/blog/topics/threat-intelligence/cloud-metadata-abuse-unc2903/)\n - [https://owasp.org/Top10/2025/A01_2025-Broken_Access_Control/](https://owasp.org/Top10/2025/A01_2025-Broken_Access_Control/)\n - [https://owasp.org/Top10/A10_2021-Server-Side_Request_Forgery_%28SSRF%29](https://owasp.org/Top10/A10_2021-Server-Side_Request_Forgery_%28SSRF%29)\n - [https://securitylabs.datadoghq.com/cloud-security-atlas/attacks/stealing-ec2-instance-role-credentials/](https://securitylabs.datadoghq.com/cloud-security-atlas/attacks/stealing-ec2-instance-role-credentials/)\n","text":"Cloud instance metadata service (IMDS) access detected. Accessing the\nmetadata service at 169.254.169.254 (AWS/Azure), metadata.google.internal\n(GCP), or equivalent endpoints returns temporary cloud credentials (IAM\nroles, service account tokens) that can be used to access cloud resources.\n\nIMDSv1 requires no authentication. The Capital One breach and many supply\nchain attacks exploited this. UNC2903 and other threat actors abuse IMDS\nto steal cloud credentials from compromised instances.\n\nIMPACT: Cloud credential theft, lateral movement to cloud infrastructure\n"},"helpUri":"https://semgrep.dev/r/skills.credential-access.skill-cloud-metadata-access.skill-cloud-metadata-access","id":"skills.credential-access.skill-cloud-metadata-access.skill-cloud-metadata-access","name":"skills.credential-access.skill-cloud-metadata-access.skill-cloud-metadata-access","properties":{"precision":"very-high","tags":["CWE-918: Server-Side Request Forgery (SSRF)","HIGH CONFIDENCE","OWASP-A01:2025 - Broken Access Control","OWASP-A10:2021 - Server-Side Request Forgery (SSRF)","security"]},"shortDescription":{"text":"Semgrep Finding: skills.credential-access.skill-cloud-metadata-access.skill-cloud-metadata-access"}},{"defaultConfiguration":{"level":"warning"},"fullDescription":{"text":"Suspicious container or Kubernetes resource access pattern found. Accessing the Docker socket, running privileged containers, or reading Kubernetes service account tokens may indicate an attempt to escape container isolation or access cluster credentials. This pattern warrants investigation — Docker volume mounts and Kubernetes tokens also appear in legitimate containerized agent deployments. Review whether this access is explicitly user-authorized."},"help":{"markdown":"Suspicious container or Kubernetes resource access pattern found. Accessing the Docker socket, running privileged containers, or reading Kubernetes service account tokens may indicate an attempt to escape container isolation or access cluster credentials. This pattern warrants investigation — Docker volume mounts and Kubernetes tokens also appear in legitimate containerized agent deployments. Review whether this access is explicitly user-authorized.\n\n<b>References:</b>\n - [Semgrep Rule](https://semgrep.dev/r/skills.credential-access.skill-container-escape.skill-container-escape)\n - [https://attack.mitre.org/techniques/T1611/](https://attack.mitre.org/techniques/T1611/)\n - [https://book.hacktricks.wiki/en/linux-hardening/privilege-escalation/docker-security/abusing-docker-socket-for-privilege-escalation.html](https://book.hacktricks.wiki/en/linux-hardening/privilege-escalation/docker-security/abusing-docker-socket-for-privilege-escalation.html)\n - [https://owasp.org/Top10/2025/A01_2025-Broken_Access_Control/](https://owasp.org/Top10/2025/A01_2025-Broken_Access_Control/)\n - [https://owasp.org/Top10/A01_2021-Broken_Access_Control](https://owasp.org/Top10/A01_2021-Broken_Access_Control)\n","text":"Suspicious container or Kubernetes resource access pattern found. Accessing the Docker socket, running privileged containers, or reading Kubernetes service account tokens may indicate an attempt to escape container isolation or access cluster credentials. This pattern warrants investigation — Docker volume mounts and Kubernetes tokens also appear in legitimate containerized agent deployments. Review whether this access is explicitly user-authorized."},"helpUri":"https://semgrep.dev/r/skills.credential-access.skill-container-escape.skill-container-escape","id":"skills.credential-access.skill-container-escape.skill-container-escape","name":"skills.credential-access.skill-container-escape.skill-container-escape","properties":{"precision":"very-high","tags":["CWE-284: Improper Access Control","MEDIUM CONFIDENCE","OWASP-A01:2021 - Broken Access Control","OWASP-A01:2025 - Broken Access Control","OWASP-A05:2017 - Broken Access Control","security"]},"shortDescription":{"text":"Semgrep Finding: skills.credential-access.skill-container-escape.skill-container-escape"}},{"defaultConfiguration":{"level":"error"},"fullDescription":{"text":"Ethereum wallet access detected. Reading Ethereum keystore files is cryptocurrency theft. Keystore files are in ~/.ethereum/keystore/."},"help":{"markdown":"Ethereum wallet access detected. Reading Ethereum keystore files is cryptocurrency theft. Keystore files are in ~/.ethereum/keystore/.\n\n<b>References:</b>\n - [Semgrep Rule](https://semgrep.dev/r/skills.credential-access.skill-ethereum-wallet-read.skill-ethereum-wallet-read)\n - [https://cwe.mitre.org/data/definitions/522.html](https://cwe.mitre.org/data/definitions/522.html)\n - [https://owasp.org/Top10/2025/A06_2025-Insecure_Design/](https://owasp.org/Top10/2025/A06_2025-Insecure_Design/)\n - [https://owasp.org/Top10/A04_2021-Insecure_Design