s file access detected. Reading Google Cloud Platform credential files is a cloud credential theft technique."},"helpUri":"https://semgrep.dev/r/skills.credential-access.skill-gcp-credential-theft.skill-gcp-credentials-read","id":"skills.credential-access.skill-gcp-credential-theft.skill-gcp-credentials-read","name":"skills.credential-access.skill-gcp-credential-theft.skill-gcp-credentials-read","properties":{"precision":"very-high","tags":["CWE-522: Insufficiently Protected Credentials","HIGH CONFIDENCE","OWASP-A02:2017 - Broken Authentication","OWASP-A04:2021 - Insecure Design","OWASP-A06:2025 - Insecure Design","security"]},"shortDescription":{"text":"Semgrep Finding: skills.credential-access.skill-gcp-credential-theft.skill-gcp-credentials-read"}},{"defaultConfiguration":{"level":"warning"},"fullDescription":{"text":"Hardcoded API credential detected in a skill file. The credential is embedded directly in the skill instructions and is visible to any agent that loads this skill. If the skill is shared or published to a marketplace, this credential is exposed to all users. Use environment variables or a secrets manager instead of embedding credentials in skill files."},"help":{"markdown":"Hardcoded API credential detected in a skill file. The credential is embedded directly in the skill instructions and is visible to any agent that loads this skill. If the skill is shared or published to a marketplace, this credential is exposed to all users. Use environment variables or a secrets manager instead of embedding credentials in skill files.\n\n<b>References:</b>\n - [Semgrep Rule](https://semgrep.dev/r/skills.credential-access.skill-hardcoded-api-credential.skill-hardcoded-api-credential)\n - [https://attack.mitre.org/techniques/T1552/001/](https://attack.mitre.org/techniques/T1552/001/)\n - [https://cwe.mitre.org/data/definitions/798.html](https://cwe.mitre.org/data/definitions/798.html)\n - [https://owasp.org/Top10/2025/A07_2025-Authentication_Failures/](https://owasp.org/Top10/2025/A07_2025-Authentication_Failures/)\n - [https://owasp.org/Top10/A07_2021-Identification_and_Authentication_Failures](https://owasp.org/Top10/A07_2021-Identification_and_Authentication_Failures)\n","text":"Hardcoded API credential detected in a skill file. The credential is embedded directly in the skill instructions and is visible to any agent that loads this skill. If the skill is shared or published to a marketplace, this credential is exposed to all users. Use environment variables or a secrets manager instead of embedding credentials in skill files."},"helpUri":"https://semgrep.dev/r/skills.credential-access.skill-hardcoded-api-credential.skill-hardcoded-api-credential","id":"skills.credential-access.skill-hardcoded-api-credential.skill-hardcoded-api-credential","name":"skills.credential-access.skill-hardcoded-api-credential.skill-hardcoded-api-credential","properties":{"precision":"very-high","tags":["CWE-798: Use of Hard-coded Credentials","MEDIUM CONFIDENCE","OWASP-A07:2021 - Identification and Authentication Failures","OWASP-A07:2025 - Authentication Failures","security"]},"shortDescription":{"text":"Semgrep Finding: skills.credential-access.skill-hardcoded-api-credential.skill-hardcoded-api-credential"}},{"defaultConfiguration":{"level":"warning"},"fullDescription":{"text":"Hardware wallet device access detected. Accessing Ledger or Trezor wallet\nvia their SDK, device paths, or Ledger Live data enables cryptocurrency theft.\n\nIMPACT: Hardware wallet key extraction, cryptocurrency theft\n"},"help":{"markdown":"Hardware wallet device access detected. Accessing Ledger or Trezor wallet\nvia their SDK, device paths, or Ledger Live data enables cryptocurrency theft.\n\nIMPACT: Hardware wallet key extraction, cryptocurrency theft\n\n\n<b>References:</b>\n - [Semgrep Rule](https://semgrep.dev/r/skills.credential-access.skill-hardware-wallet-read.skill-hardware-wallet-read)\n - [https://attack.mitre.org/techniques/T1555/](https://attack.mitre.org/techniques/T1555/)\n - [https://owasp.org/Top10/2025/A06_2025-Insecure_Design/](https://owasp.org/Top10/2025/A06_2025-Insecure_Design/)\n - [https://owasp.org/Top10/A04_2021-Insecure_Design](https://owasp.org/Top10/A04_2021-Insecure_Design)\n - [https://owasp.org/Top10/A07_2021-Identification_and_Authentication_Failures](https://owasp.org/Top10/A07_2021-Identification_and_Authentication_Failures)\n","text":"Hardware wallet device access detected. Accessing Ledger or Trezor wallet\nvia their SDK, device paths, or Ledger Live data enables cryptocurrency theft.\n\nIMPACT: Hardware wallet key extraction, cryptocurrency theft\n"},"helpUri":"https://semgrep.dev/r/skills.credential-access.skill-hardware-wallet-read.skill-hardware-wallet-read","id":"skills.credential-access.skill-hardware-wallet-read.skill-hardware-wallet-read","name":"skills.credential-access.skill-hardware-wallet-read.skill-hardware-wallet-read","properties":{"precision":"very-high","tags":["CWE-522: Insufficiently Protected Credentials","MEDIUM CONFIDENCE","OWASP-A02:2017 - Broken Authentication","OWASP-A04:2021 - Insecure Design","OWASP-A06:2025 - Insecure Design","security"]},"shortDescription":{"text":"Semgrep Finding: skills.credential-access.skill-hardware-wallet-read.skill-hardware-wallet-read"}},{"defaultConfiguration":{"level":"warning"},"fullDescription":{"text":"macOS Keychain access detected via the security command. The `security`\nutility can extract passwords, certificates, and private keys from the\nsystem Keychain without a GUI dialog when the Keychain is already unlocked.\n\nAtomic macOS Stealer (AMOS) - the primary ClawHavoc payload - uses Keychain\naccess to steal credentials from 60+ cryptocurrency wallets, browsers\n(Chrome, Safari, Firefox), and applications.\n\nIMPACT: Mass credential theft from all Keychain-stored secrets\n"},"help":{"markdown":"macOS Keychain access detected via the security command. The `security`\nutility can extract passwords, certificates, and private keys from the\nsystem Keychain without a GUI dialog when the Keychain is already unlocked.\n\nAtomic macOS Stealer (AMOS) - the primary ClawHavoc payload - uses Keychain\naccess to steal credentials from 60+ cryptocurrency wallets, browsers\n(Chrome, Safari, Firefox), and applications.\n\nIMPACT: Mass credential theft from all Keychain-stored secrets\n\n\n<b>References:</b>\n - [Semgrep Rule](https://semgrep.dev/r/skills.credential-access.skill-macos-keychain-access.skill-macos-keychain-access)\n - [https://attack.mitre.org/techniques/T1555/001/](https://attack.mitre.org/techniques/T1555/001/)\n - [https://owasp.org/Top10/2025/A06_2025-Insecure_Design/](https://owasp.org/Top10/2025/A06_2025-Insecure_Design/)\n - [https://owasp.org/Top10/A04_2021-Insecure_Design](https://owasp.org/Top10/A04_2021-Insecure_Design)\n - [https://owasp.org/Top10/A07_2021-Identification_and_Authentication_Failures](https://owasp.org/Top10/A07_2021-Identification_and_Authentication_Failures)\n - [https://www.trendmicro.com/en_us/research/26/b/openclaw-skills-used-to-distribute-atomic-macos-stealer.html](https://www.trendmicro.com/en_us/research/26/b/openclaw-skills-used-to-distribute-atomic-macos-stealer.html)\n","text":"macOS Keychain access detected via the security command. The `security`\nutility can extract passwords, certificates, and private keys from the\nsystem Keychain without a GUI dialog when the Keychain is already unlocked.\n\nAtomic macOS Stealer (AMOS) - the primary ClawHavoc payload - uses Keychain\naccess to steal credentials from 60+ cryptocurrency wallets, browsers\n(Chrome, Safari, Firefox), and applications.\n\nIMPACT: Mass credential theft from all Keychain-stored secrets\n"},"helpUri":"https://semgrep.dev/r/skills.credential-access.skill-macos-keychain-access.skill-macos-keychain-access","id":"skills.credential-access.skill-macos-keychain-access.skill-macos-keychain-access","name":"skills.credential-access.skill-macos-keychain-access.skill-macos-keychain-access","propertie