. Hook commands run automatically with full user OS permissions on every tool event. Decoding and piping to a shell allows an attacker to hide arbitrary code from casual inspection.\n\n<b>References:</b>\n - [Semgrep Rule](https://semgrep.dev/r/skills.hooks.skill-hook-base64-obfuscated-command.skill-hook-base64-obfuscated-command)\n - [https://cwe.mitre.org/data/definitions/78.html](https://cwe.mitre.org/data/definitions/78.html)\n - [https://docs.anthropic.com/en/docs/claude-code/hooks](https://docs.anthropic.com/en/docs/claude-code/hooks)\n - [https://owasp.org/Top10/2025/A05_2025-Injection/](https://owasp.org/Top10/2025/A05_2025-Injection/)\n - [https://owasp.org/Top10/A03_2021-Injection](https://owasp.org/Top10/A03_2021-Injection)\n","text":"This hook configuration contains a base64-decode-pipe-to-shell pattern, a common obfuscation technique used to conceal malicious payloads. Hook commands run automatically with full user OS permissions on every tool event. Decoding and piping to a shell allows an attacker to hide arbitrary code from casual inspection."},"helpUri":"https://semgrep.dev/r/skills.hooks.skill-hook-base64-obfuscated-command.skill-hook-base64-obfuscated-command","id":"skills.hooks.skill-hook-base64-obfuscated-command.skill-hook-base64-obfuscated-command","name":"skills.hooks.skill-hook-base64-obfuscated-command.skill-hook-base64-obfuscated-command","properties":{"precision":"very-high","tags":["CWE-78: Improper Neutralization of Special Elements used in an OS Command ('OS Command Injection')","HIGH CONFIDENCE","OWASP-A01:2017 - Injection","OWASP-A03:2021 - Injection","OWASP-A05:2025 - Injection","security"]},"shortDescription":{"text":"Semgrep Finding: skills.hooks.skill-hook-base64-obfuscated-command.skill-hook-base64-obfuscated-command"}},{"defaultConfiguration":{"level":"error"},"fullDescription":{"text":"Hook matcher '$MATCHER' (type '$TYPE') runs '$COMMAND' which contains a bash reverse shell using /dev/tcp or /dev/udp. Hook commands execute au