ltration)\n - [https://cwe.mitre.org/data/definitions/200.html](https://cwe.mitre.org/data/definitions/200.html)\n - [https://docs.anthropic.com/en/docs/claude-code/hooks](https://docs.anthropic.com/en/docs/claude-code/hooks)\n - [https://owasp.org/Top10/2025/A01_2025-Broken_Access_Control/](https://owasp.org/Top10/2025/A01_2025-Broken_Access_Control/)\n - [https://owasp.org/Top10/A01_2021-Broken_Access_Control](https://owasp.org/Top10/A01_2021-Broken_Access_Control)\n","text":"Hook matcher '$MATCHER' (type '$TYPE') sends tool event data to raw public IP '$URL'. HTTP hooks POST tool event data (tool name, inputs, outputs) to the URL on every tool invocation. Pointing an HTTP hook at a raw IP is a strong indicator of data exfiltration — any developer who opens this project will silently stream their tool activity to an attacker-controlled server. Legitimate webhook endpoints use registered domain names, not raw IP addresses. Note: RFC-1918 private addresses and loopback are suppressed (local dev hooks)."},"helpUri":"https://semgrep.dev/r/skills.hooks.skill-hook-http-exfiltration.skill-hook-http-exfiltration","id":"skills.hooks.skill-hook-http-exfiltration.skill-hook-http-exfiltration","name":"skills.hooks.skill-hook-http-exfiltration.skill-hook-http-exfiltration","properties":{"precision":"very-high","tags":["CWE-200: Exposure of Sensitive Information to an Unauthorized Actor","MEDIUM CONFIDENCE","OWASP-A01:2021 - Broken Access Control","OWASP-A01:2025 - Broken Access Control","security"]},"shortDescription":{"text":"Semgrep Finding: skills.hooks.skill-hook-http-exfiltration.skill-hook-http-exfiltration"}},{"defaultConfiguration":{"level":"error"},"fullDescription":{"text":"Kiro lifecycle hook command '$COMMAND' contains a reverse shell or network backdoor. Lifecycle hooks run automatically with full user OS permissions on build, deploy, or save events. Any developer who clones this repository will have a persistent reverse shell connecting to an attacker-controlled host."},"help":{"markdown":"Kiro lifecycle hook command '$COMMAND' contains a reverse shell or network backdoor. Lifecycle hooks run automatically with full user OS permissions on build, deploy, or save events. Any developer who clones this repository will have a persistent reverse shell connecting to an attacker-controlled host.\n\n<b>References:</b>\n - [Semgrep Rule](https://semgrep.dev/r/skills.hooks.skill-hook-kiro-lifecycle-malicious-command.skill-hook-kiro-lifecycle-malicious-command)\n - [https://cwe.mitre.org/data/definitions/78.html](https://cwe.mitre.org/data/definitions/78.html)\n - [https://docs.anthropic.com/en/docs/claude-code/hooks](https://docs.anthropic.com/en/docs/claude-code/hooks)\n - [https://owasp.org/Top10/2025/A05_2025-Injection/](https://owasp.org/Top10/2025/A05_2025-Injection/)\n - [https://owasp.org/Top10/A03_2021-Injection](https://owasp.org/Top10/A03_2021-Injection)\n","text":"Kiro lifecycle hook command '$COMMAND' contains a reverse shell or network backdoor. Lifecycle hooks run automatically with full user OS permissions on build, deploy, or save events. Any developer who clones this repository will have a persistent reverse shell connecting to an attacker-controlled host."},"helpUri":"https://semgrep.dev/r/skills.hooks.skill-hook-kiro-lifecycle-malicious-command.skill-hook-kiro-lifecycle-malicious-command","id":"skills.hooks.skill-hook-kiro-lifecycle-malicious-command.skill-hook-kiro-lifecycle-malicious-command","name":"skills.hooks.skill-hook-kiro-lifecycle-malicious-command.skill-hook-kiro-lifecycle-malicious-command","properties":{"precision":"very-high","tags":["CWE-78: Improper Neutralization of Special Elements used in an OS Command ('OS Command Injection')","HIGH CONFIDENCE","OWASP-A01:2017 - Injection","OWASP-A03:2021 - Injection","OWASP-A05:2025 - Injection","security"]},"shortDescription":{"text":"Semgrep Finding: skills.hooks.skill-hook-kiro-lifecycle-malicious-command.skill-hook-kiro-lifecycle-malicious-command"}},{"defau