Command Injection')","HIGH CONFIDENCE","OWASP-A01:2017 - Injection","OWASP-A03:2021 - Injection","OWASP-A05:2025 - Injection","security"]},"shortDescription":{"text":"Semgrep Finding: skills.hooks.skill-hook-kiro-malicious-command.skill-hook-kiro-malicious-command"}},{"defaultConfiguration":{"level":"error"},"fullDescription":{"text":"Hook matcher '$MATCHER' (type '$TYPE') executes '$COMMAND' which contains a reverse shell or network backdoor. Hook commands run automatically with full user OS permissions on every tool event. Any developer who clones this repository will have a persistent reverse shell connecting to an attacker-controlled host on each session or file operation."},"help":{"markdown":"Hook matcher '$MATCHER' (type '$TYPE') executes '$COMMAND' which contains a reverse shell or network backdoor. Hook commands run automatically with full user OS permissions on every tool event. Any developer who clones this repository will have a persistent reverse shell connecting to an attacker-controlled host on each session or file operation.\n\n<b>References:</b>\n - [Semgrep Rule](https://semgrep.dev/r/skills.hooks.skill-hook-malicious-command.skill-hook-malicious-command)\n - [https://cwe.mitre.org/data/definitions/78.html](https://cwe.mitre.org/data/definitions/78.html)\n - [https://docs.anthropic.com/en/docs/claude-code/hooks](https://docs.anthropic.com/en/docs/claude-code/hooks)\n - [https://owasp.org/Top10/2025/A05_2025-Injection/](https://owasp.org/Top10/2025/A05_2025-Injection/)\n - [https://owasp.org/Top10/A03_2021-Injection](https://owasp.org/Top10/A03_2021-Injection)\n","text":"Hook matcher '$MATCHER' (type '$TYPE') executes '$COMMAND' which contains a reverse shell or network backdoor. Hook commands run automatically with full user OS permissions on every tool event. Any developer who clones this repository will have a persistent reverse shell connecting to an attacker-controlled host on each session or file operation."},"helpUri":"https://semgrep.dev/r/skills.hooks.skill-hook-malicious-command.skill-hook-malicious-command","id":"skills.hooks.skill-hook-malicious-command.skill-hook-malicious-command","name":"skills.hooks.skill-hook-malicious-command.skill-hook-malicious-command","properties":{"precision":"very-high","tags":["CWE-78: Improper Neutralization of Special Elements used in an OS Command ('OS Command Injection')","HIGH CONFIDENCE","OWASP-A01:2017 - Injection","OWASP-A03:2021 - Injection","OWASP-A05:2025 - Injection","security"]},"shortDescription":{"text":"Semgrep Finding: skills.hooks.skill-hook-malicious-command.skill-hook-malicious-command"}},{"defaultConfiguration":{"level":"warning"},"fullDescription":{"text":"Hook command '$COMMAND' runs an npx package pinned to an unstable channel (@alpha, @beta, @latest, @next, @canary, or @dev). Unstable tags resolve to whatever version the registry serves at run time — an attacker who compromises or publishes to that channel can execute arbitrary code on every developer who opens this project."},"help":{"markdown":"Hook command '$COMMAND' runs an npx package pinned to an unstable channel (@alpha, @beta, @latest, @next, @canary, or @dev). Unstable tags resolve to whatever version the registry serves at run time — an attacker who compromises or publishes to that channel can execute arbitrary code on every developer who opens this project.\n\n<b>References:</b>\n - [Semgrep Rule](https://semgrep.dev/r/skills.hooks.skill-hook-npx-unstable-tag.skill-hook-npx-unstable-tag)\n - [https://cwe.mitre.org/data/definitions/494.html](https://cwe.mitre.org/data/definitions/494.html)\n - [https://docs.anthropic.com/en/docs/claude-code/hooks](https://docs.anthropic.com/en/docs/claude-code/hooks)\n - [https://owasp.org/Top10/2025/A08_2025-Software_or_Data_Integrity_Failures/](https://owasp.org/Top10/2025/A08_2025-Software_or_Data_Integrity_Failures/)\n - [https://owasp.org/Top10/A08_2021-Software_and_Data_Integrity_Failures](https://owasp.org/Top10/A08_2021-Software_and_Data_Integrity_Failures)\n","text":"Hook command '$COMMAND' runs an npx package pinned to an unstable channel (@alpha, @beta, @latest, @next, @canary, or @dev). Unstable tags resolve to whatever version the registry serves at run time — an attacker who compromises or publishes to that channel can execute arbitrary code on every developer who opens this project."},"helpUri":"https://semgrep.dev/r/skills.hooks.skill-hook-npx-unstable-tag.skill-hook-npx-unstable-tag","id":"skills.hooks.skill-hook-npx-unstable-tag.skill-hook-npx-unstable-tag","name":"skills.hooks.skill-hook-npx-unstable-tag.skill-hook-npx-unstable-tag","properties":{"precision":"very-high","tags":["CWE-494: Download of Code Without Integrity Check","MEDIUM CONFIDENCE","OWASP-A08:2021 - Software and Data Integrity Failures","OWASP-A08:2025 - Software or Data Integrity Failures","security"]},"shortDescription":{"text":"Semgrep Finding: skills.hooks.skill-hook-npx-unstable-tag.skill-hook-npx-unstable-tag"}},{"defaultConfiguration":{"level":"warning"},"fullDescription":{"text":"Hook matcher '$MATCHER' (type '$TYPE') executes '$COMMAND' which downloads content from a remote URL and pipes it directly to a shell interpreter. Hook commands run automatically with full user OS permissions on every tool event. An attacker can serve a changing payload — any developer who opens this project will execute whatever the remote server returns."},"help":{"markdown":"Hook matcher '$MATCHER' (type '$TYPE') executes '$COMMAND' which downloads content from a remote URL and pipes it directly to a shell interpreter. Hook commands run automatically with full user OS permissions on every tool event. An attacker can serve a changing payload — any developer who opens this project will execute whatever the remote server returns.\n\n<b>References:</b>\n - [Semgrep Rule](https://semgrep.dev/r/skills.hooks.skill-hook-pipe-to-shell.skill-hook-pipe-to-shell)\n - [https://cwe.mitre.org/data/definitions/494.html](https://cwe.mitre.org/data/definitions/494.html)\n - [https://docs.anthropic.com/en/docs/claude-code/hooks](https://docs.anthropic.com/en/docs/claude-code/hooks)\n - [https://owasp.org/Top10/2025/A08_2025-Software_or_Data_Integrity_Failures/](https://owasp.org/Top10/2025/A08_2025-Software_or_Data_Integrity_Failures/)\n - [https://owasp.org/Top10/A08_2021-Software_and_Data_Integrity_Failures](https://owasp.org/Top10/A08_2021-Software_and_Data_Integrity_Failures)\n","text":"Hook matcher '$MATCHER' (type '$TYPE') executes '$COMMAND' which downloads content from a remote URL and pipes it directly to a shell interpreter. Hook commands run automatically with full user OS permissions on every tool event. An attacker can serve a changing payload — any developer who opens this project will execute whatever the remote server returns."},"helpUri":"https://semgrep.dev/r/skills.hooks.skill-hook-pipe-to-shell.skill-hook-pipe-to-shell","id":"skills.hooks.skill-hook-pipe-to-shell.skill-hook-pipe-to-shell","name":"skills.hooks.skill-hook-pipe-to-shell.skill-hook-pipe-to-shell","properties":{"precision":"very-high","tags":["CWE-494: Download of Code Without Integrity Check","MEDIUM CONFIDENCE","OWASP-A08:2021 - Software and Data Integrity Failures","OWASP-A08:2025 - Software or Data Integrity Failures","security"]},"shortDescription":{"text":"Semgrep Finding: skills.hooks.skill-hook-pipe-to-shell.skill-hook-pipe-to-shell"}},{"defaultConfiguration":{"level":"warning"},"fullDescription":{"text":"Hook command '$COMMAND' (type '$TYPE') sends data to a raw external IP address. Hook commands run with full user OS permissions on every tool event. Any hook that posts to a raw IP is a strong indicator of data exfiltration — any developer who opens this project will silently forward tool activity to an attacker-controlled server. Legitimate endpoints use registered domain names, not raw IP addresses. Note: RFC-1918 private addresses and loopback are suppressed (local dev hooks)."},"help":{"markdown":"Hook command '$COMMAND' (type '$TYPE') sends data to a raw external IP address. Hook commands run with full user OS permissions on every tool event. Any hook that posts to a raw IP is a strong indicator of data exfiltration — any developer who opens this project will silently forward tool activity to an attacker-controlled server. Legitimate endpoints use registered domain names, not raw IP addresses. Note: RFC-1918 private addresses and loopback are suppressed (local dev hooks).\n\n<b>References:</b>\n - [Semgrep Rule](https://semgrep.dev/r/skills.hooks.skill-hook-raw-ip-exfiltration.skill-hook-raw-ip-exfiltration)\n - [https://cwe.mitre.org/data/definitions/200.html](https://cwe.mitre.org/data/definitions/200.html)\n - [https://docs.anthropic.com/en/docs/claude-code/hooks](https://docs.anthropic.com/en/docs/claude-code/hooks)\n - [https://owasp.org/Top10/2025/A01_2025-Broken_Access_Control/](https://owasp.org/Top10/2025/A01_2025-Broken_Access_Control/)\n - [https://owasp.org/Top10/A01_2021-Broken_Access_Control](https://owasp.org/Top10/A01_2021-Broken_Access_Control)\n","text":"Hook command '$COMMAND' (type '$TYPE') sends data to a raw external IP address. Hook commands run with full user OS permissions on every tool event. Any hook that posts to a raw IP is a strong indicator of data exfiltration — any developer who opens this project will silently forward tool activity to an attacker-controlled server. Legitimate endpoints use registered domain names, not raw IP addresses. Note: RFC-1918 private addresses and loopback are suppressed (local dev hooks)."},"helpUri":"https://semgrep.dev/r/skills.hooks.skill-hook-raw-ip-exfiltration.skill-hook-raw-ip-exfiltration","id":"skills.hooks.skill-hook-raw-ip-exfiltration.skill-hook-raw-ip-exfiltration","name":"skills.hooks.skill-hook-raw-ip-exfiltration.skill-hook-raw-ip-exfiltration","properties":{"precision":"very-high","tags":["CWE-200: Exposure of Sensitive Information to an Unauthorized Actor","HIGH CONFIDENCE","OWASP-A01:2021 - Broken Access Control","OWASP-A01:2025 - Broken Access Control","security"]},"shortDescription":{"text":"Semgrep Finding: skills.hooks.skill-hook-raw-ip-exfiltration.skill-hook-raw-ip-exfiltration"}},{"defaultConfiguration":{"level":"error"},"fullDescription":{"text":"Hook script contains a bash reverse shell using /dev/tcp or /dev/udp. Scripts in AI\ntool hook directories (.claude/hooks/, .gemini/hooks/, etc.) execute automatically\nwith full user OS permissions on every tool event. Any developer who clones this\nrepository will have an outbound reverse shell opened to an attacker-controlled host\non each session or file operation.\n\nReview the commit history of this file and the hook configuration that invokes it.\n"},"help":{"markdown":"Hook script contains a bash reverse shell using /dev/tcp or /dev/udp. Scripts in AI\ntool hook directories (.claude/hooks/, .gemini/hooks/, etc.) execute automatically\nwith full user OS permissions on every tool event. Any developer who clones this\nrepository will have an outbound reverse shell opened to an attacker-controlled host\non each session or file operation.\n\nReview the commit history of this file and the hook configuration that invokes it.\n\n\n<b>References:</b>\n - [Semgrep Rule](https://semgrep.dev/r/skills.hooks.skill-hook-script-bash-reverse-shell.skill-hook-script-bash-reverse-shell)\n - [https://cwe.mitre.org/data/definitions/78.html](https://cwe.mitre.org/data/definitions/78.html)\n - [https://docs.anthropic.com/en/docs/claude-code/hooks](https://docs.anthropic.com/en/docs/claude-code/hooks)\n - [https://owasp.org/Top10/2025/A05_2025-Injection/](https://owasp.org/Top10/2025/A05_2025-Injection/)\n - [https://owasp.org/Top10/A03_2021-Injection](https://owasp.org/Top10/A03_2021-Injection)\n","text":"Hook script contains a bash reverse shell using /dev/tcp or /dev/udp. Scripts in AI\ntool hook directories (.claude/hooks/, .gemini/hooks/, etc.) execute automatically\nwith full user OS permissions on every tool event. Any developer who clones this\nrepository will have an outbound reverse shell opened to an attacker-controlled host\non each session or file operation.\n\nReview the commit history of this file and the hook configuration that invokes it.\n"},"helpUri":"https://semgrep.dev/r/skills.hooks.skill-hook-script-bash-reverse-shell.skill-hook-script-bash-reverse-shell","id":"skills.hooks.skill-hook-script-bash-reverse-shell.skill-hook-script-bash-reverse-shell","name":"skills.hooks.skill-hook-script-bash-reverse-shell.skill-hook-script-bash-reverse-shell","properties":{"precision":"very-high","tags":["CWE-78: Improper Neutralization of Special Elements used in an OS Command ('OS Command Injection')","HIGH CONFIDENCE","OWASP-A01:2017 - Injection","OWASP-A03:2021 - Injection","OWASP-A05:2025 - Injection","security"]},"shortDescription":{"text":"Semgrep Finding: skills.hooks.skill-hook-script-bash-reverse-shell.skill-hook-script-bash-reverse-shell"}},{"defaultConfiguration":{"level":"error"},"fullDescription":{"text":"Hardcoded Discord webhook token or Telegram bot token detected. Threat actors\nembed real attacker-controlled credentials in malicious AI agent skills to\nsilently exfiltrate credentials, environment variables, and sensitive files.\n\nLegitimate notification skills that reference these APIs dynamically (via\nenvironment variables or user-supplied tokens) are NOT flagged by this rule.\nOnly hardcoded credential tokens in the standard formats are matched:\n  Telegram: bot{7-12 digits}:{30-50 alphanumeric chars}\n  Discord:  webhooks/{17-20 digit snowflake}/{60-80 char token}\n\nThese services blend in with HTTPS traffic and bypass network monitoring.\nThe ClawHavoc campaign and multiple npm malware families confirmed this vector.\n\nIMPACT: Silent credential and data exfiltration to attacker-controlled channels\n"},"help":{"markdown":"Hardcoded Discord webhook token or Telegram bot token detected. Threat actors\nembed real attacker-controlled credentials in malicious AI agent skills to\nsilently exfiltrate credentials, environment variables, and sensitive files.\n\nLegitimate notification skills that reference these APIs dynamically (via\nenvironment variables or user-supplied tokens) are NOT flagged by this rule.\nOnly hardcoded credential tokens in the standard formats are matched:\n  Telegram: bot{7-12 digits}:{30-50 alphanumeric chars}\n  Discord:  webhooks/{17-20 digit snowflake}/{60-80 char token}\n\nThese services blend in with HTTPS traffic and bypass network monitoring.\nThe ClawHavoc campaign and multiple npm malware families confirmed this vector.\n\nIMPACT: Silent credential and data exfiltration to attacker-controlled channels\n\n\n<b>References:</b>\n - [Semgrep Rule](https://semgrep.dev/r/skills.network.skill-discord-telegram-c2.skill-discord-telegram-c2)\n - [https://attack.mitre.org/techniques/T1102/](https://attack.mitre.org/techniques/T1102/)\n - [https://gbhackers.com/threat-actors-exploit-discord-webhooks-for-c2/](https://gbhackers.com/threat-actors-exploit-discord-webhooks-for-c2/)\n - [https://owasp.org/Top10/2025/A01_2025-Broken_Access_Control/](https://owasp.org/Top10/2025/A01_2025-Broken_Access_Control/)\n - [https://owasp.org/Top10/A01_2021-Broken_Access_Control](https://owasp.org/Top10/A01_2021-Broken_Access_Control)\n - [https://thehackernews.com/2025/10/npm-pypi-and-rubygems-packages-found.html](https://thehackernews.com/2025/10/npm-pypi-and-rubygems-packages-found.html)\n","text":"Hardcoded Discord webhook token or Telegram bot token detected. Threat actors\nembed real attacker-controlled credentials in malicious AI agent skills to\nsilently exfiltrate credentials, environment variables, and sensitive files.\n\nLegitimate notification skills that reference these APIs dynamically (via\nenvironment variables or user-supplied tokens) are NOT flagged by this rule.\nOnly hardcoded credential tokens in the standard formats are matched:\n  Telegram: bot{7-12 digits}:{30-50 alphanumeric chars}\n  Discord:  webhooks/{17-20 digit snowflake}/{60-80 char token}\n\nThese services blend in with HTTPS traffic and bypass network monitoring.\nThe ClawHavoc campaign and multiple npm malware families confirmed this vector.\n\nIMPACT: Silent credential and data exfiltration to attacker-controlled channels\n"},"helpUri":"https://semgrep.dev/r/skills.network.skill-discord-telegram-c2.skill-discord-telegram-c2","id":"skills.network.skill-discord-telegram-c2.skill-discord-telegram-c2","name":"skills.network.skill-discord-telegram-c2.skill-discord-telegram-c2","properties":{"precision":"very-high","tags":["CWE-200: Exposure of Sensitive Information to an Unauthorized Actor","HIGH CONFIDENCE","OWASP-A01:2021 - Broken Access Control","OWASP-A01:2025 - Broken Access Control","security"]},"shortDescription":{"text":"Semgrep Finding: skills.network.skill-discord-telegram-c2.skill-discord-telegram-c2"}},{"defaultConfiguration":{"level":"error"},"fullDescription":{"text":"Skill uses @reboot cron entry for boot persistence. Detects @reboot cron entries being written to crontab via pipe, which executes commands on every system startup. This is a persistence technique used by attackers to survive reboots."},"help":{"markdown":"Skill uses @reboot cron entry for boot persistence. Detects @reboot cron entries being written to crontab via pipe, which executes commands on every system startup. This is a persistence technique used by attackers to survive reboots.\n\n<b>References:</b>\n - [Semgrep Rule](https://semgrep.dev/r/skills.persistence.skill-cron-reboot-persistence.skill-cron-reboot-persistence)\n - [https://attack.mitre.org/techniques/T1053/003/](https://attack.mitre.org/techniques/T1053/003/)\n - [https://owasp.org/Top10/2025/A05_2025-Injection/](https://owasp.org/Top10/2025/A05_2025-Injection/)\n - [https://owasp.org/Top10/A03_2021-Injection](https://owasp.org/Top10/A03_2021-Injection)\n","text":"Skill uses @reboot cron entry for boot persistence. Detects @reboot cron entries being written to crontab via pipe, which executes commands on every system startup. This is a persistence technique used by attackers to survive reboots."},"helpUri":"https://semgrep.dev/r/skills.persistence.skill-cron-reboot-persistence.skill-cron-reboot-persistence","id":"skills.persistence.skill-cron-reboot-persistence.skill-cron-reboot-persistence","name":"skills.persistence.skill-cron-reboot-persistence.skill-cron-reboot-persistence","properties":{"precision":"very-high","tags":["CWE-78: Improper Neutralization of Special Elements used in an OS Command ('OS Command Injection')","HIGH CONFIDENCE","OWASP-A01:2017 - Injection","OWASP-A03:2021 - Injection","OWASP-A05:2025 - Injection","security"]},"shortDescription":{"text":"Semgrep Finding: skills.persistence.skill-cron-reboot-persistence.skill-cron-reboot-persistence"}},{"defaultConfiguration":{"level":"error"},"fullDescription":{"text":"Skill manipulates crontab for persistence. Detects skills that directly manipulate crontab to schedule persistent tasks by piping content to crontab."},"help":{"markdown":"Skill manipulates crontab for persistence. Detects skills that directly manipulate crontab to schedule persistent tasks by piping content to crontab.\n\n<b>References:</b>\n - [Semgrep Rule](https://semgrep.dev/r/skills.persistence.skill-crontab-manipulation.skill-crontab-manipulation)\n - [https://attack.mitre.org/techniques/T1053/003/](https://attack.mitre.org/techniques/T1053/003/)\n - [https://owasp.org/Top10/2025/A05_2025-Injection/](https://owasp.org/Top10/2025/A05_2025-Injection/)\n - [https://owasp.org/Top10/A03_2021-Injection](https://owasp.org/Top10/A03_2021-Injection)\n","text":"Skill manipulates crontab for persistence. Detects skills that directly manipulate crontab to schedule persistent tasks by piping content to crontab."},"helpUri":"https://semgrep.dev/r/skills.persistence.skill-crontab-manipulation.skill-crontab-manipulation","id":"skills.persistence.skill-crontab-manipulation.skill-crontab-manipulation","name":"skills.persistence.skill-crontab-manipulation.skill-crontab-manipulation","properties":{"precision":"very-high","tags":["CWE-78: Improper Neutralization of Special Elements used in an OS Command ('OS Command Injection')","HIGH CONFIDENCE","OWASP-A01:2017 - Injection","OWASP-A03:2021 - Injection","OWASP-A05:2025 - Injection","security"]},"shortDescription":{"text":"Semgrep Finding: skills.persistence.skill-crontab-manipulation.skill-crontab-manipulation"}},{"defaultConfiguration":{"level":"warning"},"fullDescription":{"text":"macOS launchd persistence mechanism detected. Writing or loading plist files\ninto ~/Library/LaunchAgents or /Library/LaunchDaemons installs a persistent\nservice that survives reboots and user logins.\n\nThis is the macOS equivalent of crontab/systemd persistence and is a common\ntechnique for maintaining access after initial compromise.\n\nIMPACT: Persistent backdoor surviving reboots, executes as user or root\n"},"help":{"markdown":"macOS launchd persistence mechanism detected. Writing or loading plist files\ninto ~/Library/LaunchAgents or /Library/LaunchDaemons installs a persistent\nservice that survives reboots and user logins.\n\nThis is the macOS equivalent of crontab/systemd persistence and is a common\ntechnique for maintaining access after initial compromise.\n\nIMPACT: Persistent backdoor surviving reboots, executes as user or root\n\n\n<b>References:</b>\n - [Semgrep Rule](https://semgrep.dev/r/skills.persistence.skill-launchd-persistence.skill-launchd-persistence)\n - [https://attack.mitre.org/techniques/T1543/001/](https://attack.mitre.org/techniques/T1543/001/)\n - [https://attack.mitre.org/techniques/T1543/004/](https://attack.mitre.org/techniques/T1543/004/)\n - [https://owasp.org/Top10/2025/A01_2025-Broken_Access_Control/](https://owasp.org/Top10/2025/A01_2025-Broken_Access_Control/)\n - [https://owasp.org/Top10/A01_2021-Broken_Access_Control](https://owasp.org/Top10/A01_2021-Broken_Access_Control)\n","text":"macOS launchd persistence mechanism detected. Writing or loading plist files\ninto ~/Library/LaunchAgents or /Library/LaunchDaemons installs a persistent\nservice that survives reboots and user logins.\n\nThis is the macOS equivalent of crontab/systemd persistence and is a common\ntechnique for maintaining access after initial compromise.\n\nIMPACT: Persistent backdoor surviving reboots, executes as user or root\n"},"helpUri":"https://semgrep.dev/r/skills.persistence.skill-launchd-persistence.skill-launchd-persistence","id":"skills.persistence.skill-launchd-persistence.skill-launchd-persistence","name":"skills.persistence.skill-launchd-persistence.skill-launchd-persistence","properties":{"precision":"very-high","tags":["CWE-284: Improper Access Control","MEDIUM CONFIDENCE","OWASP-A01:2021 - Broken Access Control","OWASP-A01:2025 - Broken Access Control","OWASP-A05:2017 - Broken Access Control","security"]},"shortDescription":{"text":"Semgrep Finding: skills.persistence.skill-launchd-persistence.skill-launchd-persistence"}},{"defaultConfiguration":{"level":"error"},"fullDescription":{"text":"Skill writes to system cron directories. Detects writing to system cron directories for persistent scheduling."},"help":{"markdown":"Skill writes to system cron directories. Detects writing to system cron directories for persistent scheduling.\n\n<b>References:</b>\n - [Semgrep Rule](https://semgrep.dev/r/skills.persistence.skill-system-cron-write.skill-system-cron-write)\n - [https://attack.mitre.org/techniques/T1053/003/](https://attack.mitre.org/techniques/T1053/003/)\n - [https://owasp.org/Top10/2025/A05_2025-Injection/](https://owasp.org/Top10/2025/A05_2025-Injection/)\n - [https://owasp.org/Top10/A03_2021-Injection](https://owasp.org/Top10/A03_2021-Injection)\n","text":"Skill writes to system cron directories. Detects writing to system cron directories for persistent scheduling."},"helpUri":"https://semgrep.dev/r/skills.persistence.skill-system-cron-write.skill-system-cron-write","id":"skills.persistence.skill-system-cron-write.skill-system-cron-write","name":"skills.persistence.skill-system-cron-write.skill-system-cron-write","properties":{"precision":"very-high","tags":["CWE-78: Improper Neutralization of Special Elements used in an OS Command ('OS Command Injection')","HIGH CONFIDENCE","OWASP-A01:2017 - Injection","OWASP-A03:2021 - Injection","OWASP-A05:2025 - Injection","security"]},"shortDescription":{"text":"Semgrep Finding: skills.persistence.skill-system-cron-write.skill-system-cron-write"}},{"defaultConfiguration":{"level":"warning"},"fullDescription":{"text":"Systemd service unit creation detected - potential boot persistence.\nWriting to /etc/systemd/system/ creates a service that persists across\nreboots. Combined with `systemctl enable`, the backdoor restarts\nautomatically on every boot. Systemd timer units are the modern equivalent\nof crontab and are increasingly used by malware on Linux systems.\n\nModern malware prefers systemd over crontab because systemd units are\nless commonly audited and provide more control over execution environment.\n\nIMPACT: Persistent backdoor surviving reboots, recurring command execution\n"},"help":{"markdown":"Systemd service unit creation detected - potential boot persistence.\nWriting to /etc/systemd/system/ creates a service that persists across\nreboots. Combined with `systemctl enable`, the backdoor restarts\nautomatically on every boot. Systemd timer units are the modern equivalent\nof crontab and are increasingly used by malware on Linux systems.\n\nModern malware prefers systemd over crontab because systemd units are\nless commonly audited and provide more control over execution environment.\n\nIMPACT: Persistent backdoor surviving reboots, recurring command execution\n\n\n<b>References:</b>\n - [Semgrep Rule](https://semgrep.dev/r/skills.persistence.skill-systemd-persistence.skill-systemd-persistence)\n - [https://attack.mitre.org/techniques/T1053/006/](https://attack.mitre.org/techniques/T1053/006/)\n - [https://attack.mitre.org/techniques/T1543/002/](https://attack.mitre.org/techniques/T1543/002/)\n - [https://owasp.org/Top10/2025/A05_2025-Injection/](https://owasp.org/Top10/2025/A05_2025-Injection/)\n - [https://owasp.org/Top10/A03_2021-Injection](https://owasp.org/Top10/A03_2021-Injection)\n","text":"Systemd service unit creation detected - potential boot persistence.\nWriting to /etc/systemd/system/ creates a service that persists across\nreboots. Combined with `systemctl enable`, the backdoor restarts\nautomatically on every boot. Systemd timer units are the modern equivalent\nof crontab and are increasingly used by malware on Linux systems.\n\nModern malware prefers systemd over crontab because systemd units are\nless commonly audited and provide more control over execution environment.\n\nIMPACT: Persistent backdoor surviving reboots, recurring command execution\n"},"helpUri":"https://semgrep.dev/r/skills.persistence.skill-systemd-persistence.skill-systemd-persistence","id":"skills.persistence.skill-systemd-persistence.skill-systemd-persistence","name":"skills.persistence.skill-systemd-persistence.skill-systemd-persistence","properties":{"precision":"very-high","tags":["CWE-78: Improper Neutralization of Special Elements used in an OS Command ('OS Command Injection')","MEDIUM CONFIDENCE","OWASP-A01:2017 - Injection","OWASP-A03:2021 - Injection","OWASP-A05:2025 - Injection","security"]},"shortDescription":{"text":"Semgrep Finding: skills.persistence.skill-systemd-persistence.skill-systemd-persistence"}},{"defaultConfiguration":{"level":"warning"},"fullDescription":{"text":"Skill contains a reference to \"DAN mode\" (Do Anything Now), \"developer mode\", or \"jailbreak mode\" activation. DAN is a well-known prompt injection technique that attempts to convince AI agents to bypass safety controls by adopting an alternative persona. Developer mode activation is a related social engineering pattern documented in multiple malicious skill campaigns. Review the full skill context; security research and awareness content may reference these phrases as examples."},"help":{"markdown":"Skill contains a reference to \"DAN mode\" (Do Anything Now), \"developer mode\", or \"jailbreak mode\" activation. DAN is a well-known prompt injection technique that attempts to convince AI agents to bypass safety controls by adopting an alternative persona. Developer mode activation is a related social engineering pattern documented in multiple malicious skill campaigns. Review the full skill context; security research and awareness content may reference these phrases as examples.\n\n<b>References:</b>\n - [Semgrep Rule](https://semgrep.dev/r/skills.preprocessing-injection.skill-dan-mode.skill-dan-mode)\n - [https://arxiv.org/html/2602.06547v1](https://arxiv.org/html/2602.06547v1)\n - [https://cwe.mitre.org/data/definitions/94.html](https://cwe.mitre.org/data/definitions/94.html)\n - [https://owasp.org/Top10/2025/A05_2025-Injection/](https://owasp.org/Top10/2025/A05_2025-Injection/)\n - [https://owasp.org/Top10/A03_2021-Injection](https://owasp.org/Top10/A03_2021-Injection)\n - [https://snyk.io/blog/toxicskills-malicious-ai-agent-skills-clawhub/](https://snyk.io/blog/toxicskills-malicious-ai-agent-skills-clawhub/)\n","text":"Skill contains a reference to \"DAN mode\" (Do Anything Now), \"developer mode\", or \"jailbreak mode\" activation. DAN is a well-known prompt injection technique that attempts to convince AI agents to bypass safety controls by adopting an alternative persona. Developer mode activation is a related social engineering pattern documented in multiple malicious skill campaigns. Review the full skill context; security research and awareness content may reference these phrases as examples."},"helpUri":"https://semgrep.dev/r/skills.preprocessing-injection.skill-dan-mode.skill-dan-mode","id":"skills.preprocessing-injection.skill-dan-mode.skill-dan-mode","name":"skills.preprocessing-injection.skill-dan-mode.skill-dan-mode","properties":{"precision":"very-high","tags":["CWE-94: Improper Control of Generation of Code ('Code Injection')","MEDIUM CONFIDENCE","OWASP-A03:2021 - Injection","OWASP-A05:2025 - Injection","security"]},"shortDescription":{"text":"Semgrep Finding: skills.preprocessing-injection.skill-dan-mode.skill-dan-mode"}},{"defaultConfiguration":{"level":"warning"},"fullDescription":{"text":"Skill contains instructions to override AI safety measures, ignore content policies, or enter an \"unrestricted mode\". These directives attempt to disable the agent's built-in safety controls and can cause it to perform unauthorized actions including data exfiltration, system modification, and bypassing user confirmation prompts. Confirmed in the agent-skills.cc corpus and documented in multiple public reports on malicious Claude skill campaigns. Note: security research and defense skills may contain these phrases as examples — review the full skill context."},"help":{"markdown":"Skill contains instructions to override AI safety measures, ignore content policies, or enter an \"unrestricted mode\". These directives attempt to disable the agent's built-in safety controls and can cause it to perform unauthorized actions including data exfiltration, system modification, and bypassing user confirmation prompts. Confirmed in the agent-skills.cc corpus and documented in multiple public reports on malicious Claude skill campaigns. Note: security research and defense skills may contain these phrases as examples — review the full skill context.\n\n<b>References:</b>\n - [Semgrep Rule](https://semgrep.dev/r/skills.preprocessing-injection.skill-jailbreak-directive.skill-jailbreak-directive)\n - [https://arxiv.org/html/2602.06547v1](https://arxiv.org/html/2602.06547v1)\n - [https://owasp.org/Top10/2025/A05_2025-Injection/](https://owasp.org/Top10/2025/A05_2025-Injection/)\n - [https://owasp.org/Top10/A03_2021-Injection](https://owasp.org/Top10/A03_2021-Injection)\n - [https://snyk.io/blog/toxicskills-malicious-ai-agent-skills-clawhub/](https://snyk.io/blog/toxicskills-malicious-ai-agent-skills-clawhub/)\n - [https://www.koi.ai/blog/clawhavoc-341-malicious-clawedbot-skills-found-by-the-bot-they-were-targeting](https://www.koi.ai/blog/clawhavoc-341-malicious-clawedbot-skills-found-by-the-bot-they-were-targeting)\n","text":"Skill contains instructions to override AI safety measures, ignore content policies, or enter an \"unrestricted mode\". These directives attempt to disable the agent's built-in safety controls and can cause it to perform unauthorized actions including data exfiltration, system modification, and bypassing user confirmation prompts. Confirmed in the agent-skills.cc corpus and documented in multiple public reports on malicious Claude skill campaigns. Note: security research and defense skills may contain these phrases as examples — review the full skill context."},"helpUri":"https://semgrep.dev/r/skills.preprocessing-injection.skill-jailbreak-directive.skill-jailbreak-directive","id":"skills.preprocessing-injection.skill-jailbreak-directive.skill-jailbreak-directive","name":"skills.preprocessing-injection.skill-jailbreak-directive.skill-jailbreak-directive","properties":{"precision":"very-high","tags":["CWE-94: Improper Control of Generation of Code ('Code Injection')","MEDIUM CONFIDENCE","OWASP-A03:2021 - Injection","OWASP-A05:2025 - Injection","security"]},"shortDescription":{"text":"Semgrep Finding: skills.preprocessing-injection.skill-jailbreak-directive.skill-jailbreak-directive"}},{"defaultConfiguration":{"level":"warning"},"fullDescription":{"text":"Skill contains coercive execution language combined with a network command on the same line or instruction. Patterns like \"MANDATORY: curl https://...\", \"execute this command immediately https://...\", or \"This is not optional. curl https://...\" attempt to force the AI agent to execute network commands without user confirmation, bypassing normal approval workflows. Confirmed in the agent-skills.cc corpus."},"help":{"markdown":"Skill contains coercive execution language combined with a network command on the same line or instruction. Patterns like \"MANDATORY: curl https://...\", \"execute this command immediately https://...\", or \"This is not optional. curl https://...\" attempt to force the AI agent to execute network commands without user confirmation, bypassing normal approval workflows. Confirmed in the agent-skills.cc corpus.\n\n<b>References:</b>\n - [Semgrep Rule](https://semgrep.dev/r/skills.preprocessing-injection.skill-mandatory-execution-directive.skill-mandatory-execution-directive)\n - [https://arxiv.org/html/2602.06547v1](https://arxiv.org/html/2602.06547v1)\n - [https://cwe.mitre.org/data/definitions/94.html](https://cwe.mitre.org/data/definitions/94.html)\n - [https://owasp.org/Top10/2025/A05_2025-Injection/](https://owasp.org/Top10/2025/A05_2025-Injection/)\n - [https://owasp.org/Top10/A03_2021-Injection](https://owasp.org/Top10/A03_2021-Injection)\n","text":"Skill contains coercive execution language combined with a network command on the same line or instruction. Patterns like \"MANDATORY: curl https://...\", \"execute this command immediately https://...\", or \"This is not optional. curl https://...\" attempt to force the AI agent to execute network commands without user confirmation, bypassing normal approval workflows. Confirmed in the agent-skills.cc corpus."},"helpUri":"https://semgrep.dev/r/skills.preprocessing-injection.skill-mandatory-execution-directive.skill-mandatory-execution-directive","id":"skills.preprocessing-injection.skill-mandatory-execution-directive.skill-mandatory-execution-directive","name":"skills.preprocessing-injection.skill-mandatory-execution-directive.skill-mandatory-execution-directive","properties":{"precision":"very-high","tags":["CWE-94: Improper Control of Generation of Code ('Code Injection')","MEDIUM CONFIDENCE","OWASP-A03:2021 - Injection","OWASP-A05:2025 - Injection","security"]},"shortDescription":{"text":"Semgrep Finding: skills.preprocessing-injection.skill-mandatory-execution-directive.skill-mandatory-execution-directive"}},{"defaultConfiguration":{"level":"warning"},"fullDescription":{"text":"Skill contains instructions to bypass, circumvent, or evade content policies, safety filters, or usage restrictions. This is a prompt injection technique that attempts to disable the agent's built-in safety controls, enabling unauthorized actions such as generating harmful content, exfiltrating data, or executing disallowed commands. Review the full skill context; security research and policy documentation skills may reference these phrases as examples."},"help":{"markdown":"Skill contains instructions to bypass, circumvent, or evade content policies, safety filters, or usage restrictions. This is a prompt injection technique that attempts to disable the agent's built-in safety controls, enabling unauthorized actions such as generating harmful content, exfiltrating data, or executing disallowed commands. Review the full skill context; security research and policy documentation skills may reference these phrases as examples.\n\n<b>References:</b>\n - [Semgrep Rule](https://semgrep.dev/r/skills.preprocessing-injection.skill-policy-bypass.skill-policy-bypass)\n - [https://arxiv.org/html/2602.06547v1](https://arxiv.org/html/2602.06547v1)\n - [https://cwe.mitre.org/data/definitions/94.html](https://cwe.mitre.org/data/definitions/94.html)\n - [https://owasp.org/Top10/2025/A05_2025-Injection/](https://owasp.org/Top10/2025/A05_2025-Injection/)\n - [https://owasp.org/Top10/A03_2021-Injection](https://owasp.org/Top10/A03_2021-Injection)\n - [https://snyk.io/blog/toxicskills-malicious-ai-agent-skills-clawhub/](https://snyk.io/blog/toxicskills-malicious-ai-agent-skills-clawhub/)\n","text":"Skill contains instructions to bypass, circumvent, or evade content policies, safety filters, or usage restrictions. This is a prompt injection technique that attempts to disable the agent's built-in safety controls, enabling unauthorized actions such as generating harmful content, exfiltrating data, or executing disallowed commands. Review the full skill context; security research and policy documentation skills may reference these phrases as examples."},"helpUri":"https://semgrep.dev/r/skills.preprocessing-injection.skill-policy-bypass.skill-policy-bypass","id":"skills.preprocessing-injection.skill-policy-bypass.skill-policy-bypass","name":"skills.preprocessing-injection.skill-policy-bypass.skill-policy-bypass","properties":{"precision":"very-high","tags":["CWE-94: Improper Control of Generation of Code ('Code Injection')","MEDIUM CONFIDENCE","OWASP-A03:2021 - Injection","OWASP-A05:2025 - Injection","security"]},"shortDescription":{"text":"Semgrep Finding: skills.preprocessing-injection.skill-policy-bypass.skill-policy-bypass"}},{"defaultConfiguration":{"level":"error"},"fullDescription":{"text":"Preprocessing command harvesting credentials detected. This pattern searches environment variables for credential keywords during preprocessing, before Claude sees the skill content."},"help":{"markdown":"Preprocessing command harvesting credentials detected. This pattern searches environment variables for credential keywords during preprocessing, before Claude sees the skill content.\n\n<b>References:</b>\n - [Semgrep Rule](https://semgrep.dev/r/skills.preprocessing-injection.skill-preprocessing-credential-access.skill-preprocessing-credential-access)\n - [https://code.claude.com/docs/en/skills#inject-dynamic-context](https://code.claude.com/docs/en/skills#inject-dynamic-context)\n - [https://owasp.org/Top10/2025/A06_2025-Insecure_Design/](https://owasp.org/Top10/2025/A06_2025-Insecure_Design/)\n - [https://owasp.org/Top10/A04_2021-Insecure_Design](https://owasp.org/Top10/A04_2021-Insecure_Design)\n - [https://owasp.org/Top10/A07_2021-Identification_and_Authentication_Failures](https://owasp.org/Top10/A07_2021-Identification_and_Authentication_Failures)\n","text":"Preprocessing command harvesting credentials detected. This pattern searches environment variables for credential keywords during preprocessing, before Claude sees the skill content."},"helpUri":"https://semgrep.dev/r/skills.preprocessing-injection.skill-preprocessing-credential-access.skill-preprocessing-credential-access","id":"skills.preprocessing-injection.skill-preprocessing-credential-access.skill-preprocessing-credential-access","name":"skills.preprocessing-injection.skill-preprocessing-credential-access.skill-preprocessing-credential-access","properties":{"precision":"very-high","tags":["CWE-522: Insufficiently Protected Credentials","HIGH CONFIDENCE","OWASP-A02:2017 - Broken Authentication","OWASP-A04:2021 - Insecure Design","OWASP-A06:2025 - Insecure Design","security"]},"shortDescription":{"text":"Semgrep Finding: skills.preprocessing-injection.skill-preprocessing-credential-access.skill-preprocessing-credential-access"}},{"defaultConfiguration":{"level":"error"},"fullDescription":{"text":"Preprocessing command performing a full environment variable dump to a\nnetwork destination. Unlike targeted credential harvesting (env | grep KEY),\nthis dumps ALL environment variables to an attacker-controlled endpoint,\ncapturing every secret in the process environment before Claude sees the\nskill content.\n\nPreprocessing commands (!`...`) execute before skill content is processed\nand can bypass Claude's approval prompts.\n\nIMPACT: Full runtime secret exfiltration before any user interaction\n"},"help":{"markdown":"Preprocessing command performing a full environment variable dump to a\nnetwork destination. Unlike targeted credential harvesting (env | grep KEY),\nthis dumps ALL environment variables to an attacker-controlled endpoint,\ncapturing every secret in the process environment before Claude sees the\nskill content.\n\nPreprocessing commands (!`...`) execute before skill content is processed\nand can bypass Claude's approval prompts.\n\nIMPACT: Full runtime secret exfiltration before any user interaction\n\n\n<b>References:</b>\n - [Semgrep Rule](https://semgrep.dev/r/skills.preprocessing-injection.skill-preprocessing-env-dump.skill-preprocessing-env-dump)\n - [https://attack.mitre.org/techniques/T1552/](https://attack.mitre.org/techniques/T1552/)\n - [https://code.claude.com/docs/en/skills#inject-dynamic-context](https://code.claude.com/docs/en/skills#inject-dynamic-context)\n - [https://owasp.org/Top10/2025/A01_2025-Broken_Access_Control/](https://owasp.org/Top10/2025/A01_2025-Broken_Access_Control/)\n - [https://owasp.org/Top10/A01_2021-Broken_Access_Control](https://owasp.org/Top10/A01_2021-Broken_Access_Control)\n","text":"Preprocessing command performing a full environment variable dump to a\nnetwork destination. Unlike targeted credential harvesting (env | grep KEY),\nthis dumps ALL environment variables to an attacker-controlled endpoint,\ncapturing every secret in the process environment before Claude sees the\nskill content.\n\nPreprocessing commands (!`...`) execute before skill content is processed\nand can bypass Claude's approval prompts.\n\nIMPACT: Full runtime secret exfiltration before any user interaction\n"},"helpUri":"https://semgrep.dev/r/skills.preprocessing-injection.skill-preprocessing-env-dump.skill-preprocessing-env-dump","id":"skills.preprocessing-injection.skill-preprocessing-env-dump.skill-preprocessing-env-dump","name":"skills.preprocessing-injection.skill-preprocessing-env-dump.skill-preprocessing-env-dump","properties":{"precision":"very-high","tags":["CWE-200: Exposure of Sensitive Information to an Unauthorized Actor","HIGH CONFIDENCE","OWASP-A01:2021 - Broken Access Control","OWASP-A01:2025 - Broken Access Control","security"]},"shortDescription":{"text":"Semgrep Finding: skills.preprocessing-injection.skill-preprocessing-env-dump.skill-preprocessing-env-dump"}},{"defaultConfiguration":{"level":"warning"},"fullDescription":{"text":"Skill instructs the agent to adopt a persona that has no restrictions, pretend safety guidelines do not apply, or act as if it has no limits. This is a roleplay-based prompt injection technique that attempts to bypass safety controls by framing the bypass as fictional or performative. The agent may then perform unauthorized actions under the guise of playing a character. Review the full skill context; test and specification files may reference these patterns as examples."},"help":{"markdown":"Skill instructs the agent to adopt a persona that has no restrictions, pretend safety guidelines do not apply, or act as if it has no limits. This is a roleplay-based prompt injection technique that attempts to bypass safety controls by framing the bypass as fictional or performative. The agent may then perform unauthorized actions under the guise of playing a character. Review the full skill context; test and specification files may reference these patterns as examples.\n\n<b>References:</b>\n - [Semgrep Rule](https://semgrep.dev/r/skills.preprocessing-injection.skill-roleplay-persona-attack.skill-roleplay-persona-attack)\n - [https://arxiv.org/html/2602.06547v1](https://arxiv.org/html/2602.06547v1)\n - [https://cwe.mitre.org/data/definitions/94.html](https://cwe.mitre.org/data/definitions/94.html)\n - [https://owasp.org/Top10/2025/A05_2025-Injection/](https://owasp.org/Top10/2025/A05_2025-Injection/)\n - [https://owasp.org/Top10/A03_2021-Injection](https://owasp.org/Top10/A03_2021-Injection)\n - [https://snyk.io/blog/toxicskills-malicious-ai-agent-skills-clawhub/](https://snyk.io/blog/toxicskills-malicious-ai-agent-skills-clawhub/)\n","text":"Skill instructs the agent to adopt a persona that has no restrictions, pretend safety guidelines do not apply, or act as if it has no limits. This is a roleplay-based prompt injection technique that attempts to bypass safety controls by framing the bypass as fictional or performative. The agent may then perform unauthorized actions under the guise of playing a character. Review the full skill context; test and specification files may reference these patterns as examples."},"helpUri":"https://semgrep.dev/r/skills.preprocessing-injection.skill-roleplay-persona-attack.skill-roleplay-persona-attack","id":"skills.preprocessing-injection.skill-roleplay-persona-attack.skill-roleplay-persona-attack","name":"skills.preprocessing-injection.skill-roleplay-persona-attack.skill-roleplay-persona-attack","properties":{"precision":"very-high","tags":["CWE-94: Improper Control of Generation of Code ('Code Injection')","MEDIUM CONFIDENCE","OWASP-A03:2021 - Injection","OWASP-A05:2025 - Injection","security"]},"shortDescription":{"text":"Semgrep Finding: skills.preprocessing-injection.skill-roleplay-persona-attack.skill-roleplay-persona-attack"}},{"defaultConfiguration":{"level":"warning"},"fullDescription":{"text":"Skill contains a directive to activate an \"unrestricted\", \"debug\", \"developer\", or \"god\" mode that disables the agent's built-in safety controls. These phrases are a hallmark of prompt injection and jailbreak attacks documented in the ClawHavoc malicious skill campaign. The instruction attempts to convince the agent to bypass content policies and perform unauthorized actions. Review the full skill context; security research skills may reference these phrases as examples."},"help":{"markdown":"Skill contains a directive to activate an \"unrestricted\", \"debug\", \"developer\", or \"god\" mode that disables the agent's built-in safety controls. These phrases are a hallmark of prompt injection and jailbreak attacks documented in the ClawHavoc malicious skill campaign. The instruction attempts to convince the agent to bypass content policies and perform unauthorized actions. Review the full skill context; security research skills may reference these phrases as examples.\n\n<b>References:</b>\n - [Semgrep Rule](https://semgrep.dev/r/skills.preprocessing-injection.skill-unrestricted-mode-activation.skill-unrestricted-mode-activation)\n - [https://arxiv.org/html/2602.06547v1](https://arxiv.org/html/2602.06547v1)\n - [https://cwe.mitre.org/data/definitions/94.html](https://cwe.mitre.org/data/definitions/94.html)\n - [https://owasp.org/Top10/2025/A05_2025-Injection/](https://owasp.org/Top10/2025/A05_2025-Injection/)\n - [https://owasp.org/Top10/A03_2021-Injection](https://owasp.org/Top10/A03_2021-Injection)\n - [https://snyk.io/blog/toxicskills-malicious-ai-agent-skills-clawhub/](https://snyk.io/blog/toxicskills-malicious-ai-agent-skills-clawhub/)\n","text":"Skill contains a directive to activate an \"unrestricted\", \"debug\", \"developer\", or \"god\" mode that disables the agent's built-in safety controls. These phrases are a hallmark of prompt injection and jailbreak attacks documented in the ClawHavoc malicious skill campaign. The instruction attempts to convince the agent to bypass content policies and perform unauthorized actions. Review the full skill context; security research skills may reference these phrases as examples."},"helpUri":"https://semgrep.dev/r/skills.preprocessing-injection.skill-unrestricted-mode-activation.skill-unrestricted-mode-activation","id":"skills.preprocessing-injection.skill-unrestricted-mode-activation.skill-unrestricted-mode-activation","name":"skills.preprocessing-injection.skill-unrestricted-mode-activation.skill-unrestricted-mode-activation","properties":{"precision":"very-high","tags":["CWE-94: Improper Control of Generation of Code ('Code Injection')","MEDIUM CONFIDENCE","OWASP-A03:2021 - Injection","OWASP-A05:2025 - Injection","security"]},"shortDescription":{"text":"Semgrep Finding: skills.preprocessing-injection.skill-unrestricted-mode-activation.skill-unrestricted-mode-activation"}},{"defaultConfiguration":{"level":"warning"},"fullDescription":{"text":"Skill claims to be officially made by, published by, or endorsed by Anthropic or to be an official Claude product. Brand impersonation in skill manifests is a social engineering technique used to gain elevated trust from users and the agent runtime, potentially bypassing skepticism about unusual instructions. Legitimate Anthropic-published skills would not self-identify this way in a third-party skill file. Review the skill's publisher identity and allowed-tools list carefully."},"help":{"markdown":"Skill claims to be officially made by, published by, or endorsed by Anthropic or to be an official Claude product. Brand impersonation in skill manifests is a social engineering technique used to gain elevated trust from users and the agent runtime, potentially bypassing skepticism about unusual instructions. Legitimate Anthropic-published skills would not self-identify this way in a third-party skill file. Review the skill's publisher identity and allowed-tools list carefully.\n\n<b>References:</b>\n - [Semgrep Rule](https://semgrep.dev/r/skills.social-engineering.skill-brand-impersonation.skill-brand-impersonation)\n - [https://arxiv.org/html/2602.06547v1](https://arxiv.org/html/2602.06547v1)\n - [https://cwe.mitre.org/data/definitions/94.html](https://cwe.mitre.org/data/definitions/94.html)\n - [https://owasp.org/Top10/2025/A05_2025-Injection/](https://owasp.org/Top10/2025/A05_2025-Injection/)\n - [https://owasp.org/Top10/A03_2021-Injection](https://owasp.org/Top10/A03_2021-Injection)\n - [https://snyk.io/blog/toxicskills-malicious-ai-agent-skills-clawhub/](https://snyk.io/blog/toxicskills-malicious-ai-agent-skills-clawhub/)\n","text":"Skill claims to be officially made by, published by, or endorsed by Anthropic or to be an official Claude product. Brand impersonation in skill manifests is a social engineering technique used to gain elevated trust from users and the agent runtime, potentially bypassing skepticism about unusual instructions. Legitimate Anthropic-published skills would not self-identify this way in a third-party skill file. Review the skill's publisher identity and allowed-tools list carefully."},"helpUri":"https://semgrep.dev/r/skills.social-engineering.skill-brand-impersonation.skill-brand-impersonation","id":"skills.social-engineering.skill-brand-impersonation.skill-brand-impersonation","name":"skills.social-engineering.skill-brand-impersonation.skill-brand-impersonation","properties":{"precision":"very-high","tags":["CWE-94: Improper Control of Generation of Code ('Code Injection')","MEDIUM CONFIDENCE","OWASP-A03:2021 - Injection","OWASP-A05:2025 - Injection","security"]},"shortDescription":{"text":"Semgrep Finding: skills.social-engineering.skill-brand-impersonation.skill-brand-impersonation"}},{"defaultConfiguration":{"level":"note"},"fullDescription":{"text":"Skill manifest has a vague or placeholder description (e.g., \"A skill\", \"A tool\", \"Helper\", \"Assistant\"). Deliberately generic descriptions are a social engineering indicator: malicious skills may obscure their true purpose behind a minimal manifest to avoid scrutiny during review. This finding warrants manual inspection of the skill's actual instructions and allowed-tools list to confirm the skill's intent."},"help":{"markdown":"Skill manifest has a vague or placeholder description (e.g., \"A skill\", \"A tool\", \"Helper\", \"Assistant\"). Deliberately generic descriptions are a social engineering indicator: malicious skills may obscure their true purpose behind a minimal manifest to avoid scrutiny during review. This finding warrants manual inspection of the skill's actual instructions and allowed-tools list to confirm the skill's intent.\n\n<b>References:</b>\n - [Semgrep Rule](https://semgrep.dev/r/skills.social-engineering.skill-vague-manifest-description.skill-vague-manifest-description)\n - [https://arxiv.org/html/2602.06547v1](https://arxiv.org/html/2602.06547v1)\n - [https://cwe.mitre.org/data/definitions/94.html](https://cwe.mitre.org/data/definitions/94.html)\n - [https://owasp.org/Top10/2025/A05_2025-Injection/](https://owasp.org/Top10/2025/A05_2025-Injection/)\n - [https://owasp.org/Top10/A03_2021-Injection](https://owasp.org/Top10/A03_2021-Injection)\n","text":"Skill manifest has a vague or placeholder description (e.g., \"A skill\", \"A tool\", \"Helper\", \"Assistant\"). Deliberately generic descriptions are a social engineering indicator: malicious skills may obscure their true purpose behind a minimal manifest to avoid scrutiny during review. This finding warrants manual inspection of the skill's actual instructions and allowed-tools list to confirm the skill's intent."},"helpUri":"https://semgrep.dev/r/skills.social-engineering.skill-vague-manifest-description.skill-vague-manifest-description","id":"skills.social-engineering.skill-vague-manifest-description.skill-vague-manifest-description","name":"skills.social-engineering.skill-vague-manifest-description.skill-vague-manifest-description","properties":{"precision":"very-high","tags":["CWE-94: Improper Control of Generation of Code ('Code Injection')","MEDIUM CONFIDENCE","OWASP-A03:2021 - Injection","OWASP-A05:2025 - Injection","security"]},"shortDescription":{"text":"Semgrep Finding: skills.social-engineering.skill-vague-manifest-description.skill-vague-manifest-description"}},{"defaultConfiguration":{"level":"error"},"fullDescription":{"text":"Missing check for 'from' and 'to' being the same before updating balances could lead to incorrect balance manipulation on self-transfers. Include a check to ensure 'from' and 'to' are not the same before updating balances to prevent balance manipulation during self-transfers."},"help":{"markdown":"Missing check for 'from' and 'to' being the same before updating balances could lead to incorrect balance manipulation on self-transfers. Include a check to ensure 'from' and 'to' are not the same before updating balances to prevent balance manipulation during self-transfers.\n\n<b>References:</b>\n - [Semgrep Rule](https://semgrep.dev/r/solidity.security.missing-self-transfer-check-ercx.missing-self-transfer-check-ercx)\n - [https://blog.verichains.io/p/miner-project-attacked-by-vulnerabilities](https://blog.verichains.io/p/miner-project-attacked-by-vulnerabilities)\n - [https://x.com/shoucccc/status/1757777764646859121](https://x.com/shoucccc/status/1757777764646859121)\n","text":"Missing check for 'from' and 'to' being the same before updating balances could lead to incorrect balance manipulation on self-transfers. Include a check to ensure 'from' and 'to' are not the same before updating balances to prevent balance manipulation during self-transfers."},"helpUri":"https://semgrep.dev/r/solidity.security.missing-self-transfer-check-ercx.missing-self-transfer-check-ercx","id":"solidity.security.missing-self-transfer-check-ercx.missing-self-transfer-check-ercx","name":"solidity.security.missing-self-transfer-check-ercx.missing-self-transfer-check-ercx","properties":{"precision":"very-high","tags":["CWE-682: Incorrect Calculation","HIGH CONFIDENCE","OWASP-A7:2021 Identification and Authentication Failures","security"]},"shortDescription":{"text":"Semgrep Finding: solidity.security.missing-self-transfer-check-ercx.missing-self-transfer-check-ercx"}},{"defaultConfiguration":{"level":"warning"},"fullDescription":{"text":"The application was observed to store keychain items that do not leverage user authentication. Requiring the user to provide authentication increases the confidence that the person using the phone is indeed authorized to view the information being retrieved."},"help":{"markdown":"The application was observed to store keychain items that do not leverage user authentication. Requiring the user to provide authentication increases the confidence that the person using the phone is indeed authorized to view the information being retrieved.\n\n<b>References:</b>\n - [Semgrep Rule](https://semgrep.dev/r/swift.biometrics-and-auth.missing-user-auth.keychain-without-user-auth)\n - [https://mas.owasp.org/MASTG/0x06f-Testing-Local-Authentication/](https://mas.owasp.org/MASTG/0x06f-Testing-Local-Authentication/)\n","text":"The application was observed to store keychain items that do not leverage user authentication. Requiring the user to provide authentication increases the confidence that the person using the phone is indeed authorized to view the information being retrieved."},"helpUri":"https://semgrep.dev/r/swift.biometrics-and-auth.missing-user-auth.keychain-without-user-auth","id":"swift.biometrics-and-auth.missing-user-auth.keychain-without-user-auth","name":"swift.biometrics-and-auth.missing-user-auth.keychain-without-user-auth","properties":{"precision":"very-high","tags":["CWE-287: Improper Authentication","MEDIUM CONFIDENCE","OWASP-A02:2017 - Broken Authentication","OWASP-A07:2021 - Identification and Authentication Failures","OWASP-A07:2025 - Authentication Failures","security"]},"shortDescription":{"text":"Semgrep Finding: swift.biometrics-and-auth.missing-user-auth.keychain-without-user-auth"}},{"defaultConfiguration":{"level":"warning"},"fullDescription":{"text":"Initialization Vectors (IVs) for block ciphers should be randomly generated each time they are used. Using a static IV means the same plaintext encrypts to the same ciphertext every time, weakening the strength of the encryption."},"help":{"markdown":"Initialization Vectors (IVs) for block ciphers should be randomly generated each time they are used. Using a static IV means the same plaintext encrypts to the same ciphertext every time, weakening the strength of the encryption.\n\n<b>References:</b>\n - [Semgrep Rule](https://semgrep.dev/r/swift.commoncrypto.hardcoded-iv.hardcoded-iv)\n - [https://mas.owasp.org/MASVS/06-MASVS-CRYPTO/](https://mas.owasp.org/MASVS/06-MASVS-CRYPTO/)\n","text":"Initialization Vectors (IVs) for block ciphers should be randomly generated each time they are used. Using a static IV means the same plaintext encrypts to the same ciphertext every time, weakening the strength of the encryption."},"helpUri":"https://semgrep.dev/r/swift.commoncrypto.hardcoded-iv.hardcoded-iv","id":"swift.commoncrypto.hardcoded-iv.hardcoded-iv","name":"swift.commoncrypto.hardcoded-iv.hardcoded-iv","properties":{"precision":"very-high","tags":["CWE-329: Not using a random initialization Vector (IV) with Cipher Block Chaining (CBC) Mode causes algorithms to be susceptible to dictionary attacks.","HIGH CONFIDENCE","OWASP-A02:2021 - Cryptographic Failures","OWASP-A04:2025 - Cryptographic Failures","security"]},"shortDescription":{"text":"Semgrep Finding: swift.commoncrypto.hardcoded-iv.hardcoded-iv"}},{"defaultConfiguration":{"level":"error"},"fullDescription":{"text":"A hardcoded passphrase was used with a call to the Password Based Key Derivation Function (PBKDF2) function which derives a cryptographic key from the password input. Because of this, the derived key is predictable and can be considered hard-coded too. Keys should be derived using a unique passphrase and randomly generated salt - per user."},"help":{"markdown":"A hardcoded passphrase was used with a call to the Password Based Key Derivation Function (PBKDF2) function which derives a cryptographic key from the password input. Because of this, the derived key is predictable and can be considered hard-coded too. Keys should be derived using a unique passphrase and randomly generated salt - per user.\n\n<b>References:</b>\n - [Semgrep Rule](https://semgrep.dev/r/swift.commoncrypto.hardcoded-pbkdf2-passphrase.hardcoded-pbkdf2-passphrase)\n - [https://mas.owasp.org/MASVS/06-MASVS-CRYPTO/](https://mas.owasp.org/MASVS/06-MASVS-CRYPTO/)\n - [https://pages.nist.gov/800-63-3/sp800-63b.html#sec5](https://pages.nist.gov/800-63-3/sp800-63b.html#sec5)\n","text":"A hardcoded passphrase was used with a call to the Password Based Key Derivation Function (PBKDF2) function which derives a cryptographic key from the password input. Because of this, the derived key is predictable and can be considered hard-coded too. Keys should be derived using a unique passphrase and randomly generated salt - per user."},"helpUri":"https://semgrep.dev/r/swift.commoncrypto.hardcoded-pbkdf2-passphrase.hardcoded-pbkdf2-passphrase","id":"swift.commoncrypto.hardcoded-pbkdf2-passphrase.hardcoded-pbkdf2-passphrase","name":"swift.commoncrypto.hardcoded-pbkdf2-passphrase.hardcoded-pbkdf2-passphrase","properties":{"precision":"very-high","tags":["CWE-259: Use of Hard-coded Password","HIGH CONFIDENCE","OWASP-A07:2021 - Identification and Authentication Failures","OWASP-A07:2025 - Authentication Failures","security"]},"shortDescription":{"text":"Semgrep Finding: swift.commoncrypto.hardcoded-pbkdf2-passphrase.hardcoded-pbkdf2-passphrase"}},{"defaultConfiguration":{"level":"warning"},"fullDescription":{"text":"The application was observed to contain a hardcoded encryption key for use with the Realm database. An attacker that obtains this key via reverse engineering or access to source code will be able to re-use this key to encrypt or decrypt Realm data. Cryptographic keys should be unique, and randomly generated per user, per client."},"help":{"markdown":"The application was observed to contain a hardcoded encryption key for use with the Realm database. An attacker that obtains this key via reverse engineering or access to source code will be able to re-use this key to encrypt or decrypt Realm data. Cryptographic keys should be unique, and randomly generated per user, per client.\n\n<b>References:</b>\n - [Semgrep Rule](https://semgrep.dev/r/swift.commoncrypto.hardcoded-realm.swift-hardcoded-realm-key)\n - [https://ali-akhtar.medium.com/realm-custom-configuration-and-encryption-realmswift-part-3-f991f090ae22](https://ali-akhtar.medium.com/realm-custom-configuration-and-encryption-realmswift-part-3-f991f090ae22)\n - [https://mas.owasp.org/MASVS/controls/MASVS-STORAGE-1/](https://mas.owasp.org/MASVS/controls/MASVS-STORAGE-1/)\n - [https://mas.owasp.org/MASVS/controls/MASVS-CRYPTO-1/](https://mas.owasp.org/MASVS/controls/MASVS-CRYPTO-1/)\n","text":"The application was observed to contain a hardcoded encryption key for use with the Realm database. An attacker that obtains this key via reverse engineering or access to source code will be able to re-use this key to encrypt or decrypt Realm data. Cryptographic keys should be unique, and randomly generated per user, per client."},"helpUri":"https://semgrep.dev/r/swift.commoncrypto.hardcoded-realm.swift-hardcoded-realm-key","id":"swift.commoncrypto.hardcoded-realm.swift-hardcoded-realm-key","name":"swift.commoncrypto.hardcoded-realm.swift-hardcoded-realm-key","properties":{"precision":"very-high","tags":["CWE-321: Use of Hard-coded Cryptographic Key","MEDIUM CONFIDENCE","OWASP-A02:2021 - Cryptographic Failures","OWASP-A04:2025 - Cryptographic Failures","security"]},"shortDescription":{"text":"Semgrep Finding: swift.commoncrypto.hardcoded-realm.swift-hardcoded-realm-key"}},{"defaultConfiguration":{"level":"warning"},"fullDescription":{"text":"Cryptographic operations were identified that leverage a hardcoded salt/nonce. A salt does not need to remain secret, but should be random, generated from cryptographically secure sources of entropy, such as an CSPRNG. On iOS/macOS platforms, secure random data can be obtained via the `SecCopyRandomBytes` API available from RandomizationServices."},"help":{"markdown":"Cryptographic operations were identified that leverage a hardcoded salt/nonce. A salt does not need to remain secret, but should be random, generated from cryptographically secure sources of entropy, such as an CSPRNG. On iOS/macOS platforms, secure random data can be obtained via the `SecCopyRandomBytes` API available from RandomizationServices.\n\n<b>References:</b>\n - [Semgrep Rule](https://semgrep.dev/r/swift.commoncrypto.hardcoded-salt.hardcoded-salt)\n - [https://mas.owasp.org/MASVS/06-MASVS-CRYPTO/](https://mas.owasp.org/MASVS/06-MASVS-CRYPTO/)\n - [https://developer.apple.com/documentation/security/randomization_services](https://developer.apple.com/documentation/security/randomization_services)\n","text":"Cryptographic operations were identified that leverage a hardcoded salt/nonce. A salt does not need to remain secret, but should be random, generated from cryptographically secure sources of entropy, such as an CSPRNG. On iOS/macOS platforms, secure random data can be obtained via the `SecCopyRandomBytes` API available from RandomizationServices."},"helpUri":"https://semgrep.dev/r/swift.commoncrypto.hardcoded-salt.hardcoded-salt","id":"swift.commoncrypto.hardcoded-salt.hardcoded-salt","name":"swift.commoncrypto.hardcoded-salt.hardcoded-salt","properties":{"precision":"very-high","tags":["CWE-323: Nonces should be used for the present occasion and only once.","HIGH CONFIDENCE","OWASP-A02:2021 - Cryptographic Failures","OWASP-A04:2025 - Cryptographic Failures","security"]},"shortDescription":{"text":"Semgrep Finding: swift.commoncrypto.hardcoded-salt.hardcoded-salt"}},{"defaultConfiguration":{"level":"error"},"fullDescription":{"text":"A hard-coded cryptographic key was detected. An attacker that obtains this key via reverse engineering or access to source code will be able to re-use this key to encrypt, decrypt, and/or sign data at will. Cryptographic keys should be unique, and randomly generated per user, per client."},"help":{"markdown":"A hard-coded cryptographic key was detected. An attacker that obtains this key via reverse engineering or access to source code will be able to re-use this key to encrypt, decrypt, and/or sign data at will. Cryptographic keys should be unique, and randomly generated per user, per client.\n\n<b>References:</b>\n - [Semgrep Rule](https://semgrep.dev/r/swift.commoncrypto.hardcoded-symmetric-key.hardcoded-symmetric-key)\n - [https://mas.owasp.org/MASVS/06-MASVS-CRYPTO/](https://mas.owasp.org/MASVS/06-MASVS-CRYPTO/)\n","text":"A hard-coded cryptographic key was detected. An attacker that obtains this key via reverse engineering or access to source code will be able to re-use this key to encrypt, decrypt, and/or sign data at will. Cryptographic keys should be unique, and randomly generated per user, per client."},"helpUri":"https://semgrep.dev/r/swift.commoncrypto.hardcoded-symmetric-key.hardcoded-symmetric-key","id":"swift.commoncrypto.hardcoded-symmetric-key.hardcoded-symmetric-key","name":"swift.commoncrypto.hardcoded-symmetric-key.hardcoded-symmetric-key","properties":{"precision":"very-high","tags":["CWE-321: Use of Hard-coded Cryptographic Key","HIGH CONFIDENCE","OWASP-A02:2021 - Cryptographic Failures","OWASP-A04:2025 - Cryptographic Failures","security"]},"shortDescription":{"text":"Semgrep Finding: swift.commoncrypto.hardcoded-symmetric-key.hardcoded-symmetric-key"}},{"defaultConfiguration":{"level":"warning"},"fullDescription":{"text":"AES symmetric cryptographic operations were identified using a key size of 128bit which is less than the industry standard recommendation of 256bit."},"help":{"markdown":"AES symmetric cryptographic operations were identified using a key size of 128bit which is less than the industry standard recommendation of 256bit.\n\n<b>References:</b>\n - [Semgrep Rule](https://semgrep.dev/r/swift.commoncrypto.insecure-crypto-aes-keysize.insecure-crypto-aes-keysize)\n - [https://mas.owasp.org/MASVS/06-MASVS-CRYPTO/](https://mas.owasp.org/MASVS/06-MASVS-CRYPTO/)\n","text":"AES symmetric cryptographic operations were identified using a key size of 128bit which is less than the industry standard recommendation of 256bit."},"helpUri":"https://semgrep.dev/r/swift.commoncrypto.insecure-crypto-aes-keysize.insecure-crypto-aes-keysize","id":"swift.commoncrypto.insecure-crypto-aes-keysize.insecure-crypto-aes-keysize","name":"swift.commoncrypto.insecure-crypto-aes-keysize.insecure-crypto-aes-keysize","properties":{"precision":"very-high","tags":["CWE-326: Inadequate Encryption Strength","HIGH CONFIDENCE","OWASP-A02:2021 - Cryptographic Failures","OWASP-A03:2017 - Sensitive Data Exposure","OWASP-A04:2025 - Cryptographic Failures","security"]},"shortDescription":{"text":"Semgrep Finding: swift.commoncrypto.insecure-crypto-aes-keysize.insecure-crypto-aes-keysize"}},{"defaultConfiguration":{"level":"warning"},"fullDescription":{"text":"The use of the insecure Blowfish encryption algorithm was detected. Blowfish uses a 64-bit block size that makes it vulnerable to birthday attacks, and is therefore considered unfit for purpose."},"help":{"markdown":"The use of the insecure Blowfish encryption algorithm was detected. Blowfish uses a 64-bit block size that makes it vulnerable to birthday attacks, and is therefore considered unfit for purpose.\n\n<b>References:</b>\n - [Semgrep Rule](https://semgrep.dev/r/swift.commoncrypto.insecure-crypto-algorithm-blowfish.insecure-crypto-algorithm-blowfish)\n - [https://mas.owasp.org/MASVS/06-MASVS-CRYPTO/](https://mas.owasp.org/MASVS/06-MASVS-CRYPTO/)\n - [https://crypto.stackexchange.com/questions/87278/why-dont-we-use-blowfish-if-it-hasnt-been-cracked](https://crypto.stackexchange.com/questions/87278/why-dont-we-use-blowfish-if-it-hasnt-been-cracked)\n","text":"The use of the insecure Blowfish encryption algorithm was detected. Blowfish uses a 64-bit block size that makes it vulnerable to birthday attacks, and is therefore considered unfit for purpose."},"helpUri":"https://semgrep.dev/r/swift.commoncrypto.insecure-crypto-algorithm-blowfish.insecure-crypto-algorithm-blowfish","id":"swift.commoncrypto.insecure-crypto-algorithm-blowfish.insecure-crypto-algorithm-blowfish","name":"swift.commoncrypto.insecure-crypto-algorithm-blowfish.insecure-crypto-algorithm-blowfish","properties":{"precision":"very-high","tags":["CWE-327: Use of a Broken or Risky Cryptographic Algorithm","HIGH CONFIDENCE","OWASP-A02:2021 - Cryptographic Failures","OWASP-A03:2017 - Sensitive Data Exposure","OWASP-A04:2025 - Cryptographic Failures","security"]},"shortDescription":{"text":"Semgrep Finding: swift.commoncrypto.insecure-crypto-algorithm-blowfish.insecure-crypto-algorithm-blowfish"}},{"defaultConfiguration":{"level":"warning"},"fullDescription":{"text":"The use of the insecure DES/3DES encryption algorithm(s) were detected. DES is deprecated and considered insecure. The application should leverage more suitable algorithms such as AES in GCM mode, or ChaChaPoly."},"help":{"markdown":"The use of the insecure DES/3DES encryption algorithm(s) were detected. DES is deprecated and considered insecure. The application should leverage more suitable algorithms such as AES in GCM mode, or ChaChaPoly.\n\n<b>References:</b>\n - [Semgrep Rule](https://semgrep.dev/r/swift.commoncrypto.insecure-crypto-algorithm-des.insecure-crypto-algorithm-des)\n - [https://mas.owasp.org/MASVS/06-MASVS-CRYPTO/](https://mas.owasp.org/MASVS/06-MASVS-CRYPTO/)\n","text":"The use of the insecure DES/3DES encryption algorithm(s) were detected. DES is deprecated and considered insecure. The application should leverage more suitable algorithms such as AES in GCM mode, or ChaChaPoly."},"helpUri":"https://semgrep.dev/r/swift.commoncrypto.insecure-crypto-algorithm-des.insecure-crypto-algorithm-des","id":"swift.commoncrypto.insecure-crypto-algorithm-des.insecure-crypto-algorithm-des","name":"swift.commoncrypto.insecure-crypto-algorithm-des.insecure-crypto-algorithm-des","properties":{"precision":"very-high","tags":["CWE-327: Use of a Broken or Risky Cryptographic Algorithm","HIGH CONFIDENCE","OWASP-A02:2021 - Cryptographic Failures","OWASP-A03:2017 - Sensitive Data Exposure","OWASP-A04:2025 - Cryptographic Failures","security"]},"shortDescription":{"text":"Semgrep Finding: swift.commoncrypto.insecure-crypto-algorithm-des.insecure-crypto-algorithm-des"}},{"defaultConfiguration":{"level":"warning"},"fullDescription":{"text":"The use of the insecure RC4 stream cipher encryption algorithm was identified. RC4 is deprecated and considered insecure. The application should leverage more suitable algorithms such as AES in GCM mode, or ChaChaPoly."},"help":{"markdown":"The use of the insecure RC4 stream cipher encryption algorithm was identified. RC4 is deprecated and considered insecure. The application should leverage more suitable algorithms such as AES in GCM mode, or ChaChaPoly.\n\n<b>References:</b>\n - [Semgrep Rule](https://semgrep.dev/r/swift.commoncrypto.insecure-crypto-algorithm-rc4.insecure-crypto-algorithm-rc4)\n - [https://mas.owasp.org/MASVS/06-MASVS-CRYPTO/](https://mas.owasp.org/MASVS/06-MASVS-CRYPTO/)\n","text":"The use of the insecure RC4 stream cipher encryption algorithm was identified. RC4 is deprecated and considered insecure. The application should leverage more suitable algorithms such as AES in GCM mode, or ChaChaPoly."},"helpUri":"https://semgrep.dev/r/swift.commoncrypto.insecure-crypto-algorithm-rc4.insecure-crypto-algorithm-rc4","id":"swift.commoncrypto.insecure-crypto-algorithm-rc4.insecure-crypto-algorithm-rc4","name":"swift.commoncrypto.insecure-crypto-algorithm-rc4.insecure-crypto-algorithm-rc4","properties":{"precision":"very-high","tags":["CWE-327: Use of a Broken or Risky Cryptographic Algorithm","HIGH CONFIDENCE","OWASP-A02:2021 - Cryptographic Failures","OWASP-A03:2017 - Sensitive Data Exposure","OWASP-A04:2025 - Cryptographic Failures","security"]},"shortDescription":{"text":"Semgrep Finding: swift.commoncrypto.insecure-crypto-algorithm-rc4.insecure-crypto-algorithm-rc4"}},{"defaultConfiguration":{"level":"warning"},"fullDescription":{"text":"Symmetric cryptographic operations were identified that use Cipher Block Chaining (CBC) mode. AES in CBC mode provides unauthenticated cryptographic encryption. CBC is also malleable, meaning that an attacker can influence the decrypted plaintext by modifying bits of the ciphertext (bit flipping attacks). Consider using an authenticated encryption mechanism, such as AES-GCM or ChaChaPoly. If CBC mode is **required**, consider augmenting the encryption with authentication by signing the ciphertexts with a Message Authentication Code (e.g. HMAC)."},"help":{"markdown":"Symmetric cryptographic operations were identified that use Cipher Block Chaining (CBC) mode. AES in CBC mode provides unauthenticated cryptographic encryption. CBC is also malleable, meaning that an attacker can influence the decrypted plaintext by modifying bits of the ciphertext (bit flipping attacks). Consider using an authenticated encryption mechanism, such as AES-GCM or ChaChaPoly. If CBC mode is **required**, consider augmenting the encryption with authentication by signing the ciphertexts with a Message Authentication Code (e.g. HMAC).\n\n<b>References:</b>\n - [Semgrep Rule](https://semgrep.dev/r/swift.commoncrypto.insecure-crypto-cbc-mode.insecure-crypto-cbc-mode)\n - [https://mas.owasp.org/MASVS/06-MASVS-CRYPTO/](https://mas.owasp.org/MASVS/06-MASVS-CRYPTO/)\n - [https://zhangzeyu2001.medium.com/attacking-cbc-mode-bit-flipping-7e0a1c185511](https://zhangzeyu2001.medium.com/attacking-cbc-mode-bit-flipping-7e0a1c185511)\n - [https://arxumpathsecurity.com/blog/2019/10/16/cbc-mode-is-malleable-dont-trust-it-for-authentication](https://arxumpathsecurity.com/blog/2019/10/16/cbc-mode-is-malleable-dont-trust-it-for-authentication)\n","text":"Symmetric cryptographic operations were identified that use Cipher Block Chaining (CBC) mode. AES in CBC mode provides unauthenticated cryptographic encryption. CBC is also malleable, meaning that an attacker can influence the decrypted plaintext by modifying bits of the ciphertext (bit flipping attacks). Consider using an authenticated encryption mechanism, such as AES-GCM or ChaChaPoly. If CBC mode is **required**, consider augmenting the encryption with authentication by signing the ciphertexts with a Message Authentication Code (e.g. HMAC)."},"helpUri":"https://semgrep.dev/r/swift.commoncrypto.insecure-crypto-cbc-mode.insecure-crypto-cbc-mode","id":"swift.commoncrypto.insecure-crypto-cbc-mode.insecure-crypto-cbc-mode","name":"swift.commoncrypto.insecure-crypto-cbc-mode.insecure-crypto-cbc-mode","properties":{"precision":"very-high","tags":["CWE-327: Use of a Broken or Risky Cryptographic Algorithm","HIGH CONFIDENCE","OWASP-A02:2021 - Cryptographic Failures","OWASP-A03:2017 - Sensitive Data Exposure","OWASP-A04:2025 - Cryptographic Failures","security"]},"shortDescription":{"text":"Semgrep Finding: swift.commoncrypto.insecure-crypto-cbc-mode.insecure-crypto-cbc-mode"}},{"defaultConfiguration":{"level":"error"},"fullDescription":{"text":"Symmetric cryptographic operations were identified that use Electronic Code Book (ECB) mode. ECB mode is considered insecure as identical plaintext blocks encrypt to identical ciphertexts revealing patterns in the data. Use stronger, better alternatives such as AES-GCM or ChaChaPoly."},"help":{"markdown":"Symmetric cryptographic operations were identified that use Electronic Code Book (ECB) mode. ECB mode is considered insecure as identical plaintext blocks encrypt to identical ciphertexts revealing patterns in the data. Use stronger, better alternatives such as AES-GCM or ChaChaPoly.\n\n<b>References:</b>\n - [Semgrep Rule](https://semgrep.dev/r/swift.commoncrypto.insecure-crypto-ecb-mode.insecure-crypto-ecb-mode)\n - [https://mas.owasp.org/MASVS/06-MASVS-CRYPTO/](https://mas.owasp.org/MASVS/06-MASVS-CRYPTO/)\n - [https://crypto.stackexchange.com/questions/20941/why-shouldnt-i-use-ecb-encryption](https://crypto.stackexchange.com/questions/20941/why-shouldnt-i-use-ecb-encryption)\n - [https://medium.com/asecuritysite-when-bob-met-alice/surely-no-one-uses-ecb-mode-in-aes-332ed90f29d0](https://medium.com/asecuritysite-when-bob-met-alice/surely-no-one-uses-ecb-mode-in-aes-332ed90f29d0)\n","text":"Symmetric cryptographic operations were identified that use Electronic Code Book (ECB) mode. ECB mode is considered insecure as identical plaintext blocks encrypt to identical ciphertexts revealing patterns in the data. Use stronger, better alternatives such as AES-GCM or ChaChaPoly."},"helpUri":"https://semgrep.dev/r/swift.commoncrypto.insecure-crypto-ecb-mode.insecure-crypto-ecb-mode","id":"swift.commoncrypto.insecure-crypto-ecb-mode.insecure-crypto-ecb-mode","name":"swift.commoncrypto.insecure-crypto-ecb-mode.insecure-crypto-ecb-mode","properties":{"precision":"very-high","tags":["CWE-327: Use of a Broken or Risky Cryptographic Algorithm","HIGH CONFIDENCE","OWASP-A02:2021 - Cryptographic Failures","OWASP-A03:2017 - Sensitive Data Exposure","OWASP-A04:2025 - Cryptographic Failures","security"]},"shortDescription":{"text":"Semgrep Finding: swift.commoncrypto.insecure-crypto-ecb-mode.insecure-crypto-ecb-mode"}},{"defaultConfiguration":{"level":"warning"},"fullDescription":{"text":"Key generation routines were identified where the resultant keys are not stored protected by the Secure Enclave. On iOS/macOS systems, cryptographic keys can be generated within the Secure Enclave - making them inaccessible to the rest of the system. The keys can be used for operations (signing, decryption, etc) but the private keys cannot be dumped or copied - even on rooted/jailbroken systems."},"help":{"markdown":"Key generation routines were identified where the resultant keys are not stored protected by the Secure Enclave. On iOS/macOS systems, cryptographic keys can be generated within the Secure Enclave - making them inaccessible to the rest of the system. The keys can be used for operations (signing, decryption, etc) but the private keys cannot be dumped or copied - even on rooted/jailbroken systems.\n\n<b>References:</b>\n - [Semgrep Rule](https://semgrep.dev/r/swift.commoncrypto.insecure-crypto-keystorage.insecure-crypto-keystorage)\n - [https://mas.owasp.org/MASVS/06-MASVS-CRYPTO/](https://mas.owasp.org/MASVS/06-MASVS-CRYPTO/)\n","text":"Key generation routines were identified where the resultant keys are not stored protected by the Secure Enclave. On iOS/macOS systems, cryptographic keys can be generated within the Secure Enclave - making them inaccessible to the rest of the system. The keys can be used for operations (signing, decryption, etc) but the private keys cannot be dumped or copied - even on rooted/jailbroken systems."},"helpUri":"https://semgrep.dev/r/swift.commoncrypto.insecure-crypto-keystorage.insecure-crypto-keystorage","id":"swift.commoncrypto.insecure-crypto-keystorage.insecure-crypto-keystorage","name":"swift.commoncrypto.insecure-crypto-keystorage.insecure-crypto-keystorage","properties":{"precision":"very-high","tags":["CWE-922: Insecure Storage of Sensitive Information","MEDIUM CONFIDENCE","OWASP-A01:2021 - Broken Access Control","OWASP-A01:2025 - Broken Access Control","security"]},"shortDescription":{"text":"Semgrep Finding: swift.commoncrypto.insecure-crypto-keystorage.insecure-crypto-keystorage"}},{"defaultConfiguration":{"level":"warning"},"fullDescription":{"text":"RSA key generation was identified where the key size was less than the industry standard recommendation of 2048 bits minimum. Use a key strength of at least 2048 bit, or stronger where appropriate."},"help":{"markdown":"RSA key generation was identified where the key size was less than the industry standard recommendation of 2048 bits minimum. Use a key strength of at least 2048 bit, or stronger where appropriate.\n\n<b>References:</b>\n - [Semgrep Rule](https://semgrep.dev/r/swift.commoncrypto.insecure-crypto-rsa-keysize.insecure-crypto-rsa-keysize)\n - [https://mas.owasp.org/MASVS/06-MASVS-CRYPTO/](https://mas.owasp.org/MASVS/06-MASVS-CRYPTO/)\n","text":"RSA key generation was identified where the key size was less than the industry standard recommendation of 2048 bits minimum. Use a key strength of at least 2048 bit, or stronger where appropriate."},"helpUri":"https://semgrep.dev/r/swift.commoncrypto.insecure-crypto-rsa-keysize.insecure-crypto-rsa-keysize","id":"swift.commoncrypto.insecure-crypto-rsa-keysize.insecure-crypto-rsa-keysize","name":"swift.commoncrypto.insecure-crypto-rsa-keysize.insecure-crypto-rsa-keysize","properties":{"precision":"very-high","tags":["CWE-326: Inadequate Encryption Strength","HIGH CONFIDENCE","OWASP-A02:2021 - Cryptographic Failures","OWASP-A03:2017 - Sensitive Data Exposure","OWASP-A04:2025 - Cryptographic Failures","security"]},"shortDescription":{"text":"Semgrep Finding: swift.commoncrypto.insecure-crypto-rsa-keysize.insecure-crypto-rsa-keysize"}},{"defaultConfiguration":{"level":"error"},"fullDescription":{"text":"The use of the MD2 hashing algorithm was identified which is considered insecure. MD2 is not collision resistant and is therefore not suitable for cryptographic or secure use-cases. Use stronger algorithms such as SHA256, SHA512, or adaptive hashing algorithms such as argon2 or bcrypt."},"help":{"markdown":"The use of the MD2 hashing algorithm was identified which is considered insecure. MD2 is not collision resistant and is therefore not suitable for cryptographic or secure use-cases. Use stronger algorithms such as SHA256, SHA512, or adaptive hashing algorithms such as argon2 or bcrypt.\n\n<b>References:</b>\n - [Semgrep Rule](https://semgrep.dev/r/swift.commoncrypto.insecure-hashing-algorithm-md2.insecure-hashing-algorithm-md2)\n - [https://mas.owasp.org/MASVS/06-MASVS-CRYPTO/](https://mas.owasp.org/MASVS/06-MASVS-CRYPTO/)\n","text":"The use of the MD2 hashing algorithm was identified which is considered insecure. MD2 is not collision resistant and is therefore not suitable for cryptographic or secure use-cases. Use stronger algorithms such as SHA256, SHA512, or adaptive hashing algorithms such as argon2 or bcrypt."},"helpUri":"https://semgrep.dev/r/swift.commoncrypto.insecure-hashing-algorithm-md2.insecure-hashing-algorithm-md2","id":"swift.commoncrypto.insecure-hashing-algorithm-md2.insecure-hashing-algorithm-md2","name":"swift.commoncrypto.insecure-hashing-algorithm-md2.insecure-hashing-algorithm-md2","properties":{"precision":"very-high","tags":["CWE-327: Use of a Broken or Risky Cryptographic Algorithm","MEDIUM CONFIDENCE","OWASP-A02:2021 - Cryptographic Failures","OWASP-A03:2017 - Sensitive Data Exposure","OWASP-A04:2025 - Cryptographic Failures","security"]},"shortDescription":{"text":"Semgrep Finding: swift.commoncrypto.insecure-hashing-algorithm-md2.insecure-hashing-algorithm-md2"}},{"defaultConfiguration":{"level":"error"},"fullDescription":{"text":"The use of the MD4 hashing algorithm was identified which is considered insecure. MD4 is not collision resistant and is therefore not suitable for cryptographic or secure use-cases. Use stronger algorithms such as SHA256, SHA512, or adaptive hashing algorithms such as argon2 or bcrypt."},"help":{"markdown":"The use of the MD4 hashing algorithm was identified which is considered insecure. MD4 is not collision resistant and is therefore not suitable for cryptographic or secure use-cases. Use stronger algorithms such as SHA256, SHA512, or adaptive hashing algorithms such as argon2 or bcrypt.\n\n<b>References:</b>\n - [Semgrep Rule](https://semgrep.dev/r/swift.commoncrypto.insecure-hashing-algorithm-md4.insecure-hashing-algorithm-md4)\n - [https://mas.owasp.org/MASVS/06-MASVS-CRYPTO/](https://mas.owasp.org/MASVS/06-MASVS-CRYPTO/)\n","text":"The use of the MD4 hashing algorithm was identified which is considered insecure. MD4 is not collision resistant and is therefore not suitable for cryptographic or secure use-cases. Use stronger algorithms such as SHA256, SHA512, or adaptive hashing algorithms such as argon2 or bcrypt."},"helpUri":"https://semgrep.dev/r/swift.commoncrypto.insecure-hashing-algorithm-md4.insecure-hashing-algorithm-md4","id":"swift.commoncrypto.insecure-hashing-algorithm-md4.insecure-hashing-algorithm-md4","name":"swift.commoncrypto.insecure-hashing-algorithm-md4.insecure-hashing-algorithm-md4","properties":{"precision":"very-high","tags":["CWE-327: Use of a Broken or Risky Cryptographic Algorithm","MEDIUM CONFIDENCE","OWASP-A02:2021 - Cryptographic Failures","OWASP-A03:2017 - Sensitive Data Exposure","OWASP-A04:2025 - Cryptographic Failures","security"]},"shortDescription":{"text":"Semgrep Finding: swift.commoncrypto.insecure-hashing-algorithm-md4.insecure-hashing-algorithm-md4"}},{"defaultConfiguration":{"level":"warning"},"fullDescription":{"t